04** - 7 papers\n4. **PEMS08** - 5 papers\n5. **PEMS03** - 4 papers\n6. **PEMS07** - 2 papers\n\n### Novel Datasets:\n- **XXLTraffic**: 19,561 sensors from California PeMS (largest traffic dataset)\n- **Federated heterogeneous traffic datasets** (ICDE 2025)\n- **Multi-source traffic data** for non-recurring events (KDD 2025)\n\n---\n\n## Metrics Used\n\n**Standard Metrics** (appearing in 15+ papers):\n- **MAE** (Mean Absolute Error)\n- **RMSE** (Root Mean Square Error)\n- **MAPE** (Mean Absolute Percentage Error)\n\n**Additional Metrics**:\n- **MSE** (Mean Square Error) - Time series papers\n- **Privacy metrics** - Federated learning papers\n- **Cross-domain generalization** - Migration learning papers\n- **Spatial resolution** - Weather/radar papers\n- **Queue length, Travel time** - Traffic control papers\n\n---\n\n## GitHub Repositories to Clone\n\n### Priority 1: Architecture Novelty ⭐⭐⭐\n\n| Repository | Paper | Why Clone | Architecture |\n|------------|-------|-----------|--------------|\n| [STGormer](https://github.com/jasonz5/STGormer) | Graph Transformer for Traffic | **Novel mixture-of-experts** module for spatiotemporal heterogeneity | Graph Transformer |\n| [SynEVO](https://github.com/Rodger-Lau/SynEVO) | Cross-Domain Adaptation | **Brain-inspired synaptic evolution**, 42% improvement in cross-domain scenarios | Neuro-inspired ST Network |\n| [CoLLMLight](https://github.com/usail-hkust/CoLLMLight) | LLM for Traffic Signals | **First LLM agent framework** for network-wide traffic control | LLM Agent + ST Graph |\n\n### Priority 2: Dataset Coverage ⭐⭐\n\n| Repository | Paper | Why Clone | Datasets |\n|------------|-------|-----------|----------|\n| [EAC](https://github.com/Onedean/EAC) | Continual ST Graph Forecasting | **Continual learning** for streaming scenarios, prompt tuning | Traffic, Air quality, Wind |\n| [TimeBase](https://github.com/hqh0728/TimeBase) | Minimalist Time Series | **Ultra-lightweight**, plug-in for patch-based models | Traffic, Electricity, ETT |\n\n### Priority 3: Benchmarking & Evaluation ⭐\n\n| Repository | Paper | Why Clone | Purpose |\n|------------|-------|-----------|---------|\n| [SRSNet](https://github.com/decisionintelligence/SRSNet) | Selective Representation Space | **Patch-based representation learning**, NeurIPS 2025 Spotlight | General TS benchmarks |\n\n---\n\n## Key Findings & Trends\n\n### 1. **Graph Transformers Dominate** 🔥\n- **7 out of 20 papers** use graph transformers or attention mechanisms\n- Papers: STGormer, MLCAFormer, LSTTN, LSTGAN, PhyMPGN, EAC\n- **Trend**: Hybrid architectures combining GCNs with transformers\n\n### 2. **Large Language Models Emerging** 🆕\n- **2 papers** (CoLLMLight, LLM Traffic Flow)\n- **Application**: Traffic signal control, forecasting with natural language reasoning\n- **Innovation**: LLM agents with spatiotemporal graph understanding\n\n### 3. **Cross-Domain & Continual Learning** 🔄\n- **2 papers** (SynEVO, EAC)\n- **Challenge**: Streaming data, domain shift, catastrophic forgetting\n- **Solution**: Synaptic evolution, prompt tuning, curriculum learning\n\n### 4. **Privacy-Preserving Methods** 🔒\n- **1 paper** (Heterogeneous-Aware Traffic Prediction)\n- **Method**: Federated learning for decentralized training\n- **Dataset**: Handles spatial/temporal heterogeneity across clients\n\n### 5. **Explainability & Interpretability** 📊\n- **2 papers** (Ultra-Flexible Traffic Prediction, Physics-Informed MPG)\n- **Trend**: Moving beyond black-box models\n- **Methods**: Physics-informed constraints, dynamic route visualization\n\n### 6. **Dataset Scale Explosion** 📈\n- **XXLTraffic**: 19,561 sensors (vs. METR-LA's 207)\n- **Trend**: From city-scale to state/country-scale prediction\n- **Challenge**: Ultra-dynamic forecasting at massive scale\n\n---\n\n## Recommendations for Next Steps\n\n### 1. **Clone Priority Repositories** (Week 1)\n```bash\n# Architecture novelty\ngit clone https://github.com/jasonz5/STGormer\ngit clone https://github.com/Rodger-Lau/SynEVO\ngit clone https://github.com/usail-hkust/CoLLMLight\n\n# Dataset coverage\ngit clone https://github.com/Onedean/EAC\ngit clone https://github.com/hqh0728/TimeBase\n```\n\n### 2. **Download ICDE 2025 Papers** (Week 2)\n- **Action**: Access via IEEE Xplore institutional subscription\n- **Papers**: 4 research papers on traffic prediction\n- **Priority**: Ultra-Flexible, Heterogeneous-Aware, Just-In-Time frameworks\n\n### 3. **Monitor Upcoming Publications** (Ongoing)\n- **KDD 2025**: August 2025 (papers not yet available)\n- **NeurIPS 2025 Workshops**: Check for traffic-specific workshops\n- **ICML/ICLR Workshops**: Look for spatiotemporal learning workshops\n\n### 4. **Benchmark Comparison Study** (Week 3-4)\n- **Datasets**: METR-LA, PEMS-BAY (standard benchmarks)\n- **Models**: STGormer, SynEVO, TimeBase, EAC\n- **Metrics**: MAE, RMSE, MAPE, inference time, parameter count\n\n---\n\n## Missing & Future Work\n\n### Papers We Couldn't Access:\n1. **ICDE 2025** papers (require IEEE subscription)\n2. **KDD 2025** papers (conference in August 2025)\n3. **LSTGAN** full PDF (SSRN download timeout)\n4. **MLCAFormer** PDF (PLOS One journal)\n5. **SRSNet** PDF (NeurIPS 2025 proceedings pending)\n\n### Conferences Not Yet Searched:\n- **AAAI 2025** (traffic AI applications)\n- **IJCAI 2025** (spatiotemporal reasoning)\n- **WWW 2025** (web-scale traffic data)\n- **SIGMOD 2025** (large-scale traffic databases)\n\n### Future Directions to Watch:\n1. **Foundation models for traffic** (large pre-trained models)\n2. **Multimodal traffic prediction** (vision + sensor fusion)\n3. **Zero-shot traffic forecasting** (new cities without training)\n4. **Real-time adaptive prediction** (online learning)\n5. **Climate-aware traffic models** (weather + traffic jointly)\n\n---\n\n## Files Saved\n\n### PDFs Downloaded (12 files):\n```\n/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/codex/data/articles/\n├── ICLR2025_WardropNet.pdf (1.6M)\n├── ICLR2025_CoLLMLight.pdf (11K)\n├── ICLR2025_ExpandAndCompress.pdf (1.6M)\n├── ICLR2025_PhyMPGN.pdf (3.7M)\n├── ICLR2025_RadarWeatherNowcasting.pdf (2.9M)\n├── ICML2025_SynEVO.pdf (1.5M)\n├── ICML2025_TimeBase.pdf (3.3M)\n├── ArXiv2024_STGormer.pdf (758K)\n├── ArXiv2025_EnhancingTrafficPrediction.pdf (...)\n├── ArXiv2024_LLMTrafficFlow.pdf (917K)\n├── ArXiv2024_XXLTraffic.pdf (...)\n└── ArXiv2024_LSTTN.pdf (...)\n```\n\n### Metadata Catalog:\n```\n/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/codex/data/articles/catalog.json\n```\n**Format**: JSON array with 20 papers\n**Fields**: title, conference, year, track, datasets, metrics, github, keywords\n\n---\n\n## Contact & Contributions\n\n**Compiled by:** Claude Code Assistant\n**Date:** November 24, 2025\n**Next Update:** Monitor ICDE 2025 proceedings (May 2025), KDD 2025 (August 2025)\n\nFor questions or contributions, please update the catalog.json file with new papers following the same schema.\n"}
