2025-11-25 04:37:53 | INFO | Tool Write called with {'file_path': '/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/codex/MODEL_PORTING_GUIDE.md', 'content': '# LibCity Model Porting Guide\n\nThis document describes the process of porting LSTGAN and MLCAFormer models into LibCity framework.\n\n## Models Ported\n\n### 1. LSTGAN (Long-term Spatio-Temporal Graph Attention Network)\n\n**Publication:** Expert Systems with Applications, 2025\n**Authors:** Brahim Remmouche, Doulkifli Boukraa, Anastasia Zakharova, Thierry Delot\n**Datasets:** METR-LA, PEMS-BAY\n**Repository Status:** Not available publicly (as of porting date)\n\n#### Architecture Overview\n\nLSTGAN combines graph attention mechanisms with temporal convolution for long-term traffic forecasting:\n\n1. **Graph Attention Layer**: Captures spatial dependencies between nodes with learnable attention weights\n2. **Temporal Convolution Block**: Models long-term temporal patterns using dilated convolutions\n3. **Spatio-Temporal Blocks**: Integrates spatial and temporal components with residual connections\n\n#### Model Parameters\n\n- `hidden_dim`: Hidden dimension size (default: 64)\n- `num_layers`: Number of ST blocks (default: 3)\n- `dropout`: Dropout rate (default: 0.1)\n- `num_heads`: Number of attention heads (default: 8)\n\n#### Usage\n\n```bash\npython run_model.py --task traffic_state_pred --model LSTGAN --dataset METR_LA\n```\n\n#### Configuration File\n\nLocation: `libcity/config/model/traffic_state_pred/LSTGAN.json`\n\n### 2. MLCAFormer (Multi-Level Causal Attention Transformer)\n\n**Publication:** PLOS One, 2025\n**Authors:** Hengyuan He, Zhengtao Long, Yingchao Zhang, Xiaofei Jiang\n**Institution:** College of Big Data and Information Engineering, GuiZhou University\n**Datasets:** METR-LA, PEMS-BAY, PEMS04, PEMS08\n**Repository Status:** Not available publicly (as of porting date)\n\n#### Architecture Overview\n\nMLCAFormer is a transformer-based model with multi-level causal attention:\n\n1. **Causal Multi-Head Attention**: Ensures temporal causality while capturing dependencies\n2. **Node-Identity-Aware Spatial Attention**: Uses unique node embeddings for spatial modeling\n3. **Multi-dimensional Input**: Integrates traffic data with cyclical patterns and embeddings\n4. **MLCA Blocks**: Combines temporal causal attention, spatial attention, and feed-forward networks\n\n#### Model Parameters\n\n- `d_model`: Model dimension (default: 64)\n- `num_layers`: Number of MLCA blocks (default: 3)\n- `num_heads`: Number of attention heads (default: 8)\n- `d_ff`: Feed-forward dimension (default: 256)\n- `dropout`: Dropout rate (default: 0.1)\n\n#### Usage\n\n```bash\npython run_model.py --task traffic_state_pred --model MLCAFormer --dataset METR_LA\n```\n\n#### Configuration File\n\nLocation: `libcity/config/model/traffic_state_pred/MLCAFormer.json`\n\n## Files Modified/Created\n\n### New Model Files\n\n1. `/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/LSTGAN.py`\n2. `/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/MLCAFormer.py`\n\n### New Configuration Files\n\n1. `/libcity/config/model/traffic_state_pred/LSTGAN.json`\n2. `/libcity/config/model/traffic_state_pred/MLCAFormer.json`\n\n### Modified Files\n\n1. `/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/__init__.py`\n   - Added imports for LSTGAN and MLCAFormer\n   - Added model names to `__all__` list\n\n## Implementation Details\n\nBoth models inherit from `AbstractTrafficStateModel` and implement:\n\n- `__init__(config, data_feature)`: Model initialization\n- `forward(batch)`: Forward pass\n- `predict(batch)`: Prediction interface for LibCity\n- `calculate_loss(batch)`: Loss calculation using masked MAE\n\n### Data Format\n\nBoth models expect:\n- **Input**: `batch[\'X\']` with shape `(batch_size, input_window, num_nodes, feature_dim)`\n- **Output**: Predictions with shape `(batch_size, output_window, num_nodes, output_dim)`\n\n### Loss Function\n\nBoth models use `loss.masked_mae_torch` with inverse scaling for evaluation.\n\n## Testing\n\nTo test the models:\n\n```bash\n# Test LSTGAN\npython run_model.py --task traffic_state_pred --model LSTGAN --dataset METR_LA --epochs 5\n\n# Test MLCAFormer\npython run_model.py --task traffic_state_pred --model MLCAFormer --dataset METR_LA --epochs 5\n```\n\n## TODO / Future Work\n\n### LSTGAN\n\n- [ ] Verify model architecture against paper when/if code is released\n- [ ] Tune hyperparameters on METR-LA and PEMS-BAY datasets\n- [ ] Add multi-head attention support (currently single attention)\n- [ ] Optimize temporal convolution dilation rates\n- [ ] Add support for dynamic adjacency matrix learning\n\n### MLCAFormer\n\n- [ ] Verify model architecture against paper implementation\n- [ ] Add cyclical pattern encoding (day-of-week, time-of-day)\n- [ ] Implement hierarchical attention (local to global)\n- [ ] Optimize multi-level attention structure\n- [ ] Add support for external features\n\n### General\n\n- [ ] Create dataset-specific configuration files\n- [ ] Run full benchmarks on all supported datasets\n- [ ] Compare performance with reported paper metrics\n- [ ] Document any deviations from original implementations\n- [ ] Add visualization tools for attention weights\n- [ ] Implement gradient checkpointing for memory efficiency\n\n## Notes\n\n1. **No Original Code**: These implementations are based on paper descriptions, as original code was not publicly available at the time of porting.\n\n2. **Adaptation Choices**:\n   - Used standard LibCity data formats and interfaces\n   - Implemented simplified versions that can be refined when original code becomes available\n   - Used masked MAE as loss function (standard in LibCity)\n\n3. **Verification Needed**: When original implementations become available, these models should be verified and updated to match exactly.\n\n## References\n\n1. Remmouche et al. "Long-term spatio-temporal graph attention network for traffic forecasting." Expert Systems with Applications, 2025.\n   - Paper: https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0957417425018639\n   - PDF: https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=5084788\n\n2. He et al. "Spatio-temporal transformer traffic prediction network based on multi-level causal attention." PLOS One, 2025.\n   - Paper: https://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371/journal.pone.0331139\n'}
