ed in paper\n```\n\n**Step 5: Contact Paper Authors**\n```\n# Request original implementation details\n# Clarify preprocessing steps\n# Verify hyperparameters\n# Ask about any undocumented techniques\n```\n\n### Scenario 4: Metrics Better Than Paper\n\n**Status:** 🎉 EXCELLENT (but verify)\n\n**Verification Steps:**\n1. Double-check metrics calculation\n2. Verify test set not contaminated\n3. Confirm evaluation protocol matches paper\n4. Document improvements for publication\n\n---\n\n## Metric Extraction Script\n\nOnce training completes, use this script to extract metrics:\n\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n"""\nExtract metrics from LibCity cache files\n"""\n\nimport os\nimport pandas as pd\nimport json\n\ndef extract_metrics(cache_dir, model_name, dataset_name):\n    """Extract MAE, RMSE, MAPE from LibCity cache"""\n\n    # LibCity stores results in evaluate_cache\n    eval_cache = os.path.join(cache_dir, \'evaluate_cache\')\n\n    # Find latest results CSV\n    csv_files = [f for f in os.listdir(eval_cache)\n                 if f.endswith(\'.csv\') and model_name in f and dataset_name in f]\n\n    if not csv_files:\n        return None\n\n    latest_csv = sorted(csv_files)[-1]\n    csv_path = os.path.join(eval_cache, latest_csv)\n\n    # Read results\n    df = pd.read_csv(csv_path)\n\n    metrics = {\n        \'model\': model_name,\n        \'dataset\': dataset_name,\n        \'MAE\': df[\'MAE\'].values[0] if \'MAE\' in df else None,\n        \'RMSE\': df[\'RMSE\'].values[0] if \'RMSE\' in df else None,\n        \'MAPE\': df[\'MAPE\'].values[0] if \'MAPE\' in df else None,\n        \'file\': csv_path\n    }\n\n    return metrics\n\n# Usage (after training):\ncache_dir = \'Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/cache\'\nresults = []\n\nfor model in [\'LSTGAN\', \'MLCAFormer\']:\n    for dataset in [\'METR_LA\', \'PEMS_BAY\', \'PEMS04\', \'PEMS08\']:\n        metrics = extract_metrics(cache_dir, model, dataset)\n        if metrics:\n            results.append(metrics)\n\n# Generate comparison table\ndf_results = pd.DataFrame(results)\nprint(df_results.to_markdown())\n```\n\n---\n\n## Recommended Follow-up Experiments\n\n### Phase 1: Baseline Validation (After Environment Fix)\n\n**Priority:** CRITICAL\n**Timeline:** 1-2 days\n\n1. **Quick Convergence Test (2 epochs)**\n   - Verify models train without errors\n   - Check loss decreases\n   - Confirm no NaN/Inf values\n\n2. **Short Training Run (10 epochs)**\n   - Get preliminary metrics\n   - Estimate convergence time\n   - Identify obvious issues\n\n### Phase 2: Full Metrics Collection\n\n**Priority:** HIGH\n**Timeline:** 1 week\n\n1. **LSTGAN Evaluation**\n   - METR-LA: 100 epochs\n   - PEMS-BAY: 100 epochs\n   - Collect all metrics (MAE, RMSE, MAPE)\n\n2. **MLCAFormer Evaluation**\n   - METR-LA: 100 epochs\n   - PEMS-BAY: 100 epochs\n   - PEMS04: 100 epochs\n   - PEMS08: 100 epochs\n\n### Phase 3: Performance Optimization\n\n**Priority:** MEDIUM\n**Timeline:** 2-3 weeks\n\n1. **Hyperparameter Tuning**\n   - Grid search on key parameters\n   - Learning rate optimization\n   - Architecture size variations\n\n2. **Feature Enhancement**\n   - Add cyclical time encoding (MLCAFormer)\n   - Implement hierarchical attention (MLCAFormer)\n   - Test dynamic adjacency learning (LSTGAN)\n\n### Phase 4: Extended Analysis\n\n**Priority:** LOW\n**Timeline:** 1 month\n\n1. **Ablation Studies**\n   - Remove graph attention (LSTGAN) - measure impact\n   - Remove causal masking (MLCAFormer) - measure impact\n   - Test different attention head counts\n\n2. **Cross-Dataset Generalization**\n   - Train on METR-LA, test on PEMS-BAY\n   - Analyze migration learning potential\n\n3. **Computational Efficiency**\n   - Memory profiling\n   - Speed optimization\n   - Multi-GPU scaling tests\n\n---\n\n## Current Status Summary\n\n### What We Have ✅\n\n1. **Complete Implementations**\n   - LSTGAN: 318 lines, syntax verified\n   - MLCAFormer: 365 lines, syntax verified\n\n2. **Ready-to-Run Configurations**\n   - LST