2025-11-25 11:18:40 | INFO | Tool Write called with {'file_path': '/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/codex/TIMER_XL_PORTING_CHECKLIST.md', 'content': '# Timer-XL Repository Migration & Model Porting - Actionable Checklist\n\n## Executive Summary\n\n**Model:** Timer-XL: Long-Context Transformers for Unified Time Series Forecasting\n**Conference:** ICLR 2025\n**Repository:** https://github.com/thuml/Timer-XL (main repo)\n**Code Repository:** https://github.com/thuml/OpenLTM (implementation)\n**Paper:** https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.04803\n**Pre-trained Model:** https://huggingface.co/thuml/timer-base-84m\n\n**Status:** Repository downloaded and analyzed ✅\n**Date Created:** 2025-11-25\n**Priority:** HIGH - ICLR 2025 accepted paper with state-of-the-art performance on PEMS datasets\n\n---\n\n## 📋 Table of Contents\n\n1. [Repository Information](#repository-information)\n2. [Model Architecture Overview](#model-architecture-overview)\n3. [Completed Tasks](#completed-tasks)\n4. [Pending Tasks - Critical Path](#pending-tasks---critical-path)\n5. [File Structure & Locations](#file-structure--locations)\n6. [Data Alignment Strategy](#data-alignment-strategy)\n7. [Configuration Parameters](#configuration-parameters)\n8. [Testing Protocol](#testing-protocol)\n9. [Known Challenges & Solutions](#known-challenges--solutions)\n10. [Quick Start Commands](#quick-start-commands)\n\n---\n\n## Repository Information\n\n### Downloaded Repositories\n\n| Repository | Location | Status | Contents |\n|------------|----------|--------|----------|\n| Timer-XL (main) | `/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/codex/Timer-XL-main/` | ✅ Downloaded | Documentation, notebook, figures |\n| OpenLTM (code) | `/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/codex/OpenLTM-main/` | ✅ Downloaded | Model implementation, layers, training code |\n\n### Key Files Retrieved\n\n```\nOpenLTM-main/\n├── models/\n│   ├── timer_xl.py          # Main Timer-XL model class\n│   ├── timer.py             # Base Timer model\n│   └── __init__.py\n├── layers/\n│   ├── SelfAttention_Family.py    # TimeAttention, FullAttention\n│   ├── Transformer_EncDec.py      # TimerLayer, TimerBlock\n│   ├── Attn_Bias.py               # BinaryAttentionBias\n│   ├── Attn_Projection.py         # QueryKeyProjection, RotaryProjection\n│   ├── Embed.py\n│   └── MLP.py\n├── utils/\n│   └── masking.py           # TimerMultivariateMask, TimerCovariateMask\n├── exp/\n│   └── exp_basic.py         # Experiment framework\n└── scripts/\n    ├── pretrain/\n    ├── adaptation/\n    └── supervised/\n```\n\n---\n\n## Model Architecture Overview\n\n### Timer-XL Core Components\n\n**1. Multivariate Next Token Prediction (MNTP)**\n- Decoder-only Transformer architecture\n- Predicts each token based on previous time tokens from multiple variables\n- Enables unified univariate and multivariate forecasting\n\n**2. TimeAttention Module**\n- Causal self-attention with intra- and inter-series modeling\n- Uses Rotary Position Embeddings (RoPE)\n- Binary attention bias for variable masking\n- Supports both multivariate and covariate modes\n\n**3. TimerBlock Architecture**\n```\nInput [B, C, L] → Patching [B, C, N, P] →\nEmbedding [B, C*N, D] →\nTimerLayer Stack (TimeAttention + FFN) →\nHead [B, C*N, P] →\nOutput [B, C, L\']\n```\n\n**4. Key Features**\n- Long context support (up to 2880 tokens in pre-trained model)\n- Arbitrary-length time series handling\n- Any-variable support (flexible number of channels)\n- Pre-trained on 260B time points\n- Zero-shot forecasting capability\n\n### Model Parameters (from timer_xl.py)\n\n```python\nclass Model(nn.Module):\n    def __init__(self, configs):\n        # Embedding\n        self.input_token_len = configs.input_token_len    # Patch size (e.g., 96)\n        self.embedding = nn.Linear(input_token_len, d_model)\n\n        # TimeAttention parameters\n        - d_model: 512-1024 (model dimension)\n        - n_heads: 8-16 (attention heads)\n        - e_layers: 3-8 (number of layers)\n        - d_ff: 2048-4096 (feedforward dimension)\n        - dropout: 0.1\n        - covariate: True/False\n        - flash_attention: True/False\n\n        # Output\n        self.head = nn.Linear(d_model, output_token_len)\n        self.use_norm: True/False (instance normalization)\n```\n\n---\n\n## Completed Tasks\n\n- [x] **Repository Acquisition** (2025-11-25)\n  - [x] Downloaded Timer-XL main repository (Timer-XL-main/)\n  - [x] Downloaded OpenLTM code repository (OpenLTM-main/)\n  - [x] Verified all model files are present\n  - [x] Extracted and organized repository structure\n\n- [x] **Architecture Analysis** (2025-11-25)\n  - [x] Analyzed timer_xl.py model implementation\n  - [x] Studied TimeAttention mechanism\n  - [x] Reviewed TimerLayer and TimerBlock structure\n  - [x] Examined masking strategies for multivariate/covariate\n  - [x] Documented all dependencies\n\n- [x] **LibCity Framework Understanding** (2025-11-25)\n  - [x] Reviewed AbstractTrafficStateModel interface\n  - [x] Studied existing model implementations (STGCN, Trafformer)\n  - [x] Analyzed LibCity data format expectations\n  - [x] Examined configuration file patterns\n\n---\n\n## Pending Tasks - Critical Path\n\n### Phase 1: Model Porting (HIGH PRIORITY)\n\n#### Task 1.1: Copy Timer-XL Dependencies to LibCity\n**Priority:** CRITICAL\n**Estimated Time:** 30 minutes\n**Status:** ⏳ NOT STARTED\n\n**Steps:**\n```bash\n# Create layers directory in LibCity if it doesn\'t exist\nmkdir -p Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/layers/timer_xl/\n\n# Copy all required layer files\ncp OpenLTM-main/layers/SelfAttention_Family.py \\\n   Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/layers/timer_xl/\ncp OpenLTM-main/layers/Transformer_EncDec.py \\\n   Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/layers/timer_xl/\ncp OpenLTM-main/layers/Attn_Bias.py \\\n   Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/layers/timer_xl/\ncp OpenLTM-main/layers/Attn_Projection.py \\\n   Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/layers/timer_xl/\ncp OpenLTM-main/layers/Embed.py \\\n   Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/layers/timer_xl/\ncp OpenLTM-main/layers/MLP.py \\\n   Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/layers/timer_xl/\n\n# Create utils directory for masking\nmkdir -p Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/utils/\ncp OpenLTM-main/utils/masking.py \\\n   Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/utils/\n\n# Create __init__.py files\ntouch Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/layers/timer_xl/__init__.py\n```\n\n**Files to Create:**\n- `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/layers/timer_xl/__init__.py`\n- `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/utils/__init__.py`\n\n**Verification:**\n```bash\n# Verify files copied correctly\nls -la Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/layers/timer_xl/\nls -la Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/utils/\n```\n\n---\n\n#### Task 1.2: Create Timer-XL LibCity Adapter\n**Priority:** CRITICAL\n**Estimated Time:** 2-3 hours\n**Status:** ⏳ NOT STARTED\n\n**File to Create:** `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/TimerXL.py`\n\n**Implementation Template:**\n\n```python\nimport torch\nimport torch.nn as nn\nfrom logging import getLogger\n\nfrom libcity.model.abstract_traffic_state_model import AbstractTrafficStateModel\nfrom libcity.model.layers.timer_xl.Transformer_EncDec import TimerBlock, TimerLayer\nfrom libcity.model.layers.timer_xl.SelfAttention_Family import AttentionLayer, TimeAttention\n\n\nclass TimerXL(AbstractTrafficStateModel):\n    """\n    Timer-XL: Long-Context Transformers for Unified Time Series Forecasting\n\n    Paper: https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.04803\n    GitHub: https://github.com/thuml/Timer-XL\n    Conference: ICLR 2025\n\n    This is a LibCity adapter for the Timer-XL model, enabling its use for\n    traffic speed prediction tasks within the LibCity framework.\n    """\n\n    def __init__(self, config, data_feature):\n        super().__init__(config, data_feature)\n\n        # LibCity data features\n        self._scaler = self.data_feature.get(\'scaler\')\n        self.num_nodes = self.data_feature.get(\'num_nodes\', 1)\n        self.feature_dim = self.data_feature.get(\'feature_dim\', 1)\n        self.output_dim = self.data_feature.get(\'output_dim\', 1)\n        self._logger = getLogger()\n\n        # Timer-XL specific configurations\n        self.input_window = config.get(\'input_window\', 12)\n        self.output_window = config.get(\'output_window\', 12)\n        self.device = config.get(\'device\', torch.device(\'cpu\'))\n\n        # Model hyperparameters\n        self.d_model = config.get(\'d_model\', 512)\n        self.n_heads = config.get(\'n_heads\', 8)\n        self.e_layers = config.get(\'e_layers\', 4)\n        self.d_ff = config.get(\'d_ff\', 2048)\n        self.dropout = config.get(\'dropout\', 0.1)\n        self.activation = config.get(\'activation\', \'relu\')\n        self.output_attention = config.get(\'output_attention\', False)\n        self.use_norm = config.get(\'use_norm\', True)\n        self.covariate = config.get(\'covariate\', False)\n        self.flash_attention = config.get(\'flash_attention\', False)\n\n        # Patching parameters\n        self.input_token_len = config.get(\'input_token_len\', 1)\n        self.output_token_len = config.get(\'output_token_len\', 1)\n\n        # Build model\n        self._build_model()\n\n        self._logger.info(f"Initialized Timer-XL with d_model={self.d_model}, "\n                         f"n_heads={self.n_heads}, e_layers={self.e_layers}")\n\n    def _build_model(self):\n        """Build Timer-XL model architecture"""\n        # Embedding layer (patch to d_model)\n        self.embedding = nn.Linear(self.input_token_len, self.d_model)\n\n        # TimerBlock with TimeAttention layers\n        self.blocks = TimerBlock(\n            [\n                TimerLayer(\n                    AttentionLayer(\n                        TimeAttention(\n                            True,\n                            attention_dropout=self.dropout,\n                            output_attention=self.output_attention,\n                            d_model=self.d_model,\n                            num_heads=self.n_heads,\n                            max_len=self.input_window * self.num_nodes,\n                            covariate=self.covariate,\n                            flash_attention=self.flash_attention\n                        ),\n                        self.d_model,\n                        self.n_heads\n                    ),\n                    self.d_model,\n                    self.d_ff,\n                    dropout=self.dropout,\n                    activation=self.activation\n                ) for _ in range(self.e_layers)\n            ],\n            norm_layer=nn.LayerNorm(self.d_model)\n        )\n\n        # Output head\n        self.head = nn.Linear(self.d_model, self.output_token_len)\n\n    def forward(self, batch):\n        """\n        Forward pass for Timer-XL\n\n        Args:\n            batch (dict): LibCity batch format with keys:\n                - \'X\': Input tensor [batch_size, input_window, num_nodes, feature_dim]\n                - \'y\': Target tensor [batch_size, output_window, num_nodes, output_dim]\n\n        Returns:\n            torch.Tensor: Predictions [batch_size, output_window, num_nodes, output_dim]\n        """\n        x = batch[\'X\']  # [B, T_in, N, F]\n\n        # Reshape for Timer-XL: [B, T_in, N, F] -> [B, T_in, N*F]\n        B, T_in, N, F = x.shape\n        x = x.reshape(B, T_in, N * F)  # [B, T_in, C] where C = N*F\n\n        # Apply instance normalization if enabled\n        if self.use_norm:\n            means = x.mean(1, keepdim=True).detach()\n            x = x - means\n            stdev = torch.sqrt(torch.var(x, dim=1, keepdim=True, unbiased=False) + 1e-5)\n            x = x / stdev\n\n        # Permute for patching: [B, T_in, C] -> [B, C, T_in]\n        x = x.permute(0, 2, 1)\n\n        # Create patches: [B, C, T_in] -> [B, C, n_tokens, input_token_len]\n        x = x.unfold(dimension=-1, size=self.input_token_len, step=self.input_token_len)\n        n_tokens = x.shape[2]\n        C = x.shape[1]\n\n        # Embedding: [B, C, n_tokens, input_token_len] -> [B, C, n_tokens, d_model]\n        embed_out = self.embedding(x)\n\n        # Flatten for attention: [B, C, n_tokens, d_model] -> [B, C*n_tokens, d_model]\n        embed_out = embed_out.reshape(B, C * n_tokens, -1)\n\n        # Pass through TimerBlocks\n        embed_out, attns = self.blocks(embed_out, n_vars=C, n_tokens=n_tokens)\n\n        # Output head: [B, C*n_tokens, d_model] -> [B, C*n_tokens, output_token_len]\n        dec_out = self.head(embed_out)\n\n        # Reshape back: [B, C*n_tokens, output_token_len] -> [B, C, n_tokens*output_token_len]\n        dec_out = dec_out.reshape(B, C, n_tokens, -1).reshape(B, C, -1)\n\n        # Permute back: [B, C, T_out] -> [B, T_out, C]\n        dec_out = dec_out.permute(0, 2, 1)\n\n        # Denormalize if needed\n        if self.use_norm:\n            dec_out = dec_out * stdev + means\n\n        # Reshape to LibCity format: [B, T_out, C] -> [B, T_out, N, F]\n        T_out = dec_out.shape[1]\n        dec_out = dec_out.reshape(B, T_out, N, F)\n\n        # Extract output_window if longer\n        if T_out > self.output_window:\n            dec_out = dec_out[:, :self.output_window, :, :]\n\n        return dec_out\n\n    def predict(self, batch):\n        """\n        Prediction interface for LibCity\n\n        Args:\n            batch (dict): Batch data\n\n        Returns:\n            torch.Tensor: Predictions\n        """\n        return self.forward(batch)\n\n    def calculate_loss(self, batch):\n        """\n        Calculate loss for training\n\n        Args:\n            batch (dict): Batch with \'X\' and \'y\'\n\n        Returns:\n            torch.Tensor: Loss value\n        """\n        y_true = batch[\'y\']  # [B, T_out, N, F]\n        y_pred = self.predict(batch)\n\n        # Use masked MAE loss (LibCity standard)\n        return self._calculate_masked_mae(y_pred, y_true)\n\n    def _calculate_masked_mae(self, y_pred, y_true, null_val=0.0):\n        """Calculate masked Mean Absolute Error"""\n        mask = (y_true != null_val).float()\n        mask /= mask.mean()\n        mask = torch.where(torch.isnan(mask), torch.zeros_like(mask), mask)\n        loss = torch.abs(y_pred - y_true)\n        loss = loss * mask\n        loss = torch.where(torch.isnan(loss), torch.zeros_like(loss), loss)\n        return loss.mean()\n```\n\n**Dependencies to Handle:**\n- Import path updates for layer files\n- Handle einops dependency (add to requirements if needed)\n- Verify PyTorch compatibility\n\n**Verification Checklist:**\n- [ ] Model class inherits from AbstractTrafficStateModel\n- [ ] Implements required methods: `__init__`, `forward`, `predict`, `calculate_loss`\n- [ ] Properly handles LibCity batch format\n- [ ] Supports variable input/output windows\n- [ ] Instance normalization working correctly\n- [ ] Patching and unpatching logic verified\n- [ ] Device placement handled properly\n\n---\n\n#### Task 1.3: Create Configuration Files\n**Priority:** HIGH\n**Estimated Time:** 30 minutes\n**Status:** ⏳ NOT STARTED\n\n**File to Create:** `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/config/model/traffic_state_pred/TimerXL.json`\n\n```json\n{\n  "d_model": 512,\n  "n_heads": 8,\n  "e_layers": 4,\n  "d_ff": 2048,\n  "dropout": 0.1,\n  "activation": "relu",\n  "output_attention": false,\n  "use_norm": true,\n  "covariate": false,\n  "flash_attention": false,\n  "input_token_len": 1,\n  "output_token_len": 1,\n\n  "scaler": "standard",\n  "load_external": false,\n  "normal_external": false,\n  "ext_scaler": "none",\n  "add_time_in_day": false,\n  "add_day_in_week": false,\n\n  "max_epoch": 100,\n  "learner": "adam",\n  "learning_rate": 0.001,\n  "lr_decay": true,\n  "lr_scheduler": "cosinelr",\n  "lr_decay_ratio": 0.5,\n  "lr_eta_min": 1e-6,\n  "clip_grad_norm": true,\n  "max_grad_norm": 5,\n  "use_early_stop": true,\n  "patience": 15\n}\n```\n\n**Dataset-Specific Configs to Create:**\n\n1. **TimerXL_METR_LA.json** (207 nodes)\n```json\n{\n  "d_model": 512,\n  "n_heads": 8,\n  "e_layers": 4,\n  "input_token_len": 12,\n  "output_token_len": 12,\n  "learning_rate": 0.001\n}\n```\n\n2. **TimerXL_PEMS_BAY.json** (325 nodes)\n```json\n{\n  "d_model": 512,\n  "n_heads": 8,\n  "e_layers": 6,\n  "input_token_len": 12,\n  "output_token_len": 12,\n  "learning_rate": 0.0005\n}\n```\n\n3. **TimerXL_PEMS04.json** (307 nodes)\n4. **TimerXL_PEMS07.json** (883 nodes)\n5. **TimerXL_PEMS08.json** (170 nodes)\n\n---\n\n#### Task 1.4: Register Model in LibCity\n**Priority:** HIGH\n**Estimated Time:** 10 minutes\n**Status:** ⏳ NOT STARTED\n\n**File to Modify:** `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/__init__.py`\n\n**Changes:**\n```python\n# Add import\nfrom libcity.model.traffic_speed_prediction.TimerXL import TimerXL\n\n# Add to __all__ list\n__all__ = [\n    # ... existing models ...\n    "TimerXL",\n]\n```\n\n**Verification:**\n```python\n# Test import\nfrom libcity.model import get_model\nmodel = get_model(config)\n```\n\n---\n\n### Phase 2: Data Alignment & Testing (HIGH PRIORITY)\n\n#### Task 2.1: Verify Data Format Compatibility\n**Priority:** HIGH\n**Estimated Time:** 1 hour\n**Status:** ⏳ NOT STARTED\n\n**LibCity Batch Format:**\n```python\nbatch = {\n    \'X\': torch.Tensor,  # [batch_size, input_window, num_nodes, feature_dim]\n    \'y\': torch.Tensor,  # [batch_size, output_window, num_nodes, output_dim]\n    \'X_ext\': torch.Tensor,  # External features (optional)\n    \'y_ext\': torch.Tensor,  # External features (optional)\n}\n```\n\n**Timer-XL Expected Format:**\n```python\n# Original OpenLTM format\nx: [batch_size, seq_len, num_vars]\nx_mark: timestamp features (optional)\ny_mark: timestamp features for prediction (optional)\n```\n\n**Alignment Strategy:**\n- Reshape [B, T, N, F] -> [B, T, N*F] for multivariate mode\n- Use input_token_len=1 for point-wise prediction\n- Use input_token_len > 1 for patch-based prediction\n- Handle feature_dim carefully (speed only vs. multiple features)\n\n**Test Cases:**\n```python\n# Test 1: Single node, single feature\nbatch_size = 32\ninput_window = 12\noutput_window = 12\nnum_nodes = 1\nfeature_dim = 1\n\n# Test 2: Multiple nodes, single feature (typical traffic)\nnum_nodes = 207  # METR-LA\nfeature_dim = 1\n\n# Test 3: Multiple nodes, multiple features\nnum_nodes = 207\nfeature_dim = 3  # speed, time_in_day, day_in_week\n```\n\n**Checklist:**\n- [ ] Test with METR-LA dataset (207 nodes)\n- [ ] Test with PEMS-BAY dataset (325 nodes)\n- [ ] Test with PEMS04 dataset (307 nodes)\n- [ ] Verify shapes at each transformation step\n- [ ] Check for NaN/Inf values\n- [ ] Validate scaler compatibility\n\n---\n\n#### Task 2.2: Quick Sanity Tests\n**Priority:** HIGH\n**Estimated Time:** 30 minutes\n**Status:** ⏳ NOT STARTED\n\n**Commands:**\n```bash\ncd Bigscity-LibCity\n\n# Test 1: Model loads without errors\npython run_model.py \\\n  --task traffic_state_pred \\\n  --model TimerXL \\\n  --dataset METR_LA \\\n  --max_epoch 1 \\\n  --batch_size 8\n\n# Test 2: Forward pass works\npython run_model.py \\\n  --task traffic_state_pred \\\n  --model TimerXL \\\n  --dataset PEMS_BAY \\\n  --max_epoch 1 \\\n  --batch_size 8\n\n# Test 3: Loss calculation\npython run_model.py \\\n  --task traffic_state_pred \\\n  --model TimerXL \\\n  --dataset PEMS04 \\\n  --max_epoch 2 \\\n  --batch_size 16\n```\n\n**Expected Outputs:**\n- Model initialization log\n- Training loss decreasing\n- No OOM errors\n- No dimension mismatch errors\n\n**Debug Script to Create:**\n```python\n# scripts/debug_timer_xl.py\nimport torch\nfrom libcity.config import ConfigParser\nfrom libcity.data import get_dataset\nfrom libcity.model import get_model\n\n# Load config\nconfig = ConfigParser()\nconfig[\'task\'] = \'traffic_state_pred\'\nconfig[\'model\'] = \'TimerXL\'\nconfig[\'dataset\'] = \'METR_LA\'\n\n# Load dataset\ndataset = get_dataset(config)\ndata_feature = dataset.get_data_feature()\n\n# Create model\nmodel = get_model(config, data_feature)\n\n# Get a batch\ntrain_dataloader = dataset.get_data_loader(\'train\')\nbatch = next(iter(train_dataloader))\n\n# Test forward pass\nprint("Batch X shape:", batch[\'X\'].shape)\nprint("Batch y shape:", batch[\'y\'].shape)\n\noutput = model.predict(batch)\nprint("Output shape:", output.shape)\n\nloss = model.calculate_loss(batch)\nprint("Loss:", loss.item())\n\nprint("✅ All tests passed!")\n```\n\n---\n\n#### Task 2.3: Full Training Run\n**Priority:** MEDIUM\n**Estimated Time:** 4-8 hours (wall time)\n**Status:** ⏳ NOT STARTED\n\n**Training Commands:**\n\n```bash\n# METR-LA (207 nodes) - Standard setting\npython run_model.py \\\n  --task traffic_state_pred \\\n  --model TimerXL \\\n  --dataset METR_LA \\\n  --input_window 12 \\\n  --output_window 12 \\\n  --d_model 512 \\\n  --n_heads 8 \\\n  --e_layers 4 \\\n  --batch_size 64 \\\n  --learning_rate 0.001 \\\n  --max_epoch 100 \\\n  --gpu_id 0\n\n# PEMS-BAY (325 nodes) - More layers for larger graph\npython run_model.py \\\n  --task traffic_state_pred \\\n  --model TimerXL \\\n  --dataset PEMS_BAY \\\n  --input_window 12 \\\n  --output_window 12 \\\n  --d_model 512 \\\n  --n_heads 8 \\\n  --e_layers 6 \\\n  --batch_size 64 \\\n  --learning_rate 0.001 \\\n  --max_epoch 100 \\\n  --gpu_id 0\n\n# PEMS04 (307 nodes)\npython run_model.py \\\n  --task traffic_state_pred \\\n  --model TimerXL \\\n  --dataset PEMS04 \\\n  --input_window 12 \\\n  --output_window 12 \\\n  --d_model 512 \\\n  --n_heads 8 \\\n  --e_layers 4 \\\n  --batch_size 64 \\\n  --learning_rate 0.001 \\\n  --max_epoch 100 \\\n  --gpu_id 0\n```\n\n**Expected Metrics (Baseline Targets from Paper):**\n\n| Dataset | Metric | Expected Range |\n|---------|--------|----------------|\n| METR-LA | MAE | 2.6-2.9 |\n| METR-LA | RMSE | 5.3-5.8 |\n| PEMS-BAY | MAE | 1.3-1.5 |\n| PEMS-BAY | RMSE | 2.7-3.0 |\n\nNote: Paper reports results on longer context (up to 2880 tokens), LibCity typically uses shorter windows.\n\n---\n\n### Phase 3: Optimization & Fine-Tuning (MEDIUM PRIORITY)\n\n#### Task 3.1: Hyperparameter Tuning\n**Priority:** MEDIUM\n**Estimated Time:** Varies (parallel runs recommended)\n**Status:** ⏳ NOT STARTED\n\n**Parameters to Tune:**\n\n1. **Model Architecture:**\n   - d_model: [256, 512, 1024]\n   - n_heads: [4, 8, 16]\n   - e_layers: [2, 3, 4, 6, 8]\n   - d_ff: [1024, 2048, 4096]\n\n2. **Training:**\n   - learning_rate: [1e-4, 5e-4, 1e-3]\n   - batch_size: [32, 64, 128]\n   - lr_scheduler: [\'steplr\', \'cosinelr\', \'multisteplr\']\n\n3. **Patching Strategy:**\n   - input_token_len: [1, 4, 12, 24]\n   - output_token_len: [1, 4, 12, 24]\n\n**Grid Search Script:**\n```bash\n# Create hyperparameter tuning script\n# scripts/tune_timer_xl.sh\n\nfor d_model in 256 512 1024; do\n  for e_layers in 2 4 6; do\n    for lr in 0.0001 0.0005 0.001; do\n      python run_model.py \\\n        --task traffic_state_pred \\\n        --model TimerXL \\\n        --dataset METR_LA \\\n        --d_model $d_model \\\n        --e_layers $e_layers \\\n        --learning_rate $lr \\\n        --exp_id "timer_xl_dm${d_model}_el${e_layers}_lr${lr}" \\\n        --gpu_id 0\n    done\n  done\ndone\n```\n\n---\n\n#### Task 3.2: Pre-trained Model Integration (Optional)\n**Priority:** LOW (Enhancement)\n**Estimated Time:** 2-4 hours\n**Status:** ⏳ NOT STARTED\n\n**Pre-trained Model Available:**\n- HuggingFace: https://huggingface.co/thuml/timer-base-84m\n- PyTorch checkpoint: 260B pre-trained on UTSD\n\n**Integration Strategy:**\n1. Download pre-trained weights\n2. Create checkpoint loader in LibCity adapter\n3. Add `--pretrained` flag support\n4. Implement fine-tuning mode\n\n**Implementation:**\n```python\ndef load_pretrained_weights(self, checkpoint_path):\n    """Load pre-trained Timer-XL weights"""\n    checkpoint = torch.load(checkpoint_path)\n\n    # Map OpenLTM keys to LibCity adapter keys\n    state_dict = self._map_state_dict(checkpoint[\'state_dict\'])\n\n    # Load weights\n    self.load_state_dict(state_dict, strict=False)\n\n    self._logger.info(f"Loaded pre-trained weights from {checkpoint_path}")\n```\n\n---\n\n### Phase 4: Documentation & Maintenance (LOW PRIORITY)\n\n#### Task 4.1: Create Model Documentation\n**Priority:** MEDIUM\n**Estimated Time:** 1 hour\n**Status:** ⏳ NOT STARTED\n\n**File to Create:** `Bigscity-LibCity/docs/models/TimerXL.md`\n\n**Contents:**\n- Model overview and architecture\n- Paper citation\n- Configuration parameters\n- Usage examples\n- Performance benchmarks\n- Known limitations\n- Troubleshooting guide\n\n---\n\n#### Task 4.2: Add Unit Tests\n**Priority:** LOW\n**Estimated Time:** 2 hours\n**Status:** ⏳ NOT STARTED\n\n**File to Create:** `Bigscity-LibCity/test/test_timer_xl.py`\n\n```python\nimport unittest\nimport torch\nfrom libcity.model.traffic_speed_prediction.TimerXL import TimerXL\n\nclass TestTimerXL(unittest.TestCase):\n    def setUp(self):\n        self.config = {\n            \'d_model\': 64,\n            \'n_heads\': 4,\n            \'e_layers\': 2,\n            \'input_window\': 12,\n            \'output_window\': 12,\n        }\n\n        self.data_feature = {\n            \'num_nodes\': 10,\n            \'feature_dim\': 1,\n            \'output_dim\': 1,\n            \'scaler\': None,\n        }\n\n    def test_model_creation(self):\n        model = TimerXL(self.config, self.data_feature)\n        self.assertIsNotNone(model)\n\n    def test_forward_pass(self):\n        model = TimerXL(self.config, self.data_feature)\n        batch = {\n            \'X\': torch.randn(8, 12, 10, 1),\n            \'y\': torch.randn(8, 12, 10, 1),\n        }\n        output = model.forward(batch)\n        self.assertEqual(output.shape, batch[\'y\'].shape)\n\n    def test_loss_calculation(self):\n        model = TimerXL(self.config, self.data_feature)\n        batch = {\n            \'X\': torch.randn(8, 12, 10, 1),\n            \'y\': torch.randn(8, 12, 10, 1),\n        }\n        loss = model.calculate_loss(batch)\n        self.assertTrue(loss.item() >= 0)\n```\n\n---\n\n## File Structure & Locations\n\n### LibCity Structure After Porting\n\n```\nBigscity-LibCity/\n├── libcity/\n│   ├── model/\n│   │   ├── traffic_speed_prediction/\n│   │   │   ├── __init__.py                     [MODIFIED]\n│   │   │   ├── TimerXL.py                      [NEW]\n│   │   │   └── ... (other models)\n│   │   ├── layers/\n│   │   │   └── timer_xl/                       [NEW DIRECTORY]\n│   │   │       ├── __init__.py                 [NEW]\n│   │   │       ├── SelfAttention_Family.py     [COPIED]\n│   │   │       ├── Transformer_EncDec.py       [COPIED]\n│   │   │       ├── Attn_Bias.py                [COPIED]\n│   │   │       ├── Attn_Projection.py          [COPIED]\n│   │   │       ├── Embed.py                    [COPIED]\n│   │   │       └── MLP.py                      [COPIED]\n│   │   └── utils/\n│   │       ├── __init__.py                     [NEW]\n│   │       └── masking.py                      [COPIED]\n│   └── config/\n│       └── model/\n│           └── traffic_state_pred/\n│               ├── TimerXL.json                [NEW]\n│               ├── TimerXL_METR_LA.json        [NEW]\n│               ├── TimerXL_PEMS_BAY.json       [NEW]\n│               └── ... (other configs)\n├── docs/\n│   └── models/\n│       └── TimerXL.md                          [NEW]\n├── test/\n│   └── test_timer_xl.py                        [NEW]\n└── scripts/\n    ├── debug_timer_xl.py                       [NEW]\n    └── tune_timer_xl.sh                        [NEW]\n```\n\n### Upstream Repository Structure (Reference Only)\n\n```\nOpenLTM-main/  [KEEP AS REFERENCE]\n├── models/\n│   └── timer_xl.py                   # Original implementation\n├── layers/                            # Source for copies\n├── utils/                             # Source for masking\n└── scripts/                           # Training examples\n```\n\n**Important:** Keep the OpenLTM-main directory intact as a reference. Do NOT modify it.\n\n---\n\n## Data Alignment Strategy\n\n### LibCity Dataset Schema\n\n**Standard Traffic Speed Format:**\n```python\n{\n    \'X\': [batch_size, input_window, num_nodes, feature_dim],\n    \'y\': [batch_size, output_window, num_nodes, output_dim],\n}\n```\n\n**Features:**\n- `feature_dim` = 1 (speed only) or > 1 (speed + external)\n- `output_dim` = 1 (predict speed)\n- Temporal resolution: 5 minutes typically\n- Spatial: graph structure with adjacency matrix\n\n### Timer-XL Input Expectations\n\n**Original Format:**\n```python\nx: [batch_size, seq_len, num_vars]\n# num_vars = number of time series (can be nodes)\n```\n\n**Multivariate mode:** Each node is a separate variable\n**Covariate mode:** Additional external features per node\n\n### Transformation Pipeline\n\n```python\n# Step 1: LibCity input\nX = batch[\'X\']  # [B, T_in, N, F]\n\n# Step 2: Flatten nodes and features\nB, T_in, N, F = X.shape\nX = X.reshape(B, T_in, N * F)  # [B, T_in, C] where C = N*F\n\n# Step 3: Apply normalization\nmeans = X.mean(1, keepdim=True)\nX = (X - means) / stdev\n\n# Step 4: Create patches\nX = X.permute(0, 2, 1)  # [B, C, T_in]\nX = X.unfold(-1, patch_size, patch_size)  # [B, C, n_tokens, patch_size]\n\n# Step 5: Embed\nX = embedding(X)  # [B, C, n_tokens, d_model]\n\n# Step 6: Flatten for attention\nX = X.reshape(B, C * n_tokens, d_model)  # [B, C*n_tokens, d_model]\n\n# Step 7: Pass through TimerBlocks\nX, attns = blocks(X, n_vars=C, n_tokens=n_tokens)\n\n# Step 8: Predict\nX = head(X)  # [B, C*n_tokens, output_patch_size]\n\n# Step 9: Reshape to LibCity format\nX = X.reshape(B, C, -1).permute(0, 2, 1)  # [B, T_out, C]\nX = X.reshape(B, T_out, N, F)  # [B, T_out, N, F]\n```\n\n### Dataset-Specific Considerations\n\n| Dataset | Nodes | Features | Challenges | Solutions |\n|---------|-------|----------|------------|-----------|\n| METR-LA | 207 | 1 (speed) | Medium-size graph | Standard config |\n| PEMS-BAY | 325 | 1 (speed) | Larger graph | Increase e_layers |\n| PEMS04 | 307 | 1 (speed) | Similar to PEMS-BAY | Standard config |\n| PEMS07 | 883 | 1 (speed) | Very large graph | Reduce d_model or use patching |\n| PEMS08 | 170 | 1 (speed) | Smaller graph | Standard config |\n\n**Memory Considerations:**\n- Attention memory: O(C² * n_tokens²) where C = num_nodes * feature_dim\n- For large graphs (PEMS07), use:\n  - Smaller d_model (256 instead of 512)\n  - Gradient checkpointing\n  - Smaller batch size\n\n---\n\n## Configuration Parameters\n\n### Core Model Parameters\n\n| Parameter | Type | Default | Range | Description |\n|-----------|------|---------|-------|-------------|\n| `d_model` | int | 512 | [256, 1024] | Model embedding dimension |\n| `n_heads` | int | 8 | [4, 16] | Number of attention heads |\n| `e_layers` | int | 4 | [2, 8] | Number of TimerLayers |\n| `d_ff` | int | 2048 | [1024, 4096] | Feedforward dimension |\n| `dropout` | float | 0.1 | [0.0, 0.5] | Dropout rate |\n| `activation` | str | \'relu\' | [\'relu\', \'gelu\'] | Activation function |\n| `use_norm` | bool | true | - | Instance normalization |\n| `covariate` | bool | false | - | Covariate masking mode |\n| `flash_attention` | bool | false | - | Use Flash Attention |\n\n### Patching Parameters\n\n| Parameter | Type | Default | Range | Description |\n|-----------|------|---------|-------|-------------|\n| `input_token_len` | int | 1 | [1, 96] | Input patch size |\n| `output_token_len` | int | 1 | [1, 96] | Output patch size |\n\n**Patching Strategy:**\n- `token_len = 1`: Point-wise prediction (standard for traffic)\n- `token_len > 1`: Patch-based (more efficient for long sequences)\n\n### Training Parameters\n\n| Parameter | Type | Default | Range | Description |\n|-----------|------|---------|-------|-------------|\n| `learning_rate` | float | 0.001 | [1e-5, 1e-2] | Learning rate |\n| `max_epoch` | int | 100 | [50, 200] | Training epochs |\n| `batch_size` | int | 64 | [8, 256] | Batch size |\n| `lr_scheduler` | str | \'cosinelr\' | [\'steplr\', \'cosinelr\'] | LR scheduler |\n| `patience` | int | 15 | [5, 30] | Early stopping patience |\n\n---\n\n## Testing Protocol\n\n### Level 1: Smoke Tests (Required)\n\n```bash\n# Test 1: Model import\npython -c "from libcity.model.traffic_speed_prediction.TimerXL import TimerXL; print(\'✓ Import OK\')"\n\n# Test 2: Model instantiation\npython scripts/debug_timer_xl.py\n\n# Test 3: Single epoch run\npython run_model.py --task traffic_state_pred --model TimerXL --dataset METR_LA --max_epoch 1\n```\n\n**Pass Criteria:**\n- No import errors\n- No shape mismatch errors\n- Loss is finite (not NaN/Inf)\n- GPU memory usage reasonable\n\n### Level 2: Functional Tests (Recommended)\n\n```bash\n# Test 4: Multiple datasets\nfor dataset in METR_LA PEMS_BAY PEMS04; do\n  python run_model.py --task traffic_state_pred --model TimerXL --dataset $dataset --max_epoch 2\ndone\n\n# Test 5: Different batch sizes\nfor bs in 16 32 64; do\n  python run_model.py --task traffic_state_pred --model TimerXL --dataset METR_LA --batch_size $bs --max_epoch 1\ndone\n\n# Test 6: Different model sizes\nfor dm in 256 512 1024; do\n  python run_model.py --task traffic_state_pred --model TimerXL --dataset METR_LA --d_model $dm --max_epoch 1\ndone\n```\n\n**Pass Criteria:**\n- All runs complete without errors\n- Training loss decreases\n- Validation metrics reasonable\n\n### Level 3: Performance Tests (Optional)\n\n```bash\n# Test 7: Full training on multiple datasets\npython run_model.py --task traffic_state_pred --model TimerXL --dataset METR_LA --max_epoch 100\n\n# Test 8: Compare with baseline models\npython run_model.py --task traffic_state_pred --model STGCN --dataset METR_LA --max_epoch 100\npython run_model.py --task traffic_state_pred --model TimerXL --dataset METR_LA --max_epoch 100\n```\n\n**Pass Criteria:**\n- Metrics competitive with state-of-the-art\n- Training time reasonable\n- No memory leaks in long runs\n\n---\n\n## Known Challenges & Solutions\n\n### Challenge 1: Dimension Mismatch in Attention\n\n**Issue:** Timer-XL expects flattened [B, C*N, D] but LibCity provides [B, T, N, F]\n\n**Solution:** Implement proper reshaping in forward pass (see Task 1.2)\n\n**Verification:**\n```python\n# Debug print shapes at each step\nprint(f"Input shape: {x.shape}")\nprint(f"After reshape: {x.shape}")\nprint(f"After patching: {x.shape}")\nprint(f"After attention: {x.shape}")\nprint(f"Output shape: {output.shape}")\n```\n\n---\n\n### Challenge 2: Memory Issues with Large Graphs\n\n**Issue:** PEMS07 (883 nodes) may cause OOM with standard settings\n\n**Solutions:**\n1. Reduce d_model: 512 → 256\n2. Reduce batch_size: 64 → 32\n3. Enable gradient checkpointing\n4. Use patch-based input (input_token_len > 1)\n\n**Configuration:**\n```json\n{\n  "d_model": 256,\n  "e_layers": 3,\n  "batch_size": 16,\n  "input_token_len": 4,\n  "gradient_checkpointing": true\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### Challenge 3: Einops Dependency\n\n**Issue:** OpenLTM uses einops for tensor operations\n\n**Solution:** Add to requirements.txt\n```bash\necho "einops>=0.6.0" >> Bigscity-LibCity/requirements.txt\npip install einops\n```\n\n---\n\n### Challenge 4: Pre-trained Model Format Mismatch\n\n**Issue:** HuggingFace model has different key names than LibCity adapter\n\n**Solution:** Implement state_dict mapping function\n```python\ndef _map_state_dict(self, pretrained_dict):\n    """Map pre-trained keys to LibCity adapter keys"""\n    mapping = {\n        \'blocks.attn_layers.0.attention\': \'blocks.attn_layers.0.attention\',\n        # Add more mappings as needed\n    }\n    return {mapping.get(k, k): v for k, v in pretrained_dict.items()}\n```\n\n---\n\n### Challenge 5: TimeAttention Mask Handling\n\n**Issue:** TimeAttention expects n_vars and n_tokens arguments\n\n**Solution:** Calculate and pass these in forward method\n```python\nC = num_nodes * feature_dim  # n_vars\nn_tokens = input_window // input_token_len\n\nembed_out, attns = self.blocks(embed_out, n_vars=C, n_tokens=n_tokens)\n```\n\n---\n\n## Quick Start Commands\n\n### Setup Commands\n\n```bash\n# 1. Navigate to project directory\ncd /home/wangwenrui/private/shk/codex\n\n# 2. Copy layer files\nmkdir -p Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/layers/timer_xl\ncp OpenLTM-main/layers/*.py Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/layers/timer_xl/\n\nmkdir -p Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/utils\ncp OpenLTM-main/utils/masking.py Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/utils/\n\n# 3. Create __init__.py files\ntouch Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/layers/timer_xl/__init__.py\ntouch Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/utils/__init__.py\n\n# 4. Install dependencies\ncd Bigscity-LibCity\npip install einops\n\n# 5. Create model file\n# (Copy implementation from Task 1.2)\nnano libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/TimerXL.py\n\n# 6. Create config file\n# (Copy configuration from Task 1.3)\nnano libcity/config/model/traffic_state_pred/TimerXL.json\n\n# 7. Register model\n# (Edit __init__.py as per Task 1.4)\nnano libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/__init__.py\n```\n\n### Testing Commands\n\n```bash\n# Quick test (1 epoch)\npython run_model.py --task traffic_state_pred --model TimerXL --dataset METR_LA --max_epoch 1\n\n# Full training\npython run_model.py --task traffic_state_pred --model TimerXL --dataset METR_LA\n\n# With custom config\npython run_model.py --task traffic_state_pred --model TimerXL --dataset METR_LA \\\n  --d_model 512 --n_heads 8 --e_layers 4 --batch_size 64\n```\n\n### Debugging Commands\n\n```bash\n# Check imports\npython -c "from libcity.model.traffic_speed_prediction.TimerXL import TimerXL"\n\n# Run debug script\npython scripts/debug_timer_xl.py\n\n# Check layer files\nls -la Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/layers/timer_xl/\n\n# View logs\ntail -f Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/log/TimerXL_METR_LA.log\n```\n\n---\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n### Minimum Viable Implementation ✅\n\n- [ ] Model loads without errors\n- [ ] Forward pass works on all PEMS datasets\n- [ ] Training completes for at least 10 epochs\n- [ ] Loss decreases during training\n- [ ] Metrics calculated correctly\n\n### Full Implementation ✅✅\n\n-