d prediction through config parameters.\n\n4. **Memory Management:** For large graphs, consider gradient checkpointing and mixed precision training.\n\n### Performance Expectations\n\nBased on paper results and typical traffic forecasting:\n\n| Dataset | Expected MAE | Expected RMSE | LibCity Baseline |\n|---------|--------------|---------------|------------------|\n| METR-LA | 2.6-2.9 | 5.3-5.8 | STGCN: ~3.0 MAE |\n| PEMS-BAY | 1.3-1.5 | 2.7-3.0 | STGCN: ~1.5 MAE |\n\nTimer-XL should be competitive or better than existing LibCity models, especially with longer context windows.\n\n---\n\n**Document Version:** 1.0\n**Last Updated:** 2025-11-25\n**Maintainer:** Claude Code Agent\n**Status:** Ready for implementation\n'}
