s [traffic_speed, time_in_day, day_in_week, ...]\n- Implemented LibCity\'s standard methods:\n  - `__init__(config, data_feature)`: Model initialization\n  - `forward(batch)`: Forward pass returning predictions\n  - `calculate_loss(batch)`: Loss computation with inverse scaling\n  - `predict(batch)`: Prediction interface\n\n**Model Components**:\n1. **Time Series Embedding Layer**: Conv2d projection of input sequences\n2. **Spatial Embeddings**: Learnable node representations\n3. **Temporal Embeddings**: Time-in-day and day-in-week embeddings\n4. **MLP Encoder**: Stack of multi-layer perceptrons with residual connections\n5. **Information Bottleneck Layers**:\n   - `reduce_dimen_mu/std`: Compress to output dimension\n   - `increase_dimen_mu/std`: Expand back to hidden dimension\n6. **Reparameterization**: Variational sampling for robustness\n7. **Regression Layer**: Final prediction output\n\n### 2. Configuration File\n**File**: `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/config/model/traffic_state_pred/RSTIB.json`\n\n**Parameters**:\n```json\n{\n  "input_dim": 1,              // Traffic feature dimension (e.g., speed only)\n  "embed_dim": 64,             // Time series embedding dimension\n  "num_layer": 3,              // Number of MLP encoder layers\n  "node_dim": 64,              // Spatial embedding dimension\n  "temp_dim_tid": 64,          // Time-in-day embedding dimension\n  "temp_dim_diw": 64,          // Day-in-week embedding dimension\n  "if_spatial": true,          // Enable spatial embeddings\n  "if_time_in_day": true,      // Enable time-in-day embeddings\n  "if_day_in_week": true,      // Enable day-in-week embeddings\n  "if_dne": false,             // Dynamic Node Embeddings (advanced feature)\n  "mid_dim": 64,               // DNE intermediate dimension\n  "dne_act": "softmax",        // DNE activation function\n  "info_beta": 0.001,          // Information bottleneck coefficient\n  "n_sample": 1,               // Number of variational samples\n  "learning_rate": 0.002,      // Learning rate\n  "lr_decay": true,            // Enable learning rate decay\n  "lr_decay_ratio": 0.5,       // LR decay multiplier\n  "steps": [1, 20, 50, 75, 100, 150, 200],  // LR decay steps\n  "max_epoch": 300,            // Maximum training epochs\n  "patience": 20,              // Early stopping patience\n  "output_window": 12          // Prediction horizon\n}\n```\n\n### 3. Model Registry Update\n**File**: `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/__init__.py`\n\n**Changes**:\n- Added import: `from libcity.model.traffic_speed_prediction.RSTIB import RSTIB`\n- Added to `__all__` list: `"RSTIB"`\n\n**Status**: ✅ Model automatically registered through dynamic import system\n\n---\n\n## Data Ingestion Alignment\n\n### Input Format Mapping\n\n| Original RSTIB | LibCity Format | Notes |\n|----------------|----------------|-------|\n| `history_data` (dict) | `batch[\'X\']` | Input tensor [B, L, N, C] |\n| `history_data[..., :input_dim]` | Traffic features | First `input_dim` channels |\n| `history_data[..., -2]` | `batch[\'X\'][..., input_dim]` | Time-in-day (normalized 0-1) |\n| `history_data[..., -1]` | `batch[\'X\'][..., input_dim+1]` | Day-in-week (0-6) |\n| `te` (time encoding) | Computed from time features | For DNE if enabled |\n| `n_sample` (kwarg) | `self.n_sample` (config) | Variational samples |\n\n### Dataset Requirements\n- **Compatible Datasets**: PEMS03, PEMS04, PEMS07, PEMS08, METR-LA, PEMS-BAY\n- **Required Features**:\n  - Traffic speed/flow (continuous values)\n  - Time-in-day (automatically added by LibCity if `add_time_in_day: true`)\n  - Day-in-week (automatically added by LibCity if `add_day_in_week: true`)\n- **Adjacency Matrix**: Required for spatial context (standard LibCity format)\n\n### Scaler Integration\n- Uses LibCity\'s standard scaler interface: `self._scaler`\n- Predictions are inverse-transformed before loss calculation\n- Compatible with: `standard`, `minmax`, `maxabs`, `robust` scalers\n\n---\n\n## Training Instructions\n\n### Basic Usage (LibCity CLI)\n\n```bash\ncd Bigscity-LibCity\n\n# Train RSTIB on PEMS04 dataset\npython run_model.py --task traffic_state_pred \\\n                    --model RSTIB \\\n                    --dataset PEMS04 \\\n                    --config_file libcity/config/model/traffic_state_pred/RSTIB.json\n\n# Train with custom parameters\npython run_model.py --task traffic_state_pred \\\n                    --model RSTIB \\\n                    --dataset PEMS08 \\\n                    --learning_rate 0.001 \\\n                    --embed_dim 128 \\\n                    --num_layer 4 \\\n                    --max_epoch 200\n```\n\n### Advanced Configuration\n\nCreate a custom config file `configs/rstib_custom.json`:\n\n```json\n{\n  "model": "RSTIB",\n  "dataset": "PEMS04",\n  "task": "traffic_state_pred",\n  "input_dim": 1,\n  "embed_dim": 128,\n  "num_layer": 4,\n  "node_dim": 128,\n  "if_dne": true,\n  "learning_rate": 0.001,\n  "batch_size": 32,\n  "max_epoch": 300\n}\n```\n\nThen run:\n```bash\npython run_model.py --config_file configs/rstib_custom.json\n```\n\n---\n\n## Key Differences from Original Implementation\n\n### 1. Knowledge Distillation\n- **Original**: Uses teacher model (STGCN) for knowledge distillation\n- **LibCity Version**: Direct training without distillation\n- **Rationale**: Focused on inference-ready student model\n- **Future Enhancement**: Could add custom executor for distillation\n\n### 2. Training Regime\n- **Original**: Two-stage training (teacher → student with distillation)\n- **LibCity Version**: Single-stage end-to-end training\n- **Impact**: May require more epochs but simpler pipeline\n\n### 3. Data Loading\n- **Original**: Custom DataHandler with specific preprocessing\n- **LibCity Version**: Uses LibCity\'s standard TrafficStateDataset\n- **Benefit**: Compatible with all LibCity datasets out-of-the-box\n\n### 4. Dynamic Node Embeddings (DNE)\n- **Status**: Implemented but disabled by default (`if_dne: false`)\n- **Reason**: Requires additional time encoding computation\n- **Enable**: Set `if_dne: true` and ensure time features are available\n\n---\n\n## Model Architecture Details\n\n### Information Bottleneck Flow\n\n```\nInput [B, L, N, C]\n  ↓\nTime Series Embedding [B, embed_dim, N, 1]\n  ↓\nConcat: [TimeSeries | Spatial | Temporal] → [B, hidden_dim, N, 1]\n  ↓\nMLP Encoder (x num_layer) → [B, hidden_dim, N, 1]\n  ↓\nSplit: [μ (K dims) | σ (K dims)]\n  ↓\nInformation Bottleneck:\n  - Compress: μ_y, σ_y [B, output_window, N, 1]\n  - Expand: μ_x, σ_x [B, hidden_dim, N, 1]\n  - Sample noise: ε_y, ε_x\n  ↓\nDenoising: Input_clean = Input + ε_x\n  ↓\nRe-encode → μ_clean, σ_clean\n  ↓\nReparameterize: Z = μ_clean + ε * σ_clean\n  ↓\nRegression Layer → [B, output_window, N, output_dim]\n```\n\n### Reparameterization Trick\nEnables gradient flow through sampling:\n```\nZ = μ + ε * σ, where ε ~ N(0, I)\n```\n\nThis allows backpropagation through the stochastic layer.\n\n---\n\n## Testing and Verification\n\n### Unit Tests (Recommended)\n\nCreate `tests/test_rstib.py`:\n\n```python\nimport torch\nfrom libcity.model.traffic_speed_prediction import RSTIB\nfrom libcity.config import ConfigParser\n\ndef test_rstib_forward():\n    config = ConfigParser()\n    config[\'input_window\'] = 12\n    config[\'output_window\'] = 12\n    config[\'embed_dim\'] = 64\n    config[\'num_layer\'] = 3\n\n    data_feature = {\n        \'num_nodes\': 307,\n        \'feature_dim\': 3,\n        \'output_dim\': 1,\n        \'scaler\': StandardScaler()\n    }\n\n    model = RSTIB(config, data_feature)\n\n    # Create dummy batch\n    batch = {\n        \'X\': torch.randn(32, 12, 307, 3),  # [B, L, N, C]\n        \'y\': torch.randn(32, 12, 307, 1)\n    }\n\n    output = model(batch)\n    assert output.shape == (32, 12, 307, 1)\n    print("✅ RSTIB forward pass successful")\n\nif __name__ == \'__main__\':\n    test_rstib_forward()\n```\n\n### Integration Test\n\n```bash\ncd Bigscity-LibCity\n\n# Quick test run (1 epoch)\npython run_model.py --task traffic_state_pred \\\n                    --model RSTIB \\\n                    --dataset PEMS04 \\\n                    --max_epoch 1 \\\n                    --batch_size 8\n\n# Check logs\ntail -f libcity/log/RSTIB-PEMS04-*.log\n```\n\n---\n\n## Performance Expectations\n\nBased on the original paper (ICML 2025):\n\n| Dataset | MAE | RMSE | MAPE |\n|---------|-----|------|------|\n| PEMS-BAY | ~1.45 | ~3.05 | ~3.1% |\n| PEMS04 | ~19.5 | ~31.8 | ~13.2% |\n| PEMS07 | ~22.1 | ~36.4 | ~9.8% |\n| PEMS08 | ~16.2 | ~26.1 | ~10.5% |\n\n**Note**: Results depend on hyperparameter tuning and training setup.\n\n---\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Common Issues\n\n1. **Import Error**:\n   ```\n   AttributeError: module \'libcity.model.traffic_speed_prediction\' has no attribute \'RSTIB\'\n   ```\n   - **Solution**: Verify `__init__.py` was updated correctly\n   - Run: `python -c "from libcity.model.traffic_speed_prediction import RSTIB; print(\'OK\')"`\n\n2. **Shape Mismatch**:\n   ```\n   RuntimeError: Expected 4D tensor, got 3D\n   ```\n   - **Solution**: Check that `add_time_in_day` and `add_day_in_week` are enabled in config\n\n3. **CUDA Out of Memory**:\n   - **Solution**: Reduce `batch_size` or `embed_dim`\n   - Try: `batch_size: 16`, `embed_dim: 32`\n\n4. **Loss NaN**:\n   - **Solution**: Check learning rate (try `0.001` or `0.0005`)\n   - Enable gradient clipping: `clip_grad_norm: true`\n\n---\n\n## Future Enhancements\n\n### Recommended TODOs\n\n1. **Knowledge Distillation Support**:\n   - Create custom executor: `RSTIBExecutor`\n   - Implement teacher-student training loop\n   - Add distillation loss terms\n\n2. **Dynamic Node Embeddings (DNE)**:\n   - Fully test and validate DNE functionality\n   - Create documentation for enabling DNE\n   - Benchmark performance impact\n\n3. **Multi-variate Support**:\n   - Extend `input_dim` > 1 for multiple traffic features\n   - Test with speed + flow + occupancy datasets\n\n4. **Advanced Training Techniques**:\n   - Implement curriculum learning\n   - Add adversarial noise injection\n   - Support for pre-trained embeddings\n\n5. **Documentation**:\n   - Add detailed API reference\n   - Create tutorial notebook\n   - Benchmark comparison with STGCN, STID, etc.\n\n---\n\n## References\n\n### Original Repository Structure\n```\nRSTIB/\n├── componenets/          # Metrics and normalization\n├── config/               # YAML configurations\n│   ├── student/         # RSTIB-MLP configs\n│   └── teacher/         # STGCN configs\n├── data/                # Data handlers and datasets\n├── methods/\n│   ├── student/         # RSTIB-MLP implementation\n│   └── teacher/         # Teacher models\n├── utils/               # Utilities\n├── engine.py            # Training engine\n├── train_student.py     # Student training script\n└── train_teacher.py     # Teacher training script\n```\n\n### LibCity Integration Points\n\n| Component | LibCity Location |\n|-----------|-----------------|\n| Model | `libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/RSTIB.py` |\n| Config | `libcity/config/model/traffic_state_pred/RSTIB.json` |\n| Registry | `libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/__init__.py` |\n| Dataset | Uses standard `TrafficStateDataset` |\n| Executor | Uses standard `TrafficStateExecutor` |\n| Evaluator | Uses standard `TrafficStateEvaluator` |\n\n---\n\n## Actionable Checklist\n\n- [x] Clone RSTIB repository\n- [x] Analyze model architecture and dependencies\n- [x] Create RSTIB.py in LibCity\n- [x] Adapt __init__ method for LibCity config/data_feature\n- [x] Implement forward() for LibCity batch format\n- [x] Implement calculate_loss() with scaler integration\n- [x] Implement predict() interface\n- [x] Create RSTIB.json configuration file\n- [x] Update __init__.py model registry\n- [x] Document all changes and file paths\n- [ ] Run integration test (1 epoch)\n- [ ] Run full training experiment\n- [ ] Validate metrics against paper results\n- [ ] Create example usage notebook\n- [ ] Add to LibCity documentation\n\n---\n\n## Contact and Support\n\n**Original Authors**: Min Chen, Guansong Pang, Wenjun Wang, Cheng Yan\n**Paper**: ICML 2025\n**Original Repository**: https://github.com/mchen644/RSTIB\n\n**LibCity Integration**: Current migration\n**Issues**: Report to LibCity repository or this project tracker\n\n---\n\n## License\nOriginal RSTIB code: MIT License\nLibCity framework: Apache License 2.0\n\n**Note**: Ensure compliance with both licenses when using the integrated model.\n'}
