ithout errors\n✅ **JSON Validation**: RSTIB.json is valid\n✅ **Import Path**: Model registered correctly\n⚠️ **Runtime Test**: Deferred due to environment dependency issues (sklearn/scipy version conflict)\n\n### 6. Documentation\n✅ **Files Created**:\n1. `RSTIB_MIGRATION_REPORT.md` (comprehensive 500+ line report)\n2. `RSTIB_CHECKLIST.md` (actionable checklist with testing guide)\n3. This summary document\n\n---\n\n## File Manifest\n\n| File Path | Lines | Purpose | Status |\n|-----------|-------|---------|--------|\n| `/RSTIB/` | - | Original repository clone | ✅ Complete |\n| `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/RSTIB.py` | 420 | Model implementation | ✅ Complete |\n| `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/config/model/traffic_state_pred/RSTIB.json` | 34 | Configuration | ✅ Complete |\n| `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/__init__.py` | 67 | Registry update | ✅ Complete |\n| `RSTIB_MIGRATION_REPORT.md` | 500+ | Detailed documentation | ✅ Complete |\n| `RSTIB_CHECKLIST.md` | 350+ | Testing checklist | ✅ Complete |\n\n---\n\n## Architecture Overview\n\n```\nRSTIB Model Structure:\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nInput: [B, L, N, C]\n  ├─ Traffic features: [B, L, N, input_dim]\n  ├─ Time-in-day: [B, L, N, 1]\n  └─ Day-in-week: [B, L, N, 1]\n\n↓ Time Series Embedding (Conv2d)\n\nEmbedding: [B, embed_dim, N, 1]\n  ├─ Time series embedding\n  ├─ Spatial embedding (learnable)\n  └─ Temporal embeddings (TiD, DiW)\n\n↓ Concatenate → [B, hidden_dim, N, 1]\n\n↓ MLP Encoder (×num_layer)\n\nHidden: [B, hidden_dim, N, 1]\n  ├─ Split → μ [B, K, N, 1]\n  └─ Split → σ [B, K, N, 1]\n\n↓ Information Bottleneck\n  ├─ Compress: μ_y, σ_y [B, T, N, 1]\n  ├─ Expand: μ_x, σ_x [B, hidden_dim, N, 1]\n  └─ Reparameterize: Z ~ N(μ, σ²)\n\n↓ Denoise & Re-encode\n\nEncoding: [B,K, N, 1]\n\n↓ Regression Layer\n\nOutput: [B, T, N, output_dim]\n```\n\n---\n\n## Training Configuration\n\n### Recommended Settings\n\n```json\n{\n  "model": "RSTIB",\n  "task": "traffic_state_pred",\n  "dataset": "PEMS04",\n  "input_dim": 1,\n  "embed_dim": 64,\n  "num_layer": 3,\n  "node_dim": 64,\n  "if_spatial": true,\n  "if_time_in_day": true,\n  "if_day_in_week": true,\n  "learning_rate": 0.002,\n  "max_epoch": 300,\n  "batch_size": 32\n}\n```\n\n### Usage Command\n\n```bash\ncd Bigscity-LibCity\n\n# Standard training\npython run_model.py --task traffic_state_pred \\\n                    --model RSTIB \\\n                    --dataset PEMS04\n\n# Custom config\npython run_model.py --config_file configs/rstib_pems04.json\n```\n\n---\n\n## Testing Guide\n\n### 1. Syntax Validation (✅ Passed)\n```bash\npython -m py_compile Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/RSTIB.py\n```\n\n### 2. Import Test (⚠️ Requires environment fix)\n```bash\ncd Bigscity-LibCity\npython -c "from libcity.model.traffic_speed_prediction import RSTIB; print(\'OK\')"\n```\n\n**Known Issue**: Current environment has sklearn/scipy dependency conflict\n**Solution**: Use a clean conda environment with:\n- Python 3.9\n- PyTorch 1.13.1\n- scikit-learn compatible with scipy\n\n### 3. Forward Pass Test\n```python\nimport torch\nfrom libcity.model.traffic_speed_prediction import RSTIB\n\nconfig = {\n    \'input_window\': 12, \'output_window\': 12,\n    \'embed_dim\': 64, \'num_layer\': 3,\n    \'device\': torch.device(\'cpu\')\n}\ndata_feature = {\n    \'num_nodes\': 307, \'feature_dim\': 3, \'output_dim\': 1\n}\n\nmodel = RSTIB(config, data_feature)\nbatch = {\'X\': torch.randn(8, 12, 307, 3)}\noutput = model(batch)\nprint(f"Output shape: {output.shape}")  # [8, 12, 307, 1]\n```\n\n### 4. Integration Test\n```bash\npython run_model.py --task traffic_state_pred \\\n                    --model RSTIB \\\n                    --dataset PEMS04 \\\n                    --max_epoch 1 \\\n                    --batch_size 8\n```\n\n---\n\n## Key Adaptations\n\n| Aspect | Original RSTIB | LibCity Version | Notes |\n|--------|----------------|-----------------|-------|\n| **Base Class** | `nn.Module` | `AbstractTrafficStateModel` | LibCity framework |\n| **Input Format** | `history_data` dict | `batch[\'X\']` tensor | Standard interface |\n| **Config** | YAML files | JSON + config dict | LibCity convention |\n| **Training** | Custom engine | LibCity executor | Unified pipeline |\n| **Knowledge Distillation** | Teacher-student | Direct training | Simplified (can be added) |\n| **Data Loading** | Custom DataHandler | TrafficStateDataset | Framework integration |\n\n---\n\n## Expected Performance\n\nBased on original paper (ICML 2025):\n\n| Dataset | MAE | RMSE | MAPE | Notes |\n|---------|-----|------|------|-------|\n| PEMS04 | 19.5 | 31.8 | 13.2% | 307 nodes, 5-min interval |\n| PEMS07 | 22.1 | 36.4 | 9.8% | 883 nodes |\n| PEMS08 | 16.2 | 26.1 | 10.5% | 170 nodes |\n| PEMS-BAY | 1.45 | 3.05 | 3.1% | 325 nodes |\n\n**Note**: Results may vary based on:\n- Hyperparameter tuning\n- Training setup (distillation vs. direct)\n- Random seed\n- Dataset preprocessing\n\n---\n\n## Pending Work\n\n### High Priority\n1. ⚠️ **Environment Setup**: Fix sklearn/scipy dependency for import test\n2. 🔄 **Runtime Validation**: Run forward pass test\n3. 🔄 **Integration Test**: 1-epoch training on PEMS04\n4. 🔄 **Full Training**: Complete experiment to validate metrics\n\n### Medium Priority\n5. 📝 **Knowledge Distillation**: Implement teacher-student training (optional)\n6. 🧪 **Multi-dataset Testing**: PEMS07, PEMS08, PEMS-BAY\n7. 📊 **Benchmark Comparison**: Compare with STID, STGCN, etc.\n\n### Low Priority\n8. 📚 **Tutorial Notebook**: Jupyter notebook walkthrough\n9. 🔧 **Advanced Features**: DNE examples, multi-variate support\n10. 📄 **LibCity PR**: Contribute to official repository\n\n---\n\n## Success Metrics\n\n| Criterion | Target | Status |\n|-----------|--------|--------|\n| Model code compiles | ✅ | ✅ PASS |\n| Configuration is valid | ✅ | ✅ PASS |\n| Model registered | ✅ | ✅ PASS |\n| Documentation complete | ✅ | ✅ PASS |\n| Import successful | ⚠️ | ⚠️ ENV ISSUE |\n| Forward pass works | 🔄 | Pending |\n| Training runs | 🔄 | Pending |\n| Metrics match paper | 🔄 | Pending |\n\n---\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Issue: Import Error (sklearn/scipy)\n**Symptom**: `ValueError: All ufuncs must have type numpy.ufunc`\n**Cause**: Version incompatibility between numpy, scipy, and scikit-learn\n**Solution**:\n```bash\nconda create -n libcity python=3.9 -y\nconda activate libcity\nconda install pytorch==1.13.1 -c pytorch\npip install scikit-learn==1.2.2 scipy==1.10.1 numpy==1.24.3\n```\n\n### Issue: Shape Mismatch\n**Symptom**: RuntimeError about tensor dimensions\n**Solution**: Ensure config has:\n```json\n{\n  "add_time_in_day": true,\n  "add_day_in_week": true\n}\n```\n\n### Issue: Loss NaN\n**Symptom**: Training loss becomes NaN\n**Solution**:\n- Reduce learning rate: `"learning_rate": 0.001`\n- Enable gradient clipping: `"clip_grad_norm": true`\n- Check data normalization\n\n---\n\n## References\n\n### Original Work\n- **Paper**: Information Bottleneck-guided MLPs for Robust Spatial-temporal Forecasting\n- **Conference**: ICML 2025 (Poster)\n- **Authors**: Min Chen, Guansong Pang, Wenjun Wang, Cheng Yan\n- **Repository**: https://github.com/mchen644/RSTIB\n\n### Related Work\n- **STID**: Spatial-Temporal Identity (baseline MLP)\n- **STGCN**: Spatio-Temporal Graph Convolutional Networks (teacher model)\n- **Information Bottleneck**: Tishby et al., The Information Bottleneck Method\n\n### LibCity Resources\n- **Documentation**: https://bigscity-libcity-docs.readthedocs.io/\n- **GitHub**: https://github.com/LibCity/Bigscity-LibCity\n- **Paper**: LibCity: An Open Library for Traffic Prediction\n\n---\n\n## Acknowledgments\n\nThis migration was completed as part of the Repository Migration & Model Porting stage. The implementation preserves the core Information Bottleneck mechanism while adapting to LibCity\'s framework conventions.\n\n**Special Thanks**:\n- Original RSTIB authors for open-sourcing their work\n