n**\n```bash\n# Standard scaler (default)\npython run_model.py --dataset PEMS04 --model RSTIB --scaler standard\n\n# MinMax scaler (paper version)\npython run_model.py --dataset PEMS04 --model RSTIB --scaler minmax\n```\n\n**Test 2: Hyperparameter Sensitivity**\n```bash\n# Learning rate\nfor lr in 0.001 0.002 0.005; do\n    python run_model.py --dataset PEMS04 --model RSTIB --learning_rate $lr\ndone\n\n# Embedding dimension\nfor dim in 32 64 128; do\n    python run_model.py --dataset PEMS04 --model RSTIB --embed_dim $dim\ndone\n```\n\n### 5.3 Comparison Analysis\n\n**Baseline Models** (run for comparison):\n1. STID (MLP baseline)\n2. STGCN (Paper\'s teacher model)\n3. GWNET (Graph-based baseline)\n\n**Comparison Table Template**:\n\n```markdown\n| Model | MAE | RMSE | MAPE | Params | Time (ms) | Improvement |\n|-------|-----|------|------|--------|-----------|-------------|\n| RSTIB (Ours) | ? | ? | ? | 504K | ~8 | Baseline |\n| RSTIB (Paper) | 19.5 | 31.8 | 13.2% | 510K | 8.2 | Reference |\n| STID | ? | ? | ? | 490K | ~9 | Compare |\n| STGCN | ? | ? | ? | 480K | ~12 | Compare |\n| Delta (Ours vs Paper) | ±? | ±? | ±?% | -1.2% | - | Analysis |\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. Troubleshooting Guide\n\n### 6.1 Common Issues and Solutions\n\n#### Issue 1: High Initial Loss (> 100)\n\n**Symptoms**: Loss doesn\'t decrease in first 10 epochs\n\n**Possible Causes**:\n1. Learning rate too high\n2. Batch size too small\n3. Data not normalized\n\n**Solutions**:\n```json\n{\n  "learning_rate": 0.001,  // Reduce from 0.002\n  "batch_size": 64,        // Increase from 32\n  "scaler": "standard"     // Ensure normalization\n}\n```\n\n#### Issue 2: Loss NaN After Few Epochs\n\n**Symptoms**: Loss becomes NaN after 5-20 epochs\n\n**Possible Causes**:\n1. Gradient explosion\n2. Division by zero in loss\n3. Numerical instability in IB layers\n\n**Solutions**:\n```json\n{\n  "clip_grad_norm": true,\n  "max_grad_norm": 5,\n  "info_beta": 0.0001  // Reduce from 0.001\n}\n```\n\n#### Issue 3: Poor Performance (MAE > 30 for PEMS04)\n\n**Symptoms**: Converges but metrics far from paper\n\n**Possible Causes**:\n1. Wrong data preprocessing\n2. Suboptimal hyperparameters\n3. Missing knowledge distillation\n\n**Solutions**:\n1. Check scaler: Try "minmax" instead of "standard"\n2. Increase epochs: 400-500 instead of 300\n3. Tune learning rate: Grid search [0.0005, 0.001, 0.002, 0.005]\n4. Implement distillation (future work)\n\n#### Issue 4: Slow Convergence\n\n**Symptoms**: Loss decreases very slowly, no plateau after 200 epochs\n\n**Possible Causes**:\n1. Learning rate too low\n2. Batch size too large\n3. Model underfitting\n\n**Solutions**:\n```json\n{\n  "learning_rate": 0.005,  // Increase\n  "batch_size": 16,        // Decrease\n  "embed_dim": 128,        // Increase capacity\n  "num_layer": 4           // Increase depth\n}\n```\n\n### 6.2 Expected Training Patterns\n\n#### Normal Training Curve\n\n```\nEpoch | Train Loss | Val Loss | Val MAE | Notes\n------|-----------|----------|---------|------\n1     | 85.3      | 82.7     | 45.2    | High initial loss\n10    | 42.1      | 40.3     | 32.8    | Rapid decrease\n25    | 28.5      | 27.8     | 25.3    | Steady improvement\n50    | 22.7      | 23.1     | 21.5    | Approaching target\n100   | 20.3      | 21.2     | 20.1    | Fine-tuning\n150   | 19.8      | 20.8     | 19.8    | Near convergence\n200   | 19.6      | 20.7     | 19.7    | Converged\n250   | 19.5      | 20.7     | 19.6    | Early stopping\n```\n\n**Pattern**: Exponential decrease → Linear decrease → Plateau\n\n#### Problematic Training Curve\n\n```\nEpoch | Train Loss | Val Loss | Issue\n------|-----------|----------|------\n1-10  | No change | No change | LR too low\n15    | NaN       | NaN       | Gradient explosion\n30    | 25.0      | 35.0      | Overfitting (val > train)\n100   | 50.0      | 48.0      | Not learning (too high)\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. Metrics Comparison Summary\n\n### 7.1 Expected Performance Summary\n\n| Dataset | Metric | Paper (Be