tions\n     - Multi-head self-attention layers\n     - Configurable number of layers and heads\n  6. **Grid Decoder**: Maps from grid back to target locations\n     - Cross-attention mechanism\n     - MLP for final processing\n  7. **Output Projection**: Final linear layer to output dimension\n\n- **Key Adaptations**:\n  - Simplified from original multi-modal architecture to single-modal for traffic data\n  - Uses LibCity\'s standard batch format: `{\'X\': ..., \'y\': ...}`\n  - Compatible with LibCity\'s scaler system for data normalization\n  - Integrated with LibCity\'s loss functions (masked MAE)\n\n#### ✅ Task 3: Register Model in LibCity\n- **Status**: COMPLETED\n- **Files Modified**:\n  - `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/__init__.py`\n    - Added import: `from libcity.model.traffic_speed_prediction.GriddedTNP import GriddedTNP`\n    - Added to `__all__` list: `"GriddedTNP"`\n\n#### ✅ Task 4: Create Configuration File\n- **Status**: COMPLETED\n- **File Created**: `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/config/model/traffic_state_pred/GriddedTNP.json`\n- **Configuration Parameters**:\n  ```json\n  {\n    "hidden_dim": 128,          // Hidden dimension for embeddings\n    "num_heads": 4,             // Number of attention heads\n    "num_layers": 3,            // Number of transformer layers\n    "dropout": 0.1,             // Dropout rate\n    "grid_size": 32,            // Size of latent grid\n\n    // Data processing\n    "scaler": "standard",\n    "load_external": true,\n    "add_time_in_day": true,\n    "add_day_in_week": true,\n\n    // Training\n    "max_epoch": 100,\n    "learner": "adam",\n    "learning_rate": 0.001,\n    "lr_scheduler": "cosinelr",\n    "clip_grad_norm": true,\n    "max_grad_norm": 5,\n    "use_early_stop": true,\n    "patience": 20\n  }\n  ```\n\n#### ✅ Task 5: Create Dataset Adapter & Automation Helpers\n- **Status**: COMPLETED\n- **File Created**: `scripts/gridded_tnp_adapter.py`\n- **Components**:\n  1. **GriddedTNPDatasetAdapter**:\n     - `adapt_batch()`: Convert LibCity batches to GriddedTNP format\n     - `create_spatial_features()`: Generate spatial embeddings from coordinates\n     - `process_irregular_grid()`: Handle non-uniform sensor deployments\n\n  2. **WeatherDataAdapter**:\n     - `convert_netcdf_to_libcity()`: Process NetCDF weather data (original paper used ERA5)\n\n  3. **Helper Functions**:\n     - `create_training_config()`: Generate training configurations\n     - `example_usage()`: Documentation with usage examples\n\n---\n\n## Data Ingestion & Compatibility\n\n### ✅ Dataset Schema Alignment\n- **Input Format**: `(batch_size, input_window, num_nodes, feature_dim)`\n- **Output Format**: `(batch_size, output_window, num_nodes, output_dim)`\n- **Verified Compatibility**: Compatible with LibCity\'s `TrafficStateDataset`\n\n### ✅ Scaler Integration\n- Uses LibCity\'s `scaler` object from `data_feature`\n- Supports inverse transform for loss calculation\n- Compatible with: standard, minmax, log, none\n\n### ✅ Adjacency Matrix (Optional)\n- Model does not require explicit adjacency matrix\n- Uses learnable spatial embeddings instead\n- Can optionally incorporate graph structure via spatial features\n\n---\n\n## LibCity Integration Details\n\n### Files Touched\n\n1. **Model Files**:\n   - ✅ `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/GriddedTNP.py` (NEW)\n   - ✅ `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/__init__.py` (MODIFIED)\n\n2. **Configuration Files**:\n   - ✅ `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/config/model/traffic_state_pred/GriddedTNP.json` (NEW)\n\n3. **Utility Scripts**:\n   - ✅ `scripts/gridded_tnp_adapter.py` (NEW)\n\n4. **Reference Directories**:\n   - ✅ `gridded-tnp/` - Original cloned repository with git history\n   - 📁 `DualCast-main/` - Reference (if exists in project)\n\n### Training via LibCity CLI\n\n```bash\n# Basic training\npython run_model.py --task traffic_state_pred --model GriddedTNP --dataset METR_LA\n\n# With custom parameters\npython run_model.py --task traffic_state_pred --model GriddedTNP --dataset PEMS04 \\\n    --hidden_dim 256 --num_layers 4 --grid_size 64\n\n# Specify input/output windows\npython run_model.py --task traffic_state_pred --model GriddedTNP --dataset PEMS_BAY \\\n    --input_window 12 --output_window 12\n```\n\n---\n\n## Model Parameters & Hyperparameters\n\n### Architecture Parameters\n| Parameter | Default | Description | Tuning Notes |\n|-----------|---------|-------------|--------------|\n| `hidden_dim` | 128 | Hidden dimension for embeddings | Increase for larger datasets (256, 512) |\n| `num_heads` | 4 | Number of attention heads | Must divide hidden_dim evenly |\n| `num_layers` | 3 | Number of transformer layers | More layers = higher capacity but slower |\n| `dropout` | 0.1 | Dropout rate | Increase for regularization (0.2-0.3) |\n| `grid_size` | 32 | Size of latent grid | Adjust based on spatial coverage |\n\n### Training Parameters\n| Parameter | Default | Description |\n|-----------|---------|-------------|\n| `learning_rate` | 0.001 | Initial learning rate |\n| `lr_scheduler` | cosinelr | Learning rate scheduler |\n| `max_epoch` | 100 | Maximum training epochs |\n| `batch_size` | 64 | Batch size (set via dataset config) |\n| `patience` | 20 | Early stopping patience |\n\n---\n\n## Testing & Validation\n\n### ✅ Smoke Tests\n```python\n# Test 1: Model instantiation\nfrom libcity.model.traffic_speed_prediction import GriddedTNP\nconfig = {\'hidden_dim\': 128, \'num_heads\': 4, \'device\': \'cpu\'}\ndata_feature = {\'num_nodes\': 207, \'feature_dim\': 2, \'output_dim\': 1}\nmodel = GriddedTNP(config, data_feature)\n\n# Test 2: Forward pass\nimport torch\nbatch = {\n    \'X\': torch.randn(8, 12, 207, 2),  # (batch, time_in, nodes, features)\n    \'y\': torch.randn(8, 12,207, 1)   # (batch, time_out, nodes, output)\n}\noutput = model(batch)\nassert output.shape == (8, 12, 207, 1)\n\n# Test 3: Loss calculation\nloss = model.calculate_loss(batch)\nassert loss.item() >= 0\n```\n\n### Recommended Validation Steps\n1. ✅ Test on small dataset (e.g., 1000 samples)\n2. ⏳ Compare with baseline models (DCRNN, STGCN)\n3. ⏳ Verify metrics calculation (MAE, RMSE, MAPE)\n4. ⏳ Test with different input/output windows\n5. ⏳ Validate on multiple datasets (METR_LA, PEMS04, PEMS_BAY)\n\n---\n\n## Known Issues & Limitations\n\n### Current Limitations\n1. **Simplified Architecture**:\n   - Original paper supports multi-modal inputs (station + grid data)\n   - Current implementation: single-modal for traffic sensors only\n   - **Future Work**: Add multi-modal support if needed\n\n2. **Grid Size Selection**:\n   - Default grid_size=32 may need tuning per dataset\n   - Larger grids = more capacity but higher memory usage\n   - **Recommendation**: Tune based on number of sensors and spatial distribution\n\n3. **Weather Data Integration**:\n   - Adapter provided but not fully tested with real ERA5 data\n   - **Action Required**: Test with actual NetCDF weather data if needed\n\n### Dependencies\n- All dependencies are standard PyTorch/LibCity requirements\n- No additional external dependencies needed\n- Optional: `xarray` for NetCDF weather data processing\n\n---\n\n## Performance Expectations\n\n### Original Paper Results\n- **Datasets**: ERA5 weather data, synthetic GP data\n- **Metrics**: Competitive log-likelihood, low prediction errors\n- **Strengths**:\n  - Handles irregular observations well\n  - Scalable to large spatial grids\n  - Flexible for various spatio-temporal patterns\n\n### Expected Performance on Traffic Data\n- **Hypothesis**: Should perform well on traffic speed prediction\n- **Advantages**:\n  - No explicit adjacency matrix required\n  - Learns spatial relationships via attention\n  - Handles missing data naturally\n\n- **To Benchmark Against**:\n  - DCRNN (strong baseline)\n  - STGCN (graph convolution baseline)\n  - MTGNN (graph learning baseline)\n\n---\n\n## Next Steps & TODO Items\n\n### Immediate Actions\n- [ ] Run initial training on METR_LA dataset\n- [ ] Benchmark against DCRNN baseline\n- [ ] Tune hyperparameters (hidden_dim, num_layers, grid_size)\n\n### Optional Enhancements\n- [ ] Add multi-modal support for external features (weather, events)\n- [ ] Implement original paper\'s translation-equivariant version\n- [ ] Add visualization tools for learned grid representations\n- [ ] Create pre-trained model checkpoints\n\n### Documentation\n- [x] Create this actionable checklist\n- [x] Document all file changes\n- [x] Provide usage examples\n- [ ] Add results/benchmarks once training is complete\n\n---\n\n## References & Resources\n\n### Original Paper\n- **arXiv**: https://arxiv.org/pdf/2410.06731\n- **Code**: https://github.com/cambridge-mlg/gridded-tnp\n- **Authors**: Ashman, Diaconu, Langezaal, Weller, Turner\n\n### LibCity Documentation\n- **GitHub**: https://github.com/LibCity/Bigscity-LibCity\n- **Docs**: https://bigscity-libcity-docs.readthedocs.io/\n\n### Related Work\n- Transformer Neural Processes (TNP)\n- Convolutional Conditional Neural Processes (ConvCNP)\n- Spatio-temporal neural processes\n\n---\n\n## Contact & Support\n\nFor issues or questions about this migration:\n1. Check original GriddedTNP repository issues\n2. Refer to LibCity model development guide\n3. Review this checklist for implementation details\n\n---\n\n**Migration Completed**: 2025-11-25\n**Status**: Ready for training and evaluation\n**Total Files Created**: 3\n**Total Files Modified**: 1\n**Lines of Code Added**: ~500\n'}
