erparameters for best performance\n```json\n{\n  "hidden_dim": 256,\n  "num_layers": 6,\n  "grid_size": 64,\n  "num_heads": 8\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. Recommended Experiments\n\n### 6.1 Experiment Plan\n\n#### Phase 1: Baseline Validation (Week 1)\n**Goal**: Verify model trains successfully and achieves reasonable performance\n\n| Experiment | Dataset | Config | Expected Time | Priority |\n|------------|---------|--------|---------------|----------|\n| 1.1 Smoke Test | METR-LA | Default (5 epochs) | 30 min | 🔴 Critical |\n| 1.2 Full Training | METR-LA | Default (100 epochs) | 4 hours | 🔴 Critical |\n| 1.3 Baseline Compare | METR-LA | Default | 1 hour | 🔴 Critical |\n\n**Success Criteria**: MAE within 20% of DCRNN baseline\n\n#### Phase 2: Hyperparameter Tuning (Week 2)\n**Goal**: Match or exceed baseline performance\n\n| Experiment | Parameter | Values | Expected Gain |\n|------------|-----------|--------|---------------|\n| 2.1 Hidden Dim | hidden_dim | [128, 256, 512] | +10-15% |\n| 2.2 Grid Size | grid_size | [16, 32, 64, 128] | +5-10% |\n| 2.3 Num Layers | num_layers | [2, 3, 4, 6] | +5-10% |\n| 2.4 Learning Rate | lr | [0.0001, 0.0005, 0.001] | +3-5% |\n\n**Success Criteria**: Match or beat best baseline (MTGNN/GWNET)\n\n#### Phase 3: Multi-Dataset Validation (Week 3)\n**Goal**: Verify generalization across datasets\n\n| Experiment | Dataset | Config | Notes |\n|------------|---------|--------|-------|\n| 3.1 PEMS04 | PEMS04 | Best from Phase 2 | Larger dataset |\n| 3.2 PEMS-BAY | PEMS-BAY | Best from Phase 2 | Different region |\n| 3.3 Cross-Dataset | Train METR-LA, Test PEMS04 | Best config | Generalization test |\n\n**Success Criteria**: Consistent performance across datasets\n\n#### Phase 4: Advanced Features (Week 4)\n**Goal**: Explore enhancements and ablations\n\n| Experiment | Feature | Expected Impact |\n|------------|---------|-----------------|\n| 4.1 Multi-Modal | Add weather data | +5-10% (if available) |\n| 4.2 Larger Grid | grid_size=128 | +3-5% |\n| 4.3 External Features | time-of-day, day-of-week | +2-5% |\n| 4.4 Ensemble | Multiple seeds | +2-3% |\n\n---\n\n## 7. Metrics Tracking Template\n\n### 7.1 Standard Metrics (LibCity Format)\n\n**Masked MAE** (Primary Metric)\n```python\ndef masked_mae_torch(y_pred, y_true, null_val=0.0):\n    """\n    Masked Mean Absolute Error\n    Used when certain values should be ignored (e.g., missing data)\n    """\n    mask = (y_true != null_val).float()\n    mask /= mask.mean()\n    loss = torch.abs(y_pred - y_true)\n    loss = loss * mask\n    loss[torch.isnan(loss)] = 0\n    return loss.mean()\n```\n\n**Masked RMSE**\n```python\ndef masked_rmse_torch(y_pred, y_true, null_val=0.0):\n    """\n    Masked Root Mean Squared Error\n    """\n    mask = (y_true != null_val).float()\n    mask /= mask.mean()\n    loss = (y_pred - y_true) ** 2\n    loss = loss * mask\n    loss[torch.isnan(loss)] = 0\n    return torch.sqrt(loss.mean())\n```\n\n**Masked MAPE**\n```python\ndef masked_mape_torch(y_pred, y_true, null_val=0.0):\n    """\n    Masked Mean Absolute Percentage Error\n    """\n    mask = (y_true != null_val).float()\n    mask /= mask.mean()\n    loss = torch.abs((y_pred - y_true) / y_true)\n    loss = loss * mask\n    loss[torch.isnan(loss)] = 0\n    return loss.mean() * 100\n```\n\n### 7.2 Results Template\n\n```markdown\n## GriddedTNP - Training Results\n\n### Configuration\n- Model: GriddedTNP\n- Dataset: [DATASET_NAME]\n- Config File: `GriddedTNP.json`\n- Hyperparameters:\n  - hidden_dim: [VALUE]\n  - num_layers: [VALUE]\n  - grid_size: [VALUE]\n  - learning_rate: [VALUE]\n  - batch_size: [VALUE]\n\n### Training Metrics\n- Total Epochs: [VALUE]/100\n- Best Epoch: [VALUE]\n- Training Time: [VALUE] hours\n- GPU: [MODEL]\n\n### Test Set Performance\n\n| Metric | 15 min | 30 min | 60 min | Average |\n|--------|--------|--------|--------|---------|\n| MAE | [VAL] | [VAL] | [VAL] | **[VAL]** |\n| RMSE | [VAL] | [VAL] | [VAL] | **[VAL]** |\n| MAPE | [VAL]% | [VAL]% | [VAL]% | **[VAL]%** |\n\n### Comparison with Baselines\n\n| Model | MAE | RMSE | MAPE | Δ vs GriddedTNP |\n|-------|-----|------|------|-----------------|\n| DCRNN | [VAL] | [VAL] | [VAL]% | [+/-X%] |\n| STGCN | [VAL] | [VAL] | [VAL]% | [+/-X%] |\n| GWNET | [VAL] | [VAL] | [VAL]% | [+/-X%] |\n| MTGNN | [VAL] | [VAL] | [VAL]% | [+/-X%] |\n| **GriddedTNP** | **[VAL]** | **[VAL]** | **[VAL]%** | **Baseline** |\n\n### Analysis\n[Discussion of results, deltas, and potential improvements]\n```\n\n---\n\n## 8. Paper vs. Implementation Comparison\n\n### 8.1 Feature Comparison\n\n| Feature | Original Paper | LibCity Implementation | Status |\n|---------|----------------|------------------------|--------|\n| Grid Encoder | ✅ PT-GE, KI-GE, SetConv | ✅ Simplified attention-based | ✅ Core functionality |\n| Grid Decoder | ✅ MHCA-GD | ✅ Multi-head cross-attention | ✅ Implemented |\n| Transformer | ✅ GriddedTransformerEncoder | ✅ Standard TransformerEncoder | ✅ Implemented |\n| Spatial Embed | ✅ Learnable | ✅ Learnable per-node | ✅ Implemented |\n| Temporal Embed | ✅ Learnable | ✅ Learnable per-timestep | ✅ Implemented |\n| Multi-Modal | ✅ Station + Grid | ❌ Single modal | ⚠️ Simplified |\n| Translation Equiv | ✅ TE-TNP variant | ❌ Not implemented | ⚠️ Future work |\n| SWIN Attention | ✅ Hierarchical | ❌ Standard attention | ⚠️ Simplified |\n\n**Implementation Coverage**: ~70% of paper features (core functionality complete)\n\n### 8.2 Quantitative Comparison\n\n**Paper\'s Best Configuration**:\n```json\n{\n  "model": "Swin-TNP",\n  "grid_encoder": "PT-GE",\n  "hidden_dim": 256,\n  "num_layers": 6,\n  "num_heads": 8,\n  "grid_size": 64,\n  "dropout": 0.1\n}\n```\n\n**LibCity Default Configuration**:\n```json\n{\n  "model": "GriddedTNP",\n  "grid_encoder": "Attention-based",\n  "hidden_dim": 128,\n  "num_layers": 3,\n  "num_heads": 4,\n  "grid_size": 32,\n  "dropout": 0.1\n}\n```\n\n**Capacity Difference**:\n- Paper: ~5-10M parameters (with SWIN attention)\n- LibCity: ~1.2M parameters (default config)\n- **Ratio**: ~4-8x smaller\n\n**Expected Performance Impact**: -15% to -25%\n\n---\n\n## 9. Corrective Actions Plan\n\n### 9.1 If Performance is Below Expected\n\n**Scenario 1: MAE 20-30% worse than baselines**\n\n**Root Cause Analysis**:\n1. Check data preprocessing (scaler, normalization)\n2. Verify loss function (masked MAE implementation)\n3. Review learning rate schedule\n4. Check for gradient issues (exploding/vanishing)\n\n**Corrective Actions**:\n```python\n# Action 1: Increase model capacity\nconfig[\'hidden_dim\'] = 256  # Was: 128\nconfig[\'num_layers\'] = 4    # Was: 3\nconfig[\'grid_size\'] = 64    # Was: 32\n\n# Action 2: Adjust learning rate\nconfig[\'learning_rate\'] = 0.0005  # Was: 0.001\nconfig[\'lr_warmup_epoch\'] = 10    # Add warmup\n\n# Action 3: Increase training time\nconfig[\'max_epoch\'] = 150  # Was: 100\nconfig[\'patience\'] = 30    # Was: 20\n```\n\n**Scenario 2: Training unstable (NaN loss)**\n\n**Corrective Actions**:\n```python\n# Action 1: Gradient clipping\nconfig[\'clip_grad_norm\'] = True\nconfig[\'max_grad_norm\'] = 1.0  # Reduce from 5.0\n\n# Action 2: Lower learning rate\nconfig[\'learning_rate\'] = 0.0001\n\n# Action 3: Add layer normalization\n# Already in model, verify it\'s active\n\n# Action 4: Check for numerical issues\n# Add assertions in forward pass\n```\n\n**Scenario 3: Overfitting (large train-val gap)**\n\n**Corrective Actions**:\n```python\n# Action 1: Increase dropout\nconfig[\'dropout\'] = 0.2  # Was: 0.1\n\n# Action 2: Reduce model capacity\nconfig[\'hidden_dim\'] = 64   # Was: 128\nconfig[\'num_layers\'] = 2    # Was: 3\n\n# Action 3: Add weight decay\nconfig[\'weight_decay\'] = 0.0001\n\n# Action 4: Data augmentation\n# Add noise to inputs during training\n```\n\n### 9.2 Retry Plan\n\n**Quick Retry** (if first run fails):\n1. Fix environment dependencies\n2. Run smoke test (5 epochs)\n3. Verify loss is decreasing\n4. If OK → full training\n5. If not → debug and retry\n\n**Full Retry** (if results 