es, Foursquare\n- **General Time Series**: ETT, Weather, Electricity, Solar-Energy\n- **Federated/Custom**: PEMS-Stream, TUMTraf, Urban networks\n\n---\n\n## Common Metrics\n\n### Traffic-Specific Metrics\n- **MAE** (Mean Absolute Error) - 18 papers\n- **RMSE** (Root Mean Squared Error) - 8 papers\n- **MAPE** (Mean Absolute Percentage Error) - 3 papers\n- **MSE** (Mean Squared Error) - 15 papers\n\n### Trajectory Prediction Metrics\n- **minADE** (Minimum Average Displacement Error)\n- **minFDE** (Minimum Final Displacement Error)\n- **MR** (Miss Rate)\n\n### Probabilistic Metrics\n- **CRPS** (Continuous Ranked Probability Score) - 3 papers\n- **Log-likelihood**\n\n### Other Metrics\n- **MRR** (Mean Reciprocal Rank)\n- **Hits@k**\n- **Accuracy improvements**\n- **Efficiency metrics** (training speed, memory usage)\n\n---\n\n## Key Research Themes\n\n### 1. **Spatial-Temporal Modeling** (28 papers)\n- Graph Neural Networks for traffic\n- Spatio-temporal transformers\n- Dynamic spatial modeling\n- Continual learning approaches\n\n### 2. **Efficiency & Scalability** (8 papers)\n- Large-scale traffic forecasting\n- Lightweight models\n- Efficient transformers\n- Minimal parameter approaches\n\n### 3. **Advanced Architectures** (12 papers)\n- Foundation models\n- Diffusion models\n- Flow matching\n- Koopman operators\n- Neural processes\n\n### 4. **Privacy & Federated Learning** (5 papers)\n- Differential privacy\n- Federated traffic prediction\n- Privacy-preserving frameworks\n\n### 5. **Migration Learning & Adaptation** (6 papers)\n- Cross-domain adaptation\n- Test-time adaptation\n- Continual learning\n- Zero-shot forecasting\n\n### 6. **Probabilistic Forecasting** (5 papers)\n- Uncertainty quantification\n- Probabilistic time series models\n- Gaussian processes\n\n---\n\n## Notable Spotlight/OralPapers\n\n### ICML 2025 Spotlights (5 papers)\n1. **SynEVO** - Cross-domain adaptation with 42% improvement\n2. **TimeBase** - Minimalist long-term forecasting\n3. **K²VAE** - Koopman-Kalman enhanced VAE\n4. **Privacy Amplification** - Differential privacy for time series\n5. **Gridded TNP** - Transformer neural processes\n\n### NeurIPS 2025 Spotlights (1 paper)\n1. **SRSNet** - Selective representation spaces\n\n### Key Innovations\n- **PatchSTG (KDD)**: 10× training speed, 4× memory efficiency\n- **WardropNet (ICLR)**: 72% improvement on traffic equilibria\n- **EAC (ICLR)**: Continual learning without catastrophic forgetting\n- **FUSE-Traffic (SIGSPATIAL)**: Event-aware forecasting\n\n---\n\n## Research Gaps & Future Directions\n\n### Identified Gaps\n1. **Limited real-time traffic prediction** - Only 2 papers address just-in-time/real-time scenarios\n2. **Event-aware forecasting** - Only 1 paper (FUSE-Traffic) explicitly handles events\n3. **Explainability** - Limited focus on interpretability (1-2 papers)\n4. **Dynamic road networks** - Few papers handle evolving network topology\n\n### Emerging Trends\n1. **Foundation models** for traffic (Timer-XL, TimeBase, FlowState)\n2. **Federated learning** for privacy-preserving traffic prediction\n3. **Continual learning** for streaming traffic data\n4. **Cross-domain adaptation** for zero-shot prediction\n5. **Integration with LLMs** (TimeKD using language models)\n\n### Underexplored Areas\n1. **Multi-modal traffic prediction** (combining vision, sensors, text)\n2. **Causal traffic forecasting**\n3. **Long-horizon prediction** (>24 hours)\n4. **Extreme event handling**\n5. **Energy-efficient models** for edge deployment\n\n---\n\n## PDF Download Status\n\n✅ **21 PDFs Successfully Downloaded** (58.3%)\n\n### Downloaded Papers by Conference\n- **ICLR 2025**: 6/7 (85.7%)\n- **ICML 2025**: 10/13 (76.9%)\n- **NeurIPS 2025**: 2/4 (50.0%)\n- **KDD 2025**: 2/3 (66.7%)\n- **ICDE 2025**: 1/8 (12.5%)\n- **SIGSPATIAL 2025**: 1/1 (100%)\n\n### Papers without PDFs (15 papers)\nPrimarily ICDE 2025 papers (7) and some NeurIPS workshop/ICML papers without GitHub repos.\n\n---\n\n## GitHub Repository Status\n\n✅ **21 Papers with GitHub Repositories** (58.3%)\n\n### Top Research Groups (by # of papers with code)\n1. **Decision Intelligence Lab (USTC)** - 3 papers (SynEVO, K²VAE, SRSNet)\n2. **TUM (Technical University of Munich)** - 3 papers (WardropNet, TSFlow, Privacy Amplification)\n3. **South China University of Technology** - 1 paper (TQNet)\n4. **Cambridge Machine Learning Group** - 1 paper (Gridded TNP)\n5. **GeoAI Center** - 1 paper (FUSE-Traffic)\n\n---\n\n## Catalog Information\n\n**Catalog File**: `/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/codex/data/articles/catalog.json`\n\nAll paper metadata has been synchronized to the catalog with the following schema:\n```json\n{\n  "title": "Paper title",\n  "conference": "Conference name",\n  "year": 2025,\n  "track": "Conference/Poster/Spotlight/Workshop/Research",\n  "pdf_link": "URL to PDF",\n  "pdf_path": "Local path to downloaded PDF (or null)",\n  "datasets": ["List of datasets used"],\n  "metrics": ["List of evaluation metrics"],\n  "repo_url": "GitHub repository URL (or null)",\n  "keywords": ["Prioritized keywords including spatial-temporal, traffic-speed-forecast"]\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Search Methodology\n\n### Web Search Strategy\n1. **Conference-specific searches**: Targeted each conference with traffic/spatial-temporal keywords\n2. **Paper-level searches**: Follow-up searches for specific papers to extract metadata\n3. **Workshop searches**: Included workshop papers (NeurIPS Time Series Foundation Models)\n4. **Cross-referencing**: Used OpenReview, arXiv, conference websites, GitHub repositories\n\n### Coverage Verification\n- ✅ ICLR 2025: Searched OpenReview, conference website, paper lists\n- ✅ ICML 2025: Searched conference proceedings, GitHub aggregators, Paper Copilot\n- ✅ NeurIPS 2025: Searched main conference + workshops, Paper Digest\n- ✅ KDD 2025: Searched ACM DL, OpenReview, conference website\n- ✅ ICDE 2025: Searched IEEE Xplore, conference proceedings\n- ✅ SIGSPATIAL 2025: Searched ACM DL, arXiv\n\n### Completeness Assessment\nThis sweep represents a **comprehensive** coverage of 2025 papers targeting traffic state forecasting across the five major conferences. Multiple search iterations were performed until no new candidates appeared.\n\n---\n\n## Notes & Observations\n\n### Conference Trends\n- **ICML** leads in volume (13 papers) and innovation (spotlights on foundation models)\n- **ICLR** strong on graph neural networks and continual learning\n- **NeurIPS** emerging focus on foundation models (workshop + spotlight)\n- **KDD** emphasis on large-scale efficiency and real-world deployment\n- **ICDE** focus on federated learning and privacy-preserving methods\n\n### Dataset Accessibility\n- **PEMS family** remains the gold standard for benchmarking (13 papers)\n- Growing trend toward **larger-scale datasets** (PatchSTG: 4 large-scale datasets)\n- Emergence of **custom datasets** for specific scenarios (TUMTraf VideoQA, PEMS-Stream)\n\n### Code Availability\n- **58.3% open-source rate** - excellent for reproducibility\n- Most spotlight/high-impact papers released code\n- ICDE papers lag in code release (only 12.5%)\n\n### Publication Timing\n- Most papers available on arXiv/OpenReview before conference dates\n- Workshop papers (NeurIPS) may have limited availability\n- Some ICDE papers only on IEEE Xplore (paywall)\n\n---\n\n**End of Comprehensive Literature Sweep**\nGenerated: 2025-11-26\nTotal Papers: 36\nPapers with Code: 21\nPDFs Downloaded: 21\n'}
