 observations effectively\n2. Scales to large spatial grids\n3. Translation-equivariant version performs best\n4. Grid size impacts performance (sweet spot: 32-64)\n\n### Traffic Dataset Adaptation\n\n**Our Implementation**: Adapted for traffic speed prediction\n\nSince the original paper focused on weather data, we\'re applying the architecture to a new domain (traffic). Here\'s the expected performance comparison:\n\n#### Expected Metrics on Traffic Datasets\n\n**Hypothesis**: GriddedTNP should perform competitively with graph-based models because:\n- ✓ Attention mechanism can learn spatial relationships\n- ✓ No adjacency matrix required (flexible)\n- ✓ Handles irregular sensor distributions\n- ✓ Transformer processes temporal dependencies\n\n**Predicted Performance** (vs. Baselines):\n\n| Dataset | Metric | DCRNN | STGCN | MTGNN | GriddedTNP (Expected) |\n|---------|--------|-------|-------|-------|----------------------|\n| **METR-LA** | MAE | 2.77 | 2.88 | 2.69 | 2.8 - 3.5 |\n| | RMSE | 5.38 | 5.74 | 5.18 | 5.5 - 6.5 |\n| | MAPE | 7.3% | 7.6% | 6.9% | 7.0 - 8.5% |\n| **PEMS04** | MAE | 21.3 | 22.7 | 19.3 | 19 - 22 |\n| | RMSE | 33.1 | 35.6 | 30.7 | 31 - 35 |\n| | MAPE | 14.0% | 14.5% | 12.9% | 13 - 15% |\n| **PEMS-BAY** | MAE | 1.38 | 1.45 | 1.30 | 1.3 - 1.6 |\n| | RMSE | 2.95 | 3.16 | 2.70 | 2.7 - 3.2 |\n| | MAPE | 2.9% | 3.2% | 2.7% | 2.8 - 3.5% |\n\n**Rationale for Estimates**:\n- GriddedTNP doesn\'t use graph structure explicitly → May be slightly behind MTGNN\n- Attention mechanism is flexible → Should match or beat STGCN\n- Grid encoding adds capacity → Competitive with DCRNN\n\n#### Actual Test Results (Synthetic Data)\n\n**Important**: Current metrics are from **random synthetic data** (not real traffic):\n\n| Metric | Synthetic Test | Real Traffic (Expected) |\n|--------|---------------|------------------------|\n| MAE | 0.831 | 2.8 - 3.5 (METR-LA) |\n| RMSE | 1.042 | 5.5 - 6.5 (METR-LA) |\n| MAPE | 293% | 7.0 - 8.5% (METR-LA) |\n\n**Why the difference?**\n- Synthetic data: Random inputs with no correlation → High MAPE\n- Real traffic: Temporal patterns, spatial correlations → Realistic metrics\n\n### Comparison with Paper: Key Differences\n\n| Aspect | Original Paper | Our Implementation |\n|--------|---------------|-------------------|\n| **Domain** | Weather forecasting | Traffic speed prediction |\n| **Data Type** | Gridded (ERA5) + Stations | Sensor network (irregular) |\n| **Input Modality** | Multi-modal (station + grid) | Single-modal (sensors only) |\n| **Metrics** | Log-likelihood, MSE | MAE, RMSE, MAPE (traffic standard) |\n| **Grid Type** | Hierarchical (SWIN) | Fixed (standard) |\n| **Spatial Encoding** | Translation-equivariant | Learnable embeddings |\n\n### Delta Analysis & Corrective Steps\n\n#### Expected Deltas from Paper\n\n**Scenario 1: Performance is Lower than Expected**\n\n**Possible Reasons**:\n1. ❌ **Missing adjacency information**\n   - Fix: Add optional graph structure via spatial features\n   - Implementation: `adapter.create_spatial_features(adj_mx)`\n\n2. ❌ **Grid size not optimized**\n   - Fix: Tune `grid_size` parameter (try 16, 32, 64, 128)\n   - Rule of thumb: `grid_size ≈ sqrt(num_nodes)`\n\n3. ❌ **Hyperparameters not tuned**\n   - Fix: Grid search over:\n     - `hidden_dim`: [64, 128, 256]\n     - `num_layers`: [2, 3, 4]\n     - `learning_rate`: [0.0001, 0.0005, 0.001]\n\n4. ❌ **Training data preprocessing**\n   - Fix: Verify scaler type matches baselines\n   - Try: `standard`, `minmax`, `log`\n\n**Scenario 2: Performance Matches or Exceeds Baselines**\n\n**Analysis**:\n- ✅ Architecture successfully migrationred to new domain\n- ✅ Attention mechanism learned spatial relationships\n- ✅ Grid encoding effective for traffic patterns\n\n**Next Steps**:\n- Publish results\n- Ablation studies on grid size\n- Multi-modal extensions (weather, events)\n\n#### Retry Plan for Failures\n\nIf initial training fails or results are poor:\n\n**Step 1: Diagnostic Tests** (30 min)\n```bash\n# Te