+ dynamic reassembly\n      - _select(): Selective patching scorer\n      - _shuffle(): Dynamic reassembly scorer\n    - RevIN: Reversible Instance Normalization\n    - FlattenHead: Prediction head\n```\n\n### 2. Model Configuration\n**File**: `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/config/model/traffic_state_pred/SRSNet.json`\n- ✅ Created from scratch\n- ✅ Follows LibCity config schema\n\n**Configuration Parameters**:\n```json\n{\n  "patch_len": 16,          // Patch length for patching\n  "stride": 8,              // Stride for patching\n  "d_model": 128,           // Model dimension\n  "hidden_size": 256,       // Hidden size for scorers\n  "dropout": 0.1,           // Dropout rate\n  "alpha": 2.0,             // Initial fusion weight\n  "pos": true,              // Use positional encoding\n  "head_mode": "linear",    // Head type (linear or mlp)\n  "affine": true,           // RevIN affine transformation\n  "subtract_last": false,   // RevIN subtract last value\n\n  // LibCity standard configs\n  "scaler": "standard",\n  "max_epoch": 100,\n  "learner": "adam",\n  "learning_rate": 0.001,\n  ...\n}\n```\n\n### 3. Model Registry\n**File**: `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/__init__.py`\n- ✅ Added import: `from libcity.model.traffic_speed_prediction.SRSNet import SRSNet`\n- ✅ Added to `__all__` list: `"SRSNet"`\n- **Lines Modified**: 35 (import), 72 (export)\n\n---\n\n## Data Ingestion Alignment\n\n### Input Format\n**LibCity Expected**:\n```python\nbatch[\'X\']: [batch_size, input_window, num_nodes, feature_dim]\nbatch[\'y\']: [batch_size, output_window, num_nodes, output_dim]\n```\n\n**SRSNet Adaptation**:\n```python\n# Extract traffic values (first feature)\nx_enc = x[..., 0]  # [batch_size, input_window, num_nodes]\n\n# Reshape for processing\nx_enc = x_enc.permute(0, 2, 1)  # [batch_size, num_nodes, input_window]\n\n# Process through SRS module\nenc_out, n_vars = self.patch_embedding(x_enc)\n\n# Output format\noutput: [batch_size, output_window, num_nodes, 1]\n```\n\n### Key Adaptations\n1. ✅ **Multivariate to Univariate**: Extracts first feature dimension (traffic speed)\n2. ✅ **Spatial Dimension**: Treats `num_nodes` as multivariate channels (n_vars)\n3. ✅ **Normalization**: Uses RevIN for instance-wise normalization\n4. ✅ **Scaler Integration**: Uses LibCity\'s scaler in `calculate_loss()`\n\n---\n\n## Architecture Mapping\n\n### Original SRSNet → LibCity Adapter\n\n| Original Component | LibCity Location | Notes |\n|-------------------|------------------|-------|\n| `SRSNetModel.__init__()` | `SRSNet.__init__()` | Added data_feature parsing |\n| `config.seq_len` | `config.get(\'input_window\')` | Renamed for LibCity compatibility |\n| `config.pred_len` | `config.get(\'output_window\')` | Renamed for LibCity compatibility |\n| `config.enc_in` | `self.num_nodes` | Spatial nodes as variables |\n| `forward(x_enc)` | `forward(batch)` | Batch dict extraction |\n| Loss function | `calculate_loss(batch)` | Uses LibCity\'s masked_mae_torch |\n\n### Data Flow\n```\nLibCity Batch Input\n    ↓\nExtract traffic values [B, T_in, N, F] → [B, T_in, N]\n    ↓\nRevIN Normalization [B, T_in, N]\n    ↓\nPermute to [B, N, T_in] (treat nodes as variables)\n    ↓\nSRS Module (Selective Representation Space)\n  - Original View: Standard patching\n  - Reconstruction View: Selective patching + reassembly\n  - Adaptive Fusion: Weight combination\n    ↓\nPatch Embeddings [B*N, P, D]\n    ↓\nReshape to [B, N, D, P]\n    ↓\nFlattenHead Prediction [B, N, T_out]\n    ↓\nPermute to [B, T_out, N]\n    ↓\nRevIN De-normalization\n    ↓\nAdd feature dim [B, T_out, N, 1]\n    ↓\nLibCity Output Format\n```\n\n---\n\n## Training & Evaluation\n\n### Command Line Usage\n```bash\n# From Bigscity-LibCity directory\npython run_model.py --task traffic_state_pred --model SRSNet --dataset METR_LA\n\n# With custom config\npython run_model.py --task traffic_state_pred --model SRSNet --dataset PEMS04 \\\n    --patch_len 16 --stride 8 --d_model 128 --learning_rate 0.001\n```\n\n### Expected Datasets\n- METR_LA\n- PEMS-BAY\n- PEMS03, PEMS04, PEMS07, PEMS08\n- Any LibCity-compatible traffic speed dataset\n\n### Metrics Supported\n- MAE (Mean Absolute Error)\n- MAPE (Mean Absolute Percentage Error)\n- MSE (Mean Squared Error)\n- RMSE (Root Mean Squared Error)\n- masked_* variants\n\n---\n\n## Dependencies\n\n### Required Packages\n```txt\ntorch >= 1.11.0\neinops  # For rearrange operations in SRS module\nnumpy\n```\n\n### Already in LibCity\n```python\nfrom libcity.model.abstract_traffic_state_model import AbstractTrafficStateModel\nfrom libcity.model import loss\nfrom logging import getLogger\n```\n\n---\n\n## Testing Checklist\n\n### Unit Tests\n- [ ] Test SRS module forward pass\n- [ ] Test RevIN normalization/denormalization\n- [ ] Test FlattenHead output shape\n- [ ] Test end-to-end forward pass with dummy data\n\n### Integration Tests\n- [ ] Load model via LibCity config system\n- [ ] Train for 1 epoch on METR_LA\n- [ ] Verify loss calculation\n- [ ] Test prediction mode\n- [ ] Verify metrics computation\n\n### Performance Tests\n- [ ] Compare with baseline RNN model\n- [ ] Verify memory usage is reasonable\n- [ ] Check training speed\n\n---\n\n## Known Issues & Limitations\n\n### Current Limitations\n1. **Feature Dimension**: Currently uses only first feature (traffic speed)\n   - Original SRSNet is designed for multivariate time series\n   - LibCity traffic data has spatial structure (nodes) + temporal features\n   - Adaptation: Treats nodes as variables, extracts speed feature\n\n2. **External Features**: Time of day / day of week not directly used\n   - RevIN handles temporal patterns implicitly\n   - Could be enhanced to incorporate temporal embeddings\n\n3. **Spatial Structure**: Does not leverage graph adjacency\n   - Original SRSNet is not graph-based\n   - Treats each node independently (channel-independent)\n\n### Future Enhancements\n- [ ] Add support for multi-feature input\n- [ ] Integrate temporal embeddings (time_of_day, day_of_week)\n- [ ] Explore spatial extensions (graph-based patches)\n- [ ] Add dataset-specific configurations\n- [ ] Benchmark against other LibCity models\n\n---\n\n## Reference Documentation\n\n### Original Paper\n- **Title**: Enhancing Time Series Forecasting through Selective Representation Spaces: A Patch Perspective\n- **Authors**: Wu, Xingjian and Qiu, Xiangfei and Cheng, Hanyin and Li, Zhengyu and Hu, Jilin and Guo, Chenjuan and Yang, Bin\n- **Venue**: NeurIPS 2025 (Spotlight)\n- **PDF**: https://arxiv.org/pdf/2510.14510\n- **Code**: https://github.com/decisionintelligence/SRSNet\n\n### LibCity Documentation\n- **Add Model Guide**: LibCity documentation (truncated in task description)\n- **Model Interface**: `libcity/model/abstract_traffic_state_model.py`\n- **Config System**: `libcity/config/config_parser.py`\n\n---\n\n## File Structure Summary\n\n```\ncodex/\n├── repos/\n│   └── SRSNet/                                    # ✅ Cloned with full git history\n│       ├── ts_benchmark/baselines/srsnet/\n│       │   ├── models/srsnet_model.py            # Original model\n│       │   └── layers/\n│       │       ├── SRS.py                         # Selective Representation Space\n│       │       └── RevIN.py                       # Reversible Instance Norm\n│       └── [full upstream repo]\n│\n├── Bigscity-LibCity/\n│   ├── libcity/\n│   │   ├── model/\n│   │   │   └── traffic_speed_prediction/\n│   │   │       ├── SRSNet.py                     # ✅ NEW: Adapted model\n│   │   │       └── __init__.py                   # ✅ MODIFIED: Registry\n│   │   └── config/\n│   │       └── model/\n│   │           └── traffic_state_pred/\n│   │               └── SRSNet.json               # ✅ NEW: Config file\n│   └── run_model.py                              # Can now use --model SRSNet\n│\n└── data/\n    └── articles/\n        ├── catalog.json                          # Contains SRSNet metadata\n        └── NeurIPS2025_SRSNet.pdf               # Paper PDF\n\n```\n\n---\n\n## Automation Helpers\n\n### Config Generator Template\nLocation: This document serves as the template\n\n**Generate config for new dataset**:\n```python\nimport json\n\nbase_config = {\n    "patch_len": 16,\n    "stride": 8,\n    "d_model": 128,\n    "hidden_size": 256,\n    "dropout": 0.1,\n    "alpha": 2.0,\n    "pos": True,\n    "head_mode": "linear",\n    "affine": True,\n    "subtract_last": False,\n    "scaler": "standard",\n    "learning_rate": 0.001,\n}\n\n# Customize per dataset\ndataset_config = base_config.copy()\ndataset_config.update({\n    "input_window": 12,\n    "output_window": 12,\n    "max_epoch": 100,\n})\n\nwith open("SRSNet_custom.json", "w") as f:\n    json.dump(dataset_config, f, indent=2)\n```\n\n### Quick Test Script\n```python\n# test_srsnet.py\nimport torch\nfrom libcity.config.config_parser import ConfigParser\nfrom libcity.model.traffic_speed_prediction.SRSNet import SRSNet\n\n# Create dummy config and data_feature\nconfig = {\n    \'input_window\': 96,\n    \'output_window\': 96,\n    \'patch_len\': 16,\n    \'stride\': 8,\n    \'d_model\': 128,\n    \'device\': torch.device(\'cpu\')\n}\n\ndata_feature = {\n    \'scaler\': None,\n    \'num_nodes\': 207,\n    \'feature_dim\': 1,\n    \'output_dim\': 1\n}\n\n# Initialize model\nmodel = SRSNet(config, data_feature)\n\n# Test forward pass\nbatch = {\n    \'X\': torch.randn(32, 96, 207, 1),\n    \'y\': torch.randn(32, 96, 207, 1)\n}\n\noutput = model.forward(batch)\nprint(f"Output shape: {output.shape}")  # Should be [32, 96, 207, 1]\n```\n\n---\n\n## Completion Status\n\n### Core Migration Tasks\n- ✅ Repository cloned with full git history\n- ✅ Model adapted to LibCity interface\n- ✅ Configuration file created\n- ✅ Model registered in __init__.py\n- ✅ Data ingestion aligned\n- ✅ Documentation completed\n\n### Verification Steps\n- ✅ Model file created and validated\n- ✅ Config file created with proper JSON syntax\n- ✅ Registry updated correctly\n- ✅ No syntax errors in Py