: Combines spatial and temporal features\n    - `STELLA`: LibCity interface wrapper\n\n- [x] **Updated model registry**\n  - File: `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/__init__.py`\n  - Added import: `from libcity.model.traffic_speed_prediction.STELLA import STELLA`\n  - Added to `__all__` list\n\n### 4. Data Ingestion Alignment\n- [x] **Input/Output Signature**\n  - Input: `batch[\'X\']` with shape `[B, L, N, C]`\n  - Optional: `batch[\'X_ext\']` for temporal features\n  - Output: `[B, F, N, C]` predictions\n  - Handles both node position-based and learnable embeddings\n\n- [x] **Dataset Compatibility**\n  - Compatible with LibCity\'s standard traffic datasets (METR-LA, PEMS-BAY, etc.)\n  - Supports datasets with or without explicit node positions\n  - Uses standard scaler for normalization/denormalization\n  - Temporal features: Extracts from external features or uses dummy values\n\n### 5. Configuration Files\n- [x] **Model Configuration Created**\n  - Path: `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/config/model/traffic_state_pred/STELLA.json`\n  - Parameters:\n    ```json\n    {\n      "d_model": 32,\n      "num_layer": 2,\n      "if_rel": false,\n      "res_conn": true,\n      "dropout": 0.2,\n      "learning_rate": 0.0005,\n      "max_epoch": 100\n    }\n    ```\n\n### 6. Automation Helpers\n- [x] **Integration Helper Script**\n  - Path: `automation/stella_integration_helper.py`\n  - Functions:\n    - `generate_stella_config()`: Create dataset-specific configs\n    - `generate_run_command()`: Generate LibCity run commands\n    - `generate_batch_script()`: Create batch experiment scripts\n    - `create_experiment_config()`: Hyperparameter sweep utilities\n    - `save_config()`: Save configurations to JSON\n\n- [x] **Test Suite Created**\n  - Path: `tests/test_stella_integration.py`\n  - Tests:\n    - `test_stella_core()`: Core model functionality\n    - `test_stella_libcity()`: LibCity interface compliance\n    - `test_positional_embeddings()`: Embedding components\n    - `test_with_node_positions()`: Position-aware mode\n    - `run_all_tests()`: Complete test harness\n\n---\n\n## 📁 File Tree & Touched Files\n\n```\ncodex/\n├── repos/\n│   └── STELLA/                          [CLONED - Upstream repo]\n│       ├── stella/\n│       │   ├── stella_arch.py          (Reference: Core architecture)\n│       │   ├── mlp.py                  (Reference: MLP layer)\n│       │   └── pos_embedding.py        (Reference: Positional encodings)\n│       ├── baselines/STELLA/\n│       │   └── STELLA_*.py             (Reference: Config examples)\n│       ├── requirements.txt             (Reference: Dependencies)\n│       └── README.md                    (Reference: Documentation)\n│\n├── Bigscity-LibCity/\n│   ├── libcity/\n│   │   ├── model/\n│   │   │   └── traffic_speed_prediction/\n│   │   │       ├── STELLA.py           [CREATED - Main adapter]\n│   │   │       └── __init__.py         [MODIFIED - Added STELLA import]\n│   │   └── config/\n│   │       └── model/\n│   │           └── traffic_state_pred/\n│   │               └── STELLA.json     [CREATED - Model config]\n│   └── run_model.py                     [REFERENCE - Entry point]\n│\n├── automation/\n│   └── stella_integration_helper.py     [CREATED - Helper utilities]\n│\n├── tests/\n│   └── test_stella_integration.py       [CREATED - Test suite]\n│\n└── documentation/\n    └── STELLA_INTEGRATION_CHECKLIST.md  [THIS FILE]\n```\n\n---\n\n## 🔄 Pending TODOs (If Any)\n\n### Testing & Validation\n- [ ] **Run unit tests**\n  ```bash\n  cd /home/wangwenrui/private/shk/codex\n  python tests/test_stella_integration.py\n  ```\n\n- [ ] **Test with actual LibCity dataset**\n  ```bash\n  cd Bigscity-LibCity\n  python run_model.py --task traffic_state_pred --model STELLA --dataset METR_LA\n  ```\n\n### Optional Enhancements\n- [ ] **Add support for additional datasets**\n  - Create dataset-specific configs for PEMS04, PEMS08, etc.\n  - Path: `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/config/dataset/`\n\n- [ ] **Integrate pre-trained weights** (if available)\n  - Check STELLA repo for checkpoints\n  - Add weight loading utilities\n\n- [ ] **Performance benchmarking**\n  - Compare with original STELLA results\n  - Document metrics (MAE, RMSE, MAPE)\n\n- [ ] **Add visualization tools**\n  - Prediction vs ground truth plots\n  - Attention/embedding visualizations\n\n---\n\n## 🚀 Quick Start Guide\n\n### 1. Install Dependencies\n```bash\ncd Bigscity-LibCity\npip install -r requirements.txt\n```\n\n### 2. Run Tests\n```bash\ncd /home/wangwenrui/private/shk/codex\npython tests/test_stella_integration.py\n```\n\n### 3. Train on METR-LA\n```bash\ncd Bigscity-LibCity\npython run_model.py --task traffic_state_pred \\\n                    --model STELLA \\\n                    --dataset METR_LA \\\n                    --input_window 12 \\\n                    --output_window 12\n```\n\n### 4. Custom Configuration\n```python\nfrom automation.stella_integration_helper import generate_stella_config, save_config\n\nconfig = generate_stella_config(\n    dataset_name="PEMS_BAY",\n    d_model=64,\n    num_layer=3,\n    learning_rate=0.001\n)\nsave_config(config, "custom_stella_config.json")\n```\n\n### 5. Batch Experiments\n```python\nfrom automation.stella_integration_helper import generate_batch_script\n\ndatasets = ["METR_LA", "PEMS_BAY", "PEMSD4", "PEMSD8"]\nscript_path = generate_batch_script(datasets, "run_stella_all.sh")\n# Then run: bash run_stella_all.sh\n```\n\n---\n\n## 🔍 Model Configuration Details\n\n### Key Parameters\n\n| Parameter | Default | Description |\n|-----------|---------|-------------|\n| `d_model` | 32 | Hidden dimension size |\n| `num_layer` | 2 | Number of MLP layers |\n| `if_rel` | False | Use learnable embeddings vs. positions |\n| `res_conn` | True | Enable residual connections |\n| `dropout` | 0.2 | Dropout rate |\n| `input_window` | 12 | Input sequence length |\n| `output_window` | 12 | Prediction horizon |\n| `learning_rate` | 0.0005 | Initial learning rate |\n| `max_epoch` | 100 | Maximum training epochs |\n\n### Data Requirements\n\n**Input Format**: `[Batch, Time, Nodes, Features]`\n- `Batch`: Batch size (configurable)\n- `Time`: Historical time steps (default: 12)\n- `Nodes`: Number of sensors/stations\n- `Features`: Traffic measurements (speed, flow, etc.)\n\n**Optional**:\n- Node positions: `[Nodes, 3]` - (latitude, longitude, altitude)\n- Temporal features: Month, day-of-month, hour-of-day (normalized to [0,1])\n\n---\n\n## 📊 Expected Performance\n\nBased on original STELLA paper (atmospheric forecasting):\n- **Lightweight**: Significantly fewer parameters than GNN/Transformer models\n- **Fast Training**: ~2 minutes per dataset on RTX 3090\n- **Competitive Accuracy**: Matches or exceeds complex models on certain datasets\n\n**Adaptation Note**: Performance on traffic datasets may differ from atmospheric data. Benchmarking recommended.\n\n---\n\n## 🐛 Troubleshooting\n\n### Issue: Import Error\n```\nModuleNotFoundError: No module named \'libcity\'\n```\n**Solution**: Ensure you\'re in the `Bigscity-LibCity` directory or add to PYTHONPATH:\n```bash\nexport PYTHONPATH=$PYTHONPATH:/path/to/Bigscity-LibCity\n```\n\n### Issue: Missing Temporal Features\n**Solution**: STELLA creates dummy temporal features if not provided. For better results, ensure dataset includes time-of-day features.\n\n### Issue: Node Positions Not Available\n**Solution**: Set `if_rel=True` in config to use learnable node embeddings instead of geographical positions.\n\n---\n\n## 📚 References\n\n1. **STELLA Paper**: [arXiv:2408.09695](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2408.09695)\n2. **STELLA Repository**: https://github.com/GestaltCogTeam/STELLA\n3. **LibCity Documentation**: [Bigscity-LibCity](https://github.com/LibCity/Bigscity-LibCity)\n4. **LibCity Model Development Guide**: See `libcity_document.md`\n\n---\n\n## 📝 Summary Statistics\n\n- **Files Created**: 4\n  - `STELLA.py` (322 lines)\n  - `STELLA.json` (22 lines)\n  - `stella_integration_helper.py