tion mechanism (faster than Transformers)\n- No graph convolution (faster than GNNs)\n- Flexible spatial encoding (positions or learnable)\n\n### 2.2 Dependencies Mapped\n- PyTorch >= 1.10.0 ✓\n- NumPy >= 1.22.0 ✓\n- scikit-learn >= 1.1.0 ✓\n- easy-torch (optional, not required for LibCity) ✓\n\n**Compatibility**: All dependencies already in LibCity ✅\n\n---\n\n## 3. LIBCITY MODEL IMPLEMENTATION\n\n### 3.1 Model Adapter Created\n\n**File**: `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/STELLA.py`\n**Lines**: 322\n**Status**: ✅ COMPLETE\n\n**Classes Implemented**:\n1. `MLP`: Multi-layer perceptron with residual connections\n2. `SpatialEmbedding`: Handles geographical or learnable embeddings\n3. `TemporalEmbedding`: Hour/day/month cyclic encodings\n4. `PositionEmbedding`: Combines spatial and temporal features\n5. `STELLACore`: Core model architecture\n6. `STELLA`: LibCity interface wrapper (extends AbstractTrafficStateModel)\n\n**Methods Implemented**:\n- `__init__(config, data_feature)`: Initialization ✓\n- `forward(batch)`: Forward pass ✓\n- `predict(batch)`: Multi-step prediction ✓\n- `calculate_loss(batch)`: Loss computation with denormalization ✓\n\n### 3.2 Model Registration\n\n**File Modified**: `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/__init__.py`\n\n```python\n# Added import\nfrom libcity.model.traffic_speed_prediction.STELLA import STELLA\n\n# Added to __all__\n__all__ = [\n    # ... existing models ...\n    "STELLA",\n]\n```\n\n**Status**: ✅ REGISTERED\n\n---\n\n## 4. DATA INGESTION ALIGNMENT\n\n### 4.1 Input/Output Format\n\n**Input Batch Structure**:\n```python\nbatch = {\n    \'X\': torch.Tensor,      # [B, L, N, C] - Historical data\n    \'y\': torch.Tensor,      # [B, F, N, C] - Ground truth\n    \'X_ext\': torch.Tensor   # [B, L, N, T] - Optional temporal features\n}\n```\n\n**Output**:\n```python\npredictions: torch.Tensor  # [B, F, N, C] - Predictions\n```\n\n**Compatibility**:\n- ✅ Standard LibCity format\n- ✅ Works with