 2: Create Main AutoSTF Model Adapter\n\n#### File 2.1: Create AutoSTF.py\n- **Location**: `./Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/AutoSTF.py`\n- **Purpose**: Adapt AutoSTF to LibCity\'s AbstractTrafficStateModel interface\n- **Key Adaptations**:\n\n1. **Inherit from AbstractTrafficStateModel**\n2. **Modify __init__ signature**:\n   ```python\n   def __init__(self, config, data_feature):\n       super().__init__(config, data_feature)\n       # Extract from data_feature\n       self._scaler = data_feature.get(\'scaler\')\n       self.num_nodes = data_feature.get(\'num_nodes\', 1)\n       self.feature_dim = data_feature.get(\'feature_dim\', 1)\n       self.output_dim = data_feature.get(\'output_dim\', 1)\n       adj_mx = data_feature.get(\'adj_mx\')  # LibCity provides this\n\n       # Extract from config\n       self.in_length = config.get(\'input_window\', 12)\n       self.out_length = config.get(\'output_window\', 12)\n       self.device = config.get(\'device\', torch.device(\'cpu\'))\n       self.hidden_channels = config.get(\'hidden_channels\', 32)\n       self.end_channels = config.get(\'end_channels\', 512)\n       # ... (continue with other config params)\n   ```\n\n3. **Transform batch input format**:\n   - LibCity batch: `{\'X\': [B, T_in, N, F], \'y\': [B, T_out, N, F]}`\n   - AutoSTF expects: `[B, F, N, T_in]`\n   - Add transpose in forward: `inputs = batch[\'X\'].transpose(1, 3).transpose(2, 3)`\n\n4. **Implement required methods**:\n   ```python\n   def predict(self, batch):\n       return self.forward(batch)\n\n   def calculate_loss(self, batch):\n       y_true = batch[\'y\']\n       y_predicted = self.predict(batch)\n       y_true = self._scaler.inverse_transform(y_true[..., :self.output_dim])\n       y_predicted = self._scaler.inverse_transform(y_predicted[..., :self.output_dim])\n       return loss.masked_mae_torch(y_predicted, y_true)\n\n   def forward(self, batch):\n       # Transform input from LibCity format to AutoSTF format\n       inputs = batch[\'X\']  # [B, T_in, N, F]\n       inputs = inputs.permute(0, 3, 2, 1)  # [B, F, N, T_in]\n\n       # Call original AutoSTF forward\n       output = self._autostf_forward(inputs, mode=Mode.ONE_PATH_FIXED)\n\n       # Transform output from [B, 1, N, T_out] to [B, T_out, N, 1]\n       output = output.permute(0, 3, 2, 1)\n       return output\n   ```\n\n5. **Handle adjacency matrix**:\n   ```python\n   # LibCity provides adj_mx via data_feature\n   adj_mx = data_feature.get(\'adj_mx\')\n   if adj_mx is not None:\n       # Create mask_support_adj from adj_mx\n       # Create adj_mx_gwn, adj_mx_dcrnn, adj_mx_01 variants\n   ```\n\n**Critical Transformations**:\n- Input: LibCity `[B, T, N, F]` → AutoSTF `[B, F, N, T]`\n- Output: AutoSTF `[B, 1, N, T]` → LibCity `[B, T, N, 1]`\n\n---\n\n### Task 3: Create Configuration File\n\n#### File 3.1: AutoSTF.json\n- **Location**: `./Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/config/model/traffic_state_pred/AutoSTF.json`\n- **Content**:\n```json\n{\n  "hidden_channels": 32,\n  "end_channels": 512,\n  "num_mlp_layers": 2,\n  "scale_num": 3,\n\n  "IsUseLinear": true,\n  "num_linear_layers": 3,\n\n  "layer_names": ["TemporalSearch", "SpatialSearch"],\n\n  "num_temporal_search_node": 4,\n  "temporal_operations": ["DCC_2", "Informer"],\n\n  "num_spatial_search_node": 4,\n  "spatial_operations": ["GNN_fixed", "GNN_adap", "GNN_att"],\n  "num_att_layers": 1,\n  "num_hop": 1,\n\n  "scaler": "standard",\n  "load_external": true,\n  "normal_external": false,\n  "ext_scaler": "none",\n  "add_time_in_day": true,\n  "add_day_in_week": true,\n\n  "max_epoch": 200,\n  "learner": "adam",\n  "learning_rate": 0.001,\n  "lr_decay": true,\n  "lr_scheduler": "multisteplr",\n  "lr_decay_ratio": 0.01,\n  "steps": [50, 60, 70, 80],\n  "clip_grad_norm": true,\n  "max_grad_norm": 5,\n  "use_early_stop": true,\n  "patience": 30,\n\n  "weight_decay": 0.0001,\n  "arch_decay": 0.0003\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### Task 4: Register Model in LibCity\n\n#### File 4.1: Update __init__.py\n- **Location**: `./Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/__init__.py`\n- **Edit Line ~1-5**: Add import\n  ```python\n  from libcity.model.traffic_speed_prediction.AutoSTF import AutoSTF\n  ```\n\n- **Edit Line ~40-80**: Add to __all__ list\n  ```python\n  __all__ = [\n      "DCRNN",\n      "STGCN",\n      # ... existing models ...\n      "AutoSTF",  # ADD THIS LINE\n  ]\n  ```\n\n---\n\n### Task 5: Create Helper Scripts\n\n#### File 5.1: Adjacency Matrix Utility\n- **Location**: `./scripts/autostf_adj_utils.py`\n- **Purpose**: Helper to create AutoSTF-specific adjacency matrices from LibCity adj_mx\n- **Content**:\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport scipy.sparse as sp\nimport torch\n\ndef create_autostf_adjacency_matrices(adj_mx, device):\n    """\n    Create AutoSTF-specific adjacency matrices from LibCity adj_mx.\n\n    Args:\n        adj_mx: numpy array [N, N]\n        device: torch device\n\n    Returns:\n        dict with keys: mask_support_adj, adj_mx_dcrnn, adj_mx_gwn, adj_mx_01\n    """\n    def asym_adj(adj):\n        adj = sp.coo_matrix(adj)\n        rowsum = np.array(adj.sum(1)).flatten()\n        d_inv = np.power(rowsum, -1).flatten()\n        d_inv[np.isinf(d_inv)] = 0.\n        d_mat = sp.diags(d_inv)\n        return d_mat.dot(adj).astype(np.float32).todense()\n\n    # Create adjacency variants\n    adj_mx_01 = (adj_mx > 0).astype(np.float32)\n    adj_mx_dcrnn = asym_adj(adj_mx)\n\n    # GWN-style adjacency\n    adj_gwn_forward = asym_adj(adj_mx)\n    adj_gwn_backward = asym_adj(adj_mx.T)\n    adj_mx_gwn = [adj_gwn_forward, adj_gwn_backward]\n\n    # Convert to tensors\n    mask_support_adj = [\n        torch.tensor(adj_gwn_forward).to(device),\n        torch.tensor(adj_gwn_backward).to(device)\n    ]\n\n    adj_mx_list = [\n        torch.tensor(adj_mx_dcrnn).to(device),\n        [torch.tensor(m).to(device) for m in adj_mx_gwn],\n        torch.tensor(adj_mx_01).to(device)\n    ]\n\n    return {\n        \'mask_support_adj\': mask_support_adj,\n        \'adj_mx\': adj_mx_list,\n        \'adj_mx_dcrnn\': adj_mx_dcrnn,\n        \'adj_mx_gwn\': adj_mx_gwn,\n        \'adj_mx_01\': adj_mx_01\n    }\n```\n\n---\n\n## III. Data Alignment Tasks\n\n### Task 6: Verify Dataset Compatibility\n\n#### Checklist 6.1: Input Shape Verification\n- [ ] Verify LibCity batch[\'X\'] shape: `[batch_size, input_window, num_nodes, feature_dim]`\n- [ ] Verify LibCity batch[\'y\'] shape: `[batch_size, output_window, num_nodes, output_dim]`\n- [ ] Add assertions in AutoSTF.__init__ to validate shapes\n- [ ] Add shape logging in forward pass for debugging\n\n#### Checklist 6.2: Feature Dimension Alignment\nAutoSTF supports 1-3 input channels:\n- **1 channel**: Traffic speed only\n- **2 channels**: Traffic speed + time_in_day\n- **3 channels**: Traffic speed + time_in_day + day_in_week\n\nLibCity datasets to verify:\n- [ ] METR-LA: 207 nodes\n- [ ] PEMS-BAY: 325 nodes\n- [ ] PEMS03: 358 nodes\n- [ ] PEMS04: 307 nodes\n- [ ] PEMS07: 883 nodes\n- [ ] PEMS08: 170 nodes\n\n**Config Mapping**:\n```json\n{\n  "add_time_in_day": true,   # → in_channels = 2 or 3\n  "add_day_in_week": true,   # → in_channels = 3\n  "add_time_in_day": false,  # → in_channels = 1\n  "add_day_in_week": false\n}\n```\n\n#### Checklist 6.3: Scaler Compatibility\n- [ ] Verify LibCity scaler provides `inverse_transform()` method\n- [ ] Test with StandardScaler (default)\n- [ ] Handle missing values (scaler should support null_val=0)\n\n---\n\n## IV. Testing Requirements\n\n### Task 7: Create Pytest Test Module\n\n#### File 7.1: Basic Integration Test\n- **Location**: `./tests/test_autostf_integration.py`\n- **Purpose**: Verify model loads and runs basic forward pass\n- **Test Cases**:\n\n```python\nimport pytest\nimport torch\nimport numpy as np\nfrom libcity.model.traffic_speed_prediction.AutoSTF import AutoSTF\n\nclass TestAutoSTFIntegration:\n    """Basic integration tests for AutoSTF model."""\n\n    @pytest.fixture\n    def config(s