   num_nodes = 20\n    adj_mx = torch.rand(num_nodes, num_nodes).numpy()\n    adj_mx = (adj_mx > 0.8).astype(float)\n\n    class MockScaler:\n        def inverse_transform(self, x):\n            return x * 10.0\n        def transform(self, x):\n            return x / 10.0\n\n    data_feature = {\n        \'num_nodes\': num_nodes,\n        \'feature_dim\': 2,\n        \'output_dim\': 1,\n        \'adj_mx\': adj_mx,\n        \'scaler\': MockScaler()\n    }\n\n    model = AutoSTF(config, data_feature)\n    optimizer = torch.optim.Adam(model.parameters(), lr=0.001)\n\n    # Training loop\n    for step in range(5):\n        batch = {\n            \'X\': torch.randn(4, 12, num_nodes, 2),\n            \'y\': torch.randn(4, 12, num_nodes, 1)\n        }\n\n        optimizer.zero_grad()\n        loss = model.calculate_loss(batch)\n        loss.backward()\n        optimizer.step()\n\n        assert not torch.isnan(loss), f"NaN loss at step {step}"\n        print(f"Step {step}: Loss = {loss.item():.4f}")\n```\n\n---\n\n## V. Documentation Requirements\n\n### Task 8: Migration Summary Document\n\n#### File 8.1: AutoSTF_Migration_Summary.md\n- **Location**: `./documentation/AutoSTF_Migration_Summary.md`\n- **Required Sections**:\n\n1. **Overview**\n   - Model name, paper citation, repository link\n   - Key innovation: Decoupled NAS for ST forecasting\n   - Performance: 13.48x speedup, state-of-the-art accuracy\n\n2. **Architecture Summary**\n   - Input embedding (MLP + node/temporal embeddings)\n   - Temporal search (multi-scale processing)\n   - Spatial search (multi-granularity GNN)\n   - Output projection\n\n3. **Files Created/Modified**\n   - List all new files with paths\n   - List all modified files with line numbers\n   - Reference directory structure\n\n4. **Data Requirements**\n   - Supported datasets: METR-LA, PEMS-BAY, PEMS03/04/07/08\n   - Input format requirements\n   - Feature dimension options (1-3 channels)\n\n5. **Configuration Parameters**\n   - All hyperparameters with descriptions\n   - Default values\n   - Recommended settings per dataset\n\n6. **Testing Results**\n   - Pytest commands to run\n   - Expected test coverage\n   - Known limitations\n\n7. **Usage Example**\n   ```python\n   # Example LibCity training command\n   python run_model.py --task traffic_state_pred \\\n       --model AutoSTF \\\n       --dataset PEMS04 \\\n       --config_file AutoSTF\n   ```\n\n8. **References**\n   - Original paper: KDD 2025\n   - Original repository: https://github.com/usail-hkust/AutoSTF\n   - Related work: AutoCTS, AutoSTG\n\n---\n\n## VI. Automation Helpers\n\n### Task 9: Config Generator Script\n\n#### File 9.1: generate_autostf_config.py\n- **Location**: `./scripts/generate_autostf_config.py`\n- **Purpose**: Generate dataset-specific AutoSTF configs\n- **Usage**: `python scripts/generate_autostf_config.py --dataset PEMS04 --output libcity/config/`\n\n```python\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport os\n\nDATASET_PARAMS = {\n    \'METR_LA\': {\n        \'num_nodes\': 207,\n        \'in_channels\': 3,\n        \'scale_num\': 3,\n        \'hidden_channels\': 32,\n    },\n    \'PEMS_BAY\': {\n        \'num_nodes\': 325,\n        \'in_channels\': 3,\n        \'scale_num\': 3,\n        \'hidden_channels\': 32,\n    },\n    \'PEMS03\': {\n        \'num_nodes\': 358,\n        \'in_channels\': 3,\n        \'scale_num\': 3,\n        \'hidden_channels\': 32,\n    },\n    \'PEMS04\': {\n        \'num_nodes\': 307,\n        \'in_channels\': 3,\n        \'scale_num\': 3,\n        \'hidden_channels\': 32,\n    },\n    \'PEMS07\': {\n        \'num_nodes\': 883,\n        \'in_channels\': 3,\n        \'scale_num\': 3,\n        \'hidden_channels\': 64,  # Larger for more nodes\n    },\n    \'PEMS08\': {\n        \'num_nodes\': 170,\n        \'in_channels\': 3,\n        \'scale_num\': 3,\n        \'hidden_channels\': 32,\n    },\n}\n\ndef generate_config(dataset):\n    base_config = {\n        "hidden_channels": 32,\n        "end_channels": 512,\n        "num_mlp_layers": 2,\n        "scale_num": 3,\n        "IsUseLinear": True,\n        "num_linear_layers": 3,\n        "layer_names": ["TemporalSearch", "SpatialSearch"],\n        "num_temporal_search_node": 4,\n        "temporal_operations": ["DCC_2", "Informer"],\n        "num_spatial_search_node": 4,\n        "spatial_operations": ["GNN_fixed", "GNN_adap", "GNN_att"],\n        "num_att_layers": 1,\n        "num_hop": 1,\n        "scaler": "standard",\n        "add_time_in_day": True,\n        "add_day_in_week": True,\n        "max_epoch": 200,\n        "learner": "adam",\n        "learning_rate": 0.001,\n        "lr_decay": True,\n        "lr_scheduler": "multisteplr",\n        "lr_decay_ratio": 0.01,\n        "steps": [50, 60, 70, 80],\n        "clip_grad_norm": True,\n        "max_grad_norm": 5,\n        "use_early_stop": True,\n        "patience": 30,\n        "weight_decay": 0.0001,\n        "arch_decay": 0.0003\n    }\n\n    if dataset in DATASET_PARAMS:\n        base_config.update(DATASET_PARAMS[dataset])\n\n    return base_config\n\nif __name__ == "__main__":\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    parser.add_argument(\'--dataset\', required=True, choices=list(DATASET_PARAMS.keys()))\n    parser.add_argument(\'--output\', default=\'./libcity/config/model/traffic_state_pred/\')\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n\n    config = generate_config(args.dataset)\n    output_path = os.path.join(args.output, f\'AutoSTF_{args.dataset}.json\')\n\n    with open(output_path, \'w\') as f:\n        json.dump(config, f, indent=2)\n\n    print(f"Generated config: {output_path}")\n```\n\n---\n\n## VII. Verification Checklist\n\n### Pre-Migration Verification\n- [x] AutoSTF repository cloned to `./repos/AutoSTF/`\n- [x] Repository structure analyzed\n- [x] Key model files identified\n- [x] Dependencies documented\n\n### Code Migration Verification\n- [ ] All supporting module files copied to `autostf_layers/`\n- [ ] Import statements updated (no `src.model` references)\n- [ ] Main AutoSTF.py created with LibCity interface\n- [ ] Batch input/output transformations implemented\n- [ ] Adjacency matrix handling implemented\n- [ ] Configuration file created\n- [ ] Model registered in __init__.py\n\n### Testing Verification\n- [ ] test_autostf_integration.py passes all tests\n- [ ] test_autostf_training.py completes mini training\n- [ ] Model initializes without errors\n- [ ] Forward pass produces correct shapes\n- [ ] Loss calculation works\n- [ ] Gradient backpropagation works\n- [ ] Different feature dimensions (1-3) supported\n\n### Documentation Verification\n- [ ] AutoSTF_Migration_Summary.md created\n- [ ] All file paths documented\n- [ ] Configuration parameters documented\n- [ ] Usage examples provided\n- [ ] References cited\n\n### Integration Verification\n- [ ] LibCity can import AutoSTF model\n- [ ] Config file loads correctly\n- [ ] Model works with LibCity\'s standard datasets\n- [ ] Evaluation metrics (MAE, RMSE, MAPE) computed correctly\n\n---\n\n## VIII. File Path Reference\n\n### New Files Created\n```\n./Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/\n├── AutoSTF.py                           # Main model adapter\n└── autostf_layers/\n    ├── __init__.py\n    ├── linear_layer.py\n    ├── mode.py\n    ├── mixed_operation.py\n    ├── candidate_operation.py\n    ├── st_layers.py\n    └── transformer.py\n\n./Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/config/model/traffic_state_pred/\n└── AutoSTF.json                         # Model configuration\n\n./tests/\n├── test_autostf_integration.py          # Basic integration tests\n├── test_autostf_training.py             # Training verification\n└── test_autostf_datasets.py             # Dataset-specific tests\n\n./scripts/\n├── autostf_adj_utils.py                 # Adjacency matrix utilities\n└── generate_autostf_config.py           # Config generator\n\n./documentation/\n├── AutoSTF_Migration_Checklist.md       # This file\n└── AutoSTF_Migration_Summary.md         # Detailed summary (to be created)\n```\n\n### Modified Files\n```\n./Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/__init__.py\n  Line ~2-10:  Add import statement\n  Line ~40-80: Add \'AutoSTF\' to __all__ list\n```\n\n### Reference Directories\n```\n./repos/AutoSTF/                         # Upstream repository (read-only)\n./repos/DualCast-main/                   # Reference implementation (if exists)\n```\n\n---\n\n## IX. Pytest Execution Plan\n\n### Test Commands\n```bash\n# Run all AutoSTF tests\npytest tests/test_autostf_*.py -v\n\n# Run specific test categories\npytest tests/test_autostf_integration.py -v          # Integration tests\npytest tests/test_autostf_training.py -v             # Training tests\npytest tests/test_autostf_datasets.py -v --slow      # Dataset tests (slower)\n\n# Run with coverage\npytest tests/test_autostf_*.py --cov=libcity.model.traffic_speed_prediction.AutoSTF --cov-report=html\n\n# Run specific test\npytest tests/test_autostf_integration.py::TestAutoSTFIntegration::test_forward_pass_shape -v\n```\n\n### Expected Test Coverage\n- Model initialization: 100%\n- Forward pass: 100%\n- Loss calculation: 100%\n- Different input dimensions: 100%\n- Mini training loop: Pass\n- Real dataset integration: Pass (if datasets available)\n\n### Known Limitations\n1. **NAS Search Phase**: Current migration focuses on training with fixed architecture\n   - Architecture search (search.py) not yet integrated\n   - Mode.ONE_PATH_FIXED used by default\n   - Future work: integrate full NAS pipeline\n\n2. **Dataset Requirements**:\n   - Requires adjacency matrix in data_feature\n   - Requires StandardScaler with inverse_transform()\n   - Time embeddings (time_in_day, day_in_week) must match in_channels config\n\n3. **Performance**:\n   - Original paper uses GPU training (CUDA)\n   - CPU tests will be slower\n   - Recommend GPU for actual training\n\n---\n\n## X. Timeline & Milestones\n\n### Phase 1: Core Migration (Estimated: 4-6 hours)\n- [x] Clone repository\n- [ ] Copy supporting files (1 hour)\n- [ ] Create AutoSTF.py adapter (2 hours)\n- [ ] Create configuration file (30 min)\n- [ ] Register model in LibCity (15 min)\n\n### Phase 2: Testing (Estimated: 3-4 hours)\n- [ ] Write basic integration tests (1.5 hours)\n- [ ] Write training verification test (1 hour)\n- [ ] Debug and fix issues (1-2 hours)\n\n### Phase 3: Documentation (Estimated: 2-3 hours)\n- [ ] Write migration summary (1.5 hours)\n- [ ] Document all files and changes (1 hour)\n- [ ] Create usage examples (30 min)\n\n### Total Estimated Time: 9-13 hours\n\n---\n\n## XI. Success Criteria\n\n✅ **Migration Complete When**:\n1. All files created and organized correctly\n2. AutoSTF model can be imported: `from libcity.model import AutoSTF`\n3. All pytest tests pass\n4. Model trains for 5+ epochs without errors\n5. Documentation is complete and accurate\n6. Config file is valid JSON\n7. Model produces predictions in correct shape\n\n---\n\n## XII. Contact & References\n\n**Original Paper**: AutoSTF: Decoupled Neural Architecture Search for Cost-Effective Automated Spatio-Temporal Forecasting (KDD 2025)\n\n**Original Repository**: https://github.com/usail-hkust/AutoSTF\n\n**LibCity Framework**: https://github.com/LibCity/Bigscity-LibCity\n\n**Migration Author**: AI Agent (Claude)\n**Migration Date**: 2024-11-29\n**LibCity Version**: Compatible with standard LibCity interface\n\n---\n\n## Appendix A: Key Code Snippets\n\n### A.1: Batch Format Transformation\n```python\n# LibCity → AutoSTF\ndef libcity_to_autostf_format(batch):\n    """Transform LibCity batch to AutoSTF input format."""\n    x = batch[\'X\']  # [B, T_in, N, F]\n    x = x.permute(0, 3, 2, 1)  # [B, F, N, T_in]\n    return x\n\n# AutoSTF → LibCity\ndef autostf_to_libcity_format(output):\n    """Transform AutoSTF output to LibCity format."""\n    # output: [B, 1, N, T_out]\n    output = output.permute(0, 3, 2, 1)  # [B, T_out, N, 1]\n    return output\n```\n\n### A.2: Adjacency Matrix Creation\n```python\ndef create_mask_support_adj(adj_mx, device):\n    """Create mask support adjacency for AutoSTF."""\n    def asym_adj(adj):\n        adj = sp.coo_matrix(adj)\n        rowsum = np.array(adj.sum(1)).flatten()\n        d_inv = np.power(rowsum, -1).flatten()\n        d_inv[np.isinf(d_inv)] = 0.\n        d_mat = sp.diags(d_inv)\n        return d_mat.dot(adj).astype(np.float32).todense()\n\n    adj_forward = asym_adj(adj_mx)\n    adj_backward = asym_adj(adj_mx.T)\n\n    return [\n        torch.tensor(adj_forward).to(device),\n        torch.tensor(adj_backward).to(device)\n    ]\n```\n\n---\n\n**End of Checklist**\n'}
