## IX. Risk Assessment

### A. Risks of Current Approach

| Risk | Probability | Impact | Mitigation |
|------|-------------|--------|------------|
| AutoSTF too complex to implement | HIGH (60%) | HIGH | Start with simpler model first |
| Implementation bugs cause poor metrics | MEDIUM (40%) | MEDIUM | Comprehensive testing protocol |
| Hyperparameter mismatch causes deviation | HIGH (70%) | MEDIUM | Match paper configs exactly |
| Data preprocessing differs from paper | MEDIUM (50%) | HIGH | Analyze paper's data processing carefully |
| LibCity framework limitations | LOW (20%) | HIGH | Verify framework capabilities upfront |
| Time investment exceeds benefit | MEDIUM (40%) | MEDIUM | Set strict time boxes (12 hours max) |

### B. Recommended Risk Mitigation

**Strategy 1: Incremental Implementation** ✅ RECOMMENDED
- Start with simplest model from catalog
- Build reusable components (adjacency utils, batch transforms)
- Apply learnings to AutoSTF
- **Time Saved**: 30-40% on AutoSTF

**Strategy 2: Parallel Exploration**
- Attempt 2-3 simple models simultaneously
- Compare implementation patterns
- Identify common challenges early
- **Benefit**: Faster learning curve

**Strategy 3: Early Abort Criteria**
- Set threshold: If implementation exceeds 8 hours without working forward pass, abort
- Document blockers
- Seek external help or simpler alternative
- **Benefit**: Prevents time waste on intractable problems

