python run_model.py --task traffic_state_pred \\\n                    --model STSSDL \\\n                    --dataset PEMS04 \\\n                    --config_file STSSDL \\\n                    --device cuda \\\n                    --gpu_id 0\n```\n\n### Programmatic Usage\n\n```python\nimport torch\nimport numpy as np\nfrom libcity.model.traffic_speed_prediction import STSSDL\n\n# Configuration\nconfig = {\n    \'device\': torch.device(\'cuda\' if torch.cuda.is_available() else \'cpu\'),\n    \'input_window\': 12,\n    \'output_window\': 12,\n    \'rnn_units\': 128,\n    \'rnn_layers\': 1,\n    \'cheb_k\': 3,\n    \'prototype_num\': 20,\n    \'prototype_dim\': 64,\n    \'use_STE\': True,\n    \'node_embedding_dim\': 20,\n    \'tod_embed_dim\': 10,\n    \'adaptive_embedding_dim\': 48,\n    \'input_embedding_dim\': 128,\n    \'lamb_c\': 0.1,\n    \'lamb_d\': 1.0,\n    \'use_curriculum_learning\': True,\n    \'cl_decay_steps\': 2000,\n}\n\n# Data features\ndata_feature = {\n    \'num_nodes\': 207,          # METR-LA has 207 nodes\n    \'feature_dim\': 3,          # [speed, tod, historical]\n    \'output_dim\': 1,           # Predict speed only\n    \'adj_mx\': adj_matrix,      # Adjacency matrix (207x207)\n    \'scaler\': scaler,          # StandardScaler for data normalization\n}\n\n# Initialize model\nmodel = STSSDL(config, data_feature)\nmodel = model.to(config[\'device\'])\n\n# Training\noptimizer = torch.optim.Adam(model.parameters(), lr=0.01)\nmodel.train()\n\nfor epoch in range(200):\n    for batch in train_loader:\n        # batch[\'X\'].shape = (batch_size, 12, 207, 3)\n        # batch[\'y\'].shape = (batch_size, 12, 207, 1)\n\n        optimizer.zero_grad()\n        loss = model.calculate_loss(batch)\n        loss.backward()\n        torch.nn.utils.clip_grad_norm_(model.parameters(), max_norm=5)\n        optimizer.step()\n\n        print(f"Epoch {epoch}, Loss: {loss.item():.4f}")\n\n# Inference\nmodel.eval()\nwith torch.no_grad():\n    predictions = model.predict(test_batch)\n    # predictions.shape = (batch_size, 12, 207, 1)\n```\n\n---\n\n## 🔧 Configuration Variants\n\n### 1. METR-LA (Best Settings from Paper)\n```json\n{\n  "rnn_units": 128,\n  "input_embedding_dim": 3,\n  "node_embedding_dim": 25,\n  "tod_embed_dim": 20,\n  "adaptive_embedding_dim": 0,\n  "lamb_c": 0.01,\n  "steps": [50, 70],\n  "max_epoch": 200\n}\n```\n**Expected Performance**: MAE 2.52 | RMSE 5.03 | MAPE 5.93%\n\n### 2. PEMS-BAY\n```json\n{\n  "rnn_units": 128,\n  "input_embedding_dim": 10,\n  "node_embedding_dim": 20,\n  "tod_embed_dim": 20,\n  "adaptive_embedding_dim": 48,\n  "cl_decay_steps": 8000,\n  "steps": [10, 70, 150]\n}\n```\n**Expected Performance**: MAE 1.24 | RMSE 2.46 | MAPE 2.52%\n\n### 3. PEMS04\n```json\n{\n  "rnn_units": 32,\n  "input_embedding_dim": 32,\n  "node_embedding_dim": 24,\n  "tod_embed_dim": 40,\n  "adaptive_embedding_dim": 48,\n  "batch_size": 16,\n  "lamb_d": 0.01\n}\n```\n**Expected Performance**: MAE 18.20 | RMSE 29.22 | MAPE 12.30%\n\n### 4. PEMS07\n```json\n{\n  "rnn_units": 128,\n  "node_embedding_dim": 20,\n  "tod_embed_dim": 10,\n  "adaptive_embedding_dim": 48,\n  "input_embedding_dim": 128\n}\n```\n**Expected Performance**: MAE 20.37 | RMSE 33.39 | MAPE 8.78%\n\n### 5. PEMS08\n```json\n{\n  "rnn_units": 128,\n  "node_embedding_dim": 20,\n  "tod_embed_dim": 10,\n  "adaptive_embedding_dim": 48,\n  "input_embedding_dim": 128\n}\n```\n**Expected Performance**: MAE 15.32 | RMSE 23.95 | MAPE 10.00%\n\n---\n\n## 🔍 Data Alignment Details\n\n### Input Batch Structure\n\n**LibCity Format** (Expected by STSSDL):\n```python\nbatch = {\n    \'X\': torch.Tensor(batch_size, input_window, num_nodes, feature_dim),\n    \'y\': torch.Tensor(batch_size, output_window, num_nodes, output_dim)\n}\n```\n\n**Feature Dimensions**:\n- `feature_dim = 3` (minimum required)\n  - `[..., 0:1]`: Traffic speed values\n  - `[..., 1:2]`: Time-of-day covariates (normalized 0-1, scaled by TDAY=288)\n  - `[..., 2:3]`: Historical comparison data\n\n**Adapter Logic** (in `STSSDL.predict()` and `STSSDL.calculate_loss()`):\n```python\nx = batch[\'X\']  # (batch_size, input_window, num_nodes, feature_dim)\n\n# Extract components\nx_data = x[..., 0:1]  # Traffic speed\nx_cov = x[..., 1:2] if x.shape[-1] > 1 else torch.zeros_like(x_data)  # ToD\nx_his = x[..., 2:3] if x.shape[-1] > 2 else x_data  # Historical\n\n# Generate future covariates for decoder\ny_cov = x_cov[:, -1:, :, :].repeat(1, output_window, 1, 1)\n```\n\n### Output Format\n- **Shape**: `(batch_size, output_window, num_nodes, output_dim)`\n- **Values**: Predicted traffic speeds (de-normalized by scaler if available)\n\n### Loss Components\n```python\nloss = mae_loss + lambda_c * contrastive_loss + lambda_d * deviation_loss\n```\n\n1. **MAE Loss**: Mean absolute error between predictions and ground truth\n2. **Contrastive Loss**: Triplet margin loss with margin=0.5, weight=0.1\n3. **Deviation Loss**: L1 distance between query similarities, weight=1.0\n\n---\n\n## ⚠️ Known Issues & Limitations\n\n### 1. Data Preprocessing\n**Issue**: Original repository uses custom data preprocessing scripts\n**Location**: `./repos/ST-SSDL/generate_training_data_his_*.py`\n**Impact**: LibCity datasets may lack the historical comparison feature (`x_his`)\n**Workaround**: Use `x_data` as fallback if `x_his` not available\n**Solution**: Create LibCity dataset converter (future enhancement)\n\n### 2. Adjacency Matrix Format\n**Issue**: Original implementation expects specific graph types ("symadj", "normlap", "scalap")\n**Impact**: LibCity\'s default adjacency matrices may differ\n**Recommendation**: Use original graph preprocessing for best results\n**Files**: Check `./repos/ST-SSDL/*/adj_mx.pkl` for reference matrices\n\n### 3. Curriculum Learning Counter\n**Issue**: `batches_seen` counter resets between training runs\n**Impact**: Curriculum learning schedule may not work correctly across sessions\n**Status**: Implemented in model, but requires custom executor for persistence\n**Workaround**: Train in single session without interruption\n\n### 4. Time-of-Day Normalization\n**Issue**: ToD must be normalized to [0, 1] and scaled by TDAY=288\n**Impact**: Incorrect normalization affects temporal embeddings\n**Solution**: Ensure LibCity datasets use `add_time_in_day=True` and proper scaling\n\n### 5. Memory Requirements\n**Issue**: Large prototype memory for big networks\n**Impact**: High GPU memory usage (4-6 GB for batch_size=64)\n**Workaround**: Reduce `batch_size`, `prototype_num`, or `rnn_units`\n\n---\n\n## 📊 Performance Benchmarks (from Original Paper)\n\n| Dataset | Nodes | MAE | RMSE | MAPE (%) | Training Time* |\n|---------|-------|-----|------|----------|----------------|\n| METR-LA | 207 | 2.52 | 5.03 | 5.93 | ~2-3 hours |\n| PEMS-BAY | 325 | 1.24 | 2.46 | 2.52 | ~3-4 hours |\n| PEMS03 | 358 | - | - | - | ~3-4 hours |\n| PEMS04 | 307 | 18.20 | 29.22 | 12.30 | ~3-4 hours |\n| PEMS07 | 883 | 20.37 | 33.39 | 8.78 | ~5-6 hours |\n| PEMS08 | 170 | 15.32 | 23.95 | 10.00 | ~2-3 hours |\n\n*Estimated training time on single GPU (NVIDIA RTX 3090) for 200 epochs\n\n---\n\n## 🔬 Verification Steps\n\n### Step 1: Import Test\n```bash\ncd /home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity\npython -c "from libcity.model.traffic_speed_prediction import STSSDL; print(\'✓ Import successful\')"\n```\n\n**Expected Output**: `✓ Import successful`\n\n### Step 2: Model Instantiation\n```python\nimport torch\nimport numpy as np\nfrom libcity.model.traffic_speed_prediction import STSSDL\n\nconfig = {\n    \'device\': torch.device(\'cpu\'),\n    \'input_window\': 12,\n    \'output_window\': 12,\n}\n\ndata_feature = {\n    \'num_nodes\': 10,\n    \'feature_dim\': 1,\n    \'output_dim\': 1,\n    \'adj_mx\': np.eye(10),\n}\n\nmodel = STSSDL(config, data_feature)\nparam_count = sum(p.numel() for p in model.parameters())\nprint(f"✓ Model created with {param_count:,} parameters")\n```\n\n**Expected Output**: `✓ Model created with ~50,000-200,000 parameters`\n\n### Step 3: Forward Pass\n```python\nbatch = {\n    \'X\': torch.randn(2, 12, 10, 3),  # (batch, time, nodes, features)\n    \'y\': torch.randn(2, 12, 10, 1),  # (batch, time, nodes, 1)\n}\n\noutput = model.predict(batch)\nprint(f"✓ Forward pass successful: {output.shape}")\n```\n\n**Expected Output**: `✓ Forward pass successful: torch.Size([2, 12, 10, 1])`\n\n### Step 4: Loss Calculation\n```python\nloss = model.calculate_loss(batch)\nprint(f"✓ Loss calculation successful: {loss.item():.4f}")\n```\n\n**Expected Output**: `✓ Loss calculation successful: [positive float]`\n\n### Step 5: Run Full Test Suite\n```bash\npytest tests/test_stssdl.py -v\n```\n\n**Expected Output**: `13 passed in ~10-15s`\n\n---\n\n## 🎓 Model Architecture Summary\n\n### Core Components\n\n1. **AGCN (Adaptive Graph Convolution Network)**\n   - Chebyshev polynomial-based graph convolution (K=3)\n   - Supports both static and dynamic adjacency matrices\n   - Xavier uniform initialization\n\n2. **AGCRNCell (Adaptive Graph Convolutional Recurrent Cell)**\n   - GRU-style gating mechanism (update gate + reset gate)\n   - Graph convolution integrated into gates\n   - Hidden state: `(num_nodes, rnn_units)`\n\n3. **ADCRNN_Encoder**\n   - Multi-layer encoder (default: 1 layer)\n   - Input: `(batch, seq_len, num_nodes, input_dim)`\n   - Output: `(num_layers, batch, num_nodes, rnn_units)`\n\n4. **ADCRNN_Decoder**\n   - Multi-step ahead prediction\n   - Autoregressive generation with curriculum learning\n   - Hypernetwork for dynamic graph construction\n   - Prototype-based adjustment\n\n5. **Prototype_Learning**\n   - Learnable prototype memory: `(prototype_num, prototype_dim)`\n   - Query mechanism with attention (softmax over similarities)\n   - Contrastive loss: Triplet margin (positive vs negative prototypes)\n   - Deviation loss: L1 distance between current and historical similarities\n\n### Data Flow\n\n```\nInput (x)\n  │\n  ├─> x_data [speed values]\n  ├─> x_cov [time-of-day]\n  └─> x_his [historical comparison]\n  │\n  v\nEncoder (ADCRNN_Encoder)\n  │\n  v\nHidden States\n  │\n  v\nDecoder (ADCRNN_Decoder) <─── Prototypes\n  │                             │\n  │                             v\n  │                       Query & Match\n  │                             │\n  │                             v\n  v                       Deviation Learning\nOutput (predictions)      Contrastive Loss\n```\n\n### Embeddings (Optional with `use_STE=True`)\n\n- **Node Embeddings**: `(num_nodes, node_embedding_dim)`\n- **Time-of-Day Embeddings**: `(288, tod_embed_dim)` [288 = 24h * 60min / 5min]\n- **Adaptive Embeddings**: `(num_nodes, adaptive_embedding_dim)`\n\nAll embeddings are concatenated and projected to `input_embedding_dim`.\n\n---\n\n## 📦 Dependencies\n\n### Original Requirements\n```\ntables==3.8.0\nnumpy==1.21.5\npandas==1.5.1\nscipy==1.7.3\ntorch==1.13.1\ntorchinfo==1.8.0\nnumexpr==2.10.0\n```\n\n### LibCity Compatibility\n- ✅ Compatible with LibCity\'s PyTorch version (≥1.7.0)\n- ✅ No additional dependencies required\n- ✅ Uses LibCity\'s built-in utilities (StandardScaler, etc.)\n- ✅ Works with LibCity\'s data loaders and executors\n\n---\n\n## 🔮 Future Enhancements (Optional)\n\n### Priority: HIGH\n1. **LibCity Dataset Converter**\n   - Convert LibCity datasets to ST-SSDL format\n   - Generate historical comparison features\n   - Proper time-of-day normalization\n\n### Priority: MEDIUM\n2. **Custom Executor**\n   - Persistent `batches_seen` counter across epochs\n   - Proper curriculum learning schedule\n   - Advanced early stopping based on deviation loss\n\n3. **Hyperparameter Search**\n   - Ray Tune or Optuna integration\n   - Search space: `rnn_units`, `prototype_num`, `lamb_c`, `lamb_d`\n   - Multi-objective optimization (accuracy + efficiency)\n\n### Priority: LOW\n4. **Benchmark Automation**\n   - Automated testing on all PEMS datasets\n   - Performance comparison with other LibCity models\n   - Result visualization and reporting\n\n5. **Model Ensemble**\n 