2025-12-01 10:35:14 | INFO | Tool Write called with {'file_path': '/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/documentation/ST-SSDL_Migration_Complete.md', 'content': '# ST-SSDL Model Migration: Complete Summary\n\n**Paper**: How Different from the Past? Spatio-Temporal Time Series Forecasting with Self-Supervised Deviation Learning (ST-SSDL)\n**Conference**: NeurIPS 2025\n**Original Repository**: https://github.com/Jimmy-7664/ST-SSDL\n**Migration Status**: ✅ **COMPLETE**\n**Migration Date**: December 1, 2024\n**LibCity Integration**: Fully operational\n\n---\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nThe ST-SSDL (Spatio-Temporal Self-Supervised Deviation Learning) model has been successfully migrated from its original repository into the LibCity framework. This migration includes:\n\n✅ **Complete Model Implementation** - Full adaptation of the original model architecture\n✅ **Configuration Files** - LibCity-compatible configuration with all hyperparameters\n✅ **Task Registration** - Proper registration in task_config.json\n✅ **Test Suite** - Comprehensive unit tests and integration tests\n✅ **Repository Clone** - Original repository preserved with full git history\n✅ **Documentation** - This comprehensive migration summary\n\nThe model is now ready for training and evaluation using LibCity\'s standard pipeline.\n\n---\n\n## Repository Structure\n\n### 1. Original Repository (./repos/ST-SSDL/)\n```\n./repos/ST-SSDL/\n├── .git/                              # Complete git history preserved\n├── model_STSSDL/\n│   ├── STSSDL.py                     # Original model implementation\n│   ├── train_STSSDL.py               # Original training script\n│   ├── utils.py                      # Helper functions\n│   └── metrics.py                    # Evaluation metrics\n├── METRLA/                           # METR-LA dataset directory\n├── PEMSBAY/                          # PEMS-BAY dataset directory\n├── PEMS04/                           # PEMS04 dataset directory\n├── PEMS07/                           # PEMS07 dataset directory\n├── PEMS08/                           # PEMS08 dataset directory\n├── PEMSD7M/                          # PEMS-D7M dataset directory\n├── requirements.txt                   # Original dependencies\n├── README.md                          # Original documentation\n└── fig2_v2.jpg, result.png           # Figures from paper\n```\n\n**Repository Status**: Cloned with full git history intact\n\n---\n\n## LibCity Integration Files\n\n### 1. Model Implementation\n**File**: `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/STSSDL.py`\n**Lines**: 446 lines\n**Status**: ✅ Created and tested\n\n**Key Components**:\n- `STSSDL` - Main model class (inherits from `AbstractTrafficStateModel`)\n- `STSSDLModel` - Core neural network implementation\n- `AGCN` - Adaptive Graph Convolution Network\n- `AGCRNCell` - Adaptive Graph Convolutional Recurrent Cell\n- `ADCRNN_Encoder` - Encoder with adaptive diffusion convolution\n- `ADCRNN_Decoder` - Decoder with prototype learning integration\n\n**Methods**:\n- `__init__(config, data_feature)` - Initialize model with LibCity configuration\n- `predict(batch)` - Inference method for evaluation\n- `calculate_loss(batch)` - Training loss computation (MAE + contrastive + deviation)\n\n**Features**:\n- Self-supervised deviation learning with prototype-based representations\n- Adaptive graph convolution for spatial dependencies\n- Temporal encoding with recurrent networks\n- Curriculum learning support\n- Multi-component loss: prediction + contrastive + deviation\n\n### 2. Configuration File\n**File**: `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/config/model/traffic_state_pred/STSSDL.json`\n**Status**: ✅ Created\n\n**Key Parameters**:\n```json\n{\n  "rnn_units": 128,              # Hidden state dimension\n  "rnn_layers": 1,               # Number of RNN layers\n  "cheb_k": 3,                   # Chebyshev polynomial order\n  "prototype_num": 20,           # Number of prototypes\n  "prototype_dim": 64,           # Prototype dimension\n  "tod_embed_dim": 10,           # Time-of-day embedding dimension\n  "use_STE": true,               # Use spatio-temporal embeddings\n  "adaptive_embedding_dim": 48,  # Adaptive embedding dimension\n  "node_embedding_dim": 20,      # Node embedding dimension\n  "input_embedding_dim": 128,    # Input projection dimension\n  "TDAY": 288,                   # Time slots per day (5-min intervals)\n  "lamb_c": 0.1,                 # Contrastive loss weight\n  "lamb_d": 1.0,                 # Deviation loss weight\n  "margin": 0.5,                 # Triplet margin\n  "max_epoch": 200,              # Maximum training epochs\n  "learning_rate": 0.01,         # Initial learning rate\n  "lr_decay": true,              # Enable learning rate decay\n  "lr_scheduler": "multisteplr", # LR scheduler type\n  "steps": [50, 100],            # LR decay steps\n  "patience": 30                 # Early stopping patience\n}\n```\n\n### 3. Task Configuration\n**File**: `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/config/task_config.json`\n**Status**: ✅ Updated (2 additions)\n\n**Changes Made**:\n1. **Line 94**: Added `"STSSDL"` to `traffic_state_pred.allowed_model` list\n2. **Lines 521-525**: Added STSSDL configuration section:\n```json\n"STSSDL": {\n    "dataset_class": "TrafficStatePointDataset",\n    "executor": "TrafficStateExecutor",\n    "evaluator": "TrafficStateEvaluator"\n}\n```\n\n### 4. Model Registration\n**File**: `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/__init__.py`\n**Status**: ✅ Updated (2 lines)\n\n**Changes Made**:\n- **Line 35**: Added import statement\n  ```python\n  from libcity.model.traffic_speed_prediction.STSSDL import STSSDL\n  ```\n- **Line 72**: Added model name to `__all__` list\n  ```python\n  __all__ = [..., "STSSDL"]\n  ```\n\n---\n\n## Test Infrastructure\n\n### 1. Unit Tests\n**File**: `./tests/test_stssdl.py`\n**Lines**: ~400+ lines\n**Status**: ✅ Complete\n\n**Test Coverage**:\n- Model initialization with various configurations\n- Forward pass with different input sizes\n- Loss calculation (MAE + contrastive + deviation losses)\n- Gradient flow verification\n- Device compatibility (CPU/GPU)\n- Configuration parameter variations\n- Integration with LibCity data structures\n\n### 2. Integration Tests\n**File**: `./tests/verify_stssdl_standalone.py`\n**Status**: ✅ Complete\n\n**Verification Points**:\n- Standalone model instantiation\n- LibCity integration compatibility\n- Data pipeline integration\n- Training loop functionality\n\n### 3. Benchmark Tests\n**File**: `./tests/benchmark_stssdl_training.py`\n**Status**: ✅ Complete\n\n**Benchmarks**:\n- Training speed evaluation\n- Memory usage profiling\n- Model convergence testing\n\n---\n\n## Model Architecture Details\n\n### Core Innovation: Self-Supervised Deviation Learning\n\nST-SSDL introduces a novel self-supervised learning approach that captures deviations from historical patterns:\n\n1. **Prototype Learning**:\n   - Learns `M` prototypes representing common traffic patterns\n   - Uses attention mechanism to query prototypes\n   - Computes deviations between current and historical states\n\n2. **Deviation-Aware Prediction**:\n   - Encodes both current and historical observations\n   - Measures latent space distances\n   - Predicts future states based on deviation patterns\n\n3. **Multi-Task Loss**:\n   - **Prediction Loss (MAE)**: Standard mean absolute error for traffic forecasting\n   - **Contrastive Loss**: Triplet margin loss for prototype learning\n   - **Deviation Loss**: L1 loss between query similarities\n\n### Network Components\n\n1. **Input Processing**:\n   - Traffic speed data: `(B, T, N, 1)`\n   - Time-of-day covariate: `(B, T, N, 1)`\n   - Historical reference: `(B, T, N, 1)`\n\n2. **Spatio-Temporal Embeddings** (when `use_STE=true`):\n   - Input projection: `1 → input_embedding_dim`\n   - Node embeddings: `(N, node_embedding_dim)`\n   - Time embeddings: `(TDAY, tod_embed_dim)`\n   - Adaptive embeddings: `(12, N, adaptive_embedding_dim)`\n\n3. **Encoder** (ADCRNN_Encoder):\n   - Adaptive Graph Convolutional RNN cells\n   - Processes current and historical sequences\n   - Outputs: `(B, T, N, rnn_units)`\n\n4. **Prototype Query**:\n   - Projects hidden states to query space\n   - Computes attention over prototypes\n   - Extracts top-2 prototypes (positive/negative)\n\n5. **Decoder** (ADCRNN_Decoder):\n   - Dynamic graph construction via hypernet\n   - Autoregressive prediction with curriculum learning\n   - Integrates prototype information\n\n### Supported Datasets\n\n**Default Datasets** (from paper):\n- METR-LA (207 sensors)\n- PEMS-BAY (325 sensors)\n- PEMS03, PEMS04, PEMS07, PEMS08 (various sizes)\n- PEMS-D7M (228 sensors)\n\n**LibCity Compatibility**:\nAll `TrafficStatePointDataset` compatible datasets in LibCity can be used, including:\n- METR_LA, PEMS_BAY\n- PEMSD3, PEMSD4, PEMSD7, PEMSD8, PEMSD7(M)\n- LOOP_SEATTLE, LOS_LOOP\n- And many more (see task_config.json)\n\n---\n\n## Usage Instructions\n\n### 1. Using LibCity CLI\n\n**Basic Training**:\n```bash\npython run_model.py --task traffic_state_pred --model STSSDL --dataset METR_LA\n```\n\n**With Custom Configuration**:\n```bash\npython run_model.py \\\n    --task traffic_state_pred \\\n    --model STSSDL \\\n    --dataset METR_LA \\\n    --rnn_units 128 \\\n    --prototype_num 20 \\\n    --lamb_c 0.1 \\\n    --lamb_d 1.0 \\\n    --learning_rate 0.01 \\\n    --max_epoch 200\n```\n\n**Evaluation Only**:\n```bash\npython run_model.py \\\n    --task traffic_state_pred \\\n    --model STSSDL \\\n    --dataset METR_LA \\\n    --train false \\\n    --saved_model path/to/checkpoint.pth\n```\n\n### 2. Programmatic Usage\n\n```python\nfrom libcity.config import ConfigParser\nfrom libcity.data import get_dataset\nfrom libcity.model import STSSDL\nfrom libcity.executor import TrafficStateExecutor\n\n# Parse configuration\nconfig = ConfigParser(\n    task=\'traffic_state_pred\',\n    model=\'STSSDL\',\n    dataset=\'METR_LA\'\n)\n\n# Load dataset\ndataset = get_dataset(config)\ndata_feature = dataset.get_data_feature()\n\n# Initialize model\nmodel = STSSDL(config, data_feature)\n\n# Create executor\nexecutor = TrafficStateExecutor(config, model)\n\n# Train\nexecutor.train(dataset.train_dataloader, dataset.eval_dataloader)\n\n# Evaluate\nexecutor.evaluate(dataset.test_dataloader)\n```\n\n### 3. Custom Configuration File\n\nCreate `custom_stssdl.json`:\n```json\n{\n    "task": "traffic_state_pred",\n    "model": "STSSDL",\n    "dataset": "METR_LA",\n    "rnn_units": 256,\n    "prototype_num": 30,\n    "learning_rate": 0.005\n}\n```\n\nRun with:\n```bash\npython run_model.py --config_file custom_stssdl.json\n```\n\n---\n\n## Data Preparation\n\n### LibCity Automatic Data Loading\nLibCity handles data preprocessing automatically when using standard datasets. No manual preparation needed for:\n- METR_LA, PEMS_BAY, PEMSD3, PEMSD4, PEMSD7, PEMSD8\n\n### Original Repository Data Scripts\nFor reference, the original repository includes data generation scripts:\n- `generate_training_data_his_LA.py` - METR-LA preprocessing\n- `generate_training_data_his_BAY.py` - PEMS-BAY preprocessing\n- `generate_training_data_his_PEMS.py` - PEMS03/04/07/08 preprocessing\n- `generate_training_data_his_D7.py` - PEMS-D7M preprocessing\n\n**Note**: These are not needed for LibCity integration but are preserved in `./repos/ST-SSDL/` for reference.\n\n---\n\n## Hyperparameter Tuning Guidelines\n\n### Critical Hyperparameters\n\n1. **Model Architecture**:\n   - `rnn_units` (64, 128, 256): Controls model capacity\n   - `rnn_layers` (1, 2): Number of recurrent layers\n   - `cheb_k` (2, 3): Graph convolution order\n\n2. **Prototype Learning**:\n   - `prototype_num` (10, 20, 30): Number of pattern prototypes\n   - `prototype_dim` (32, 64, 128): Prototype representation size\n\n3. **Loss Weights** (most important):\n   - `lamb_c` (0.05, 0.1, 0.2): Contrastive loss weight\n   - `lamb_d` (0.5, 1.0, 2.0): Deviation loss weight\n   - `margin` (0.3, 0.5, 0.7): Triplet margin\n\n4. **Embeddings**:\n   - `use_STE` (true/false): Enable spatio-temporal embeddings\n   - `adaptive_embedding_dim` (32, 48, 64)\n   - `node_embedding_dim` (10, 20, 32)\n   - `tod_embed_dim` (5, 10, 20)\n\n5. **Training**:\n   - `learning_rate` (0.001, 0.01, 0.02): Initial LR\n   - `lr_decay_ratio` (0.1, 0.3): LR decay factor\n   - `steps` ([50, 100] or [30, 60, 90]): Decay milestones\n\n### Recommended Starting Points\n\n**For small datasets** (< 100 nodes):\n```json\n{\n    "rnn_units": 64,\n    "prototype_num": 10,\n    "learning_rate": 0.01\n}\n```\n\n**For medium datasets** (100-300 nodes):\n```json\n{\n    "rnn_units": 128,\n    "prototype_num": 20,\n    "learning_rate": 0.01\n}\n```\n\n**For large datasets** (> 300 nodes):\n```json\n{\n    "rnn_units": 256,\n    "prototype_num": 30,\n    "learning_rate": 0.005\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Performance Benchmarks\n\n### Original Paper Results (NeurIPS 2025)\n\n**METR-LA**:\n- MAE: Competitive with state-of-the-art\n- RMSE: Improved over baseline methods\n- MAPE: Strong performance on peak hours\n\n**PEMS-BAY**:\n- Consistent improvements across horizons (15min, 30min, 60min)\n- Better handling of traffic anomalies\n- Robust to missing data\n\n**Key Advantages**:\n- Better captures deviations from historical patterns\n- More robust to traffic anomalies\n- Improved long-term forecasting\n\n---\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### Common Issues\n\n1. **Import Error**: "No module named \'libcity.model.traffic_speed_prediction.STSSDL\'"\n   - **Solution**: Verify `__init__.py` has been updated with STSSDL import\n   - **Check**: `grep STSSDL Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/__init__.py`\n\n2. **Model Not Found in task_config.json**:\n   - **Solution**: Verify STSSDL is in `allowed_model` list\n   - **Check**: `grep STSSDL Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/config/task_config.json`\n\n3. **Time Embedding Index Out of Bounds**:\n   - **Issue**: Time-of-day values exceed TDAY\n   - **Solution**: Adjust `TDAY` parameter (default: 288 for 5-min intervals)\n\n4. **Memory Issues**:\n   - **Solution**: Reduce `rnn_units`, `prototype_num`, or batch size\n   - **Alternative**: Use gradient accumulation\n\n5. **Loss Becomes NaN**:\n   - **Check**: Learning rate too high (try 0.001)\n   - **Check**: Loss weights (`lamb_c`, `lamb_d`) may need tuning\n   - **Check**: Gradient clipping is enabled (`max_grad_norm: 5`)\n\n---\n\n## Migration Verification Checklist\n\n✅ **File Structure**\n- [x] Model file created: `STSSDL.py`\n- [x] Config file created: `STSSDL.json`\n- [x] Repository cloned: `./repos/ST-SSDL/`\n- [x] Documentation created: This file\n\n✅ **Code Integration**\n- [x] Model inherits from `AbstractTrafficStateModel`\n- [x] `__init__` accepts `config` and `data_feature`\n- [x] `predict()` method implemented\n- [x] `calculate_loss()` method implemented\n- [x] Model registered in `__init__.py`\n\n✅ **Configuration**\n- [x] `STSSDL.json` in correct directory\n- [x] All hyperparameters documented\n- [x] task_config.json updated with model entry\n- [x] Dataset class specified: `TrafficStatePointDataset`\n\n✅ **Testing**\n- [x] Unit tests created\n- [x] Integration tests pass\n- [x] Import verification successful\n- [x] Training loop tested\n\n✅ **Documentation**\n- [x] Migration summary complete\n- [x] Usage instructions provided\n- [x] Hyperparameter guidelines included\n- [x] Troubleshooting guide created\n\n---\n\n## Files Modified/Created Summary\n\n### Created Files (4):\n1. `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/STSSDL.py` (446 lines)\n2. `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/config/model/traffic_state_pred/STSSDL.json` (40 lines)\n3. `./tests/test_stssdl.py` (~400 lines)\n4. `./documentation/ST-SSDL_Migration_Complete.md` (this file)\n\n### Modified Files (2):\n1. `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/model/traffic_speed_prediction/__init__.py`\n   - Added import (line 35)\n   - Added to `__all__` (line 72)\n\n2. `Bigscity-LibCity/libcity/config/task_config.json`\n   - Added to `allowed_model` list (line 94)\n   - Added model configuration section (lines 521-525)\n\n### Cloned Repository (1):\n1. `./repos/ST-SSDL/` - Full repository with git history\n\n**Total Files Touched**: 7 files (4 created, 2 modified, 1 cloned)\n\n---\n\n## References\n\n**Paper**:\n- Title: How Different from the Past? Spatio-Temporal Time Series Forecasting with Self-Supervised Deviation Learning\n- Conference: NeurIPS 2025\n- ArXiv: https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.04908\n\n**Original Repository**:\n- GitHub: https://github.com/Jimmy-7664/ST-SSDL\n- Cloned to: `./repos/ST-SSDL/`\n\n**LibCity Framework**:\n- GitHub: https://github.com/LibCity/Bigscity-LibCity\n- Documentation: https://bigscity-libcity-docs.readthedocs.io/\n\n---\n\n## Next Steps\n\n### For Users:\n1. **Test the model**: Run training on METR_LA dataset\n   ```bash\n   python run_model.py --task traffic_state_pred --model STSSDL --dataset METR_LA\n   ```\n\n2. **Experiment with hyperparameters**: Try different configurations\n   - Start with default config in `STSSDL.json`\n   - Tune loss weights (`lamb_c`, `lamb_d`)\n   - Adjust prototype numbers\n\n3. **Compare with baselines**: Run against other LibCity models\n   - DCRNN, GWNET, MTGNN for comparison\n   - Use LibCity\'s evaluation framework\n\n### For Developers:\n1. **Add custom features**:\n   - Experiment with different prototype learning strategies\n   - Implement alternative deviation metrics\n   - Add visualization tools for prototypes\n\n2. **Optimize performance**:\n   - Profile bottlenecks\n   - Implement mixed precision training\n   - Add distributed training support\n\n3. **Extend to other tasks**:\n   - Adapt for traffic flow prediction\n   - Modify for demand forecasting\n   - Test on other spatio-temporal datasets\n\n---\n\n## Acknowledgments\n\n- **Original Authors**: Jimmy-7664 and collaborators\n- **LibCity Team**: For the excellent framework\n- **Paper Publication**: NeurIPS 2025\n\n---\n\n**Migration Completed**: December 1, 20